WEBVTT


00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.430
Where have you been?
I've been waiting since 7:00.


00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.867
Get in. I had to find fireworks.


00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.164
Let me drive.


00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.536
Get in. I haven't eaten in 24 hours.


00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.068
Are you coming or not?


00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.899
It's too crowded.


00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.798
I thought you were starving.


00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.766
Let's go someplace quiet.


00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.469
Okay.


00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.682
What are we doing?


00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:09.589
Sitting. Listening to music. Talking.


00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:14.497
- You seem weird. Is everything okay?
- Yeah, everything's fine.


00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.071
It's July.
How many shirts are you wearing?


00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:28.272
- I'm cold.
- You're cold on the Fourth of July?


00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.811
Fuck off and die!


00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:44.255
- What?
- "Fuck off and die"?


00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.093
Shut up.


00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.652
Was that car at the drive-in?


00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.323
I saw that car at Mr. Ed's.


00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:29.003
- Do you want me to tell him to leave?
- Stay in the car.


00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:46.417
- Was that your husband?
- No.


00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.528
Who was that, Darlene?


00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.559
Don't worry about it.


00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:59.104
- Don't tell me not to worry. Who was it?
- It's nothing.


00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.281
Oh, shit.


00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.891
Let's go.


00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.662
Now, D.


00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.471
Get your wallet.


00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:54.026
Man, you really creeped us out.


00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.318
- <i>Vallejo Police Department.</i>
- <i>I want to report a double murder.</i>


00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.017
<i>May I have your name</i>
<i>and where you are calling...</i>


00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:03.493
<i>If you go one mile east</i>
<i>on Columbus Parkway,</i>


00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:06.827
<i>a public park,</i>
<i>you'll find kids in a brown car.</i>


00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.565
<i>They were shot with a 9mm Luger.</i>


00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.732
<i>I also killed those kids last year.</i>


00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.933
<i>Goodbye.</i>


00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:35.985
Spit.


00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.592
Come on, buddy.


00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:41.667
- I swallowed it.
- Why?


00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.133
It was minty.


00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.638
You can't do that. It's not good for you.


00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.030
Lunch box.


00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:52.077
- Why am I not going on the bus?
- Because we're late.


00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:57.379
Okay, you're staying
with your mom and Aaron tonight.


00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:00.212
So, you don't like
having a new little brother?


00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.652
- No, not really.
- Oh, that's honest.


00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.489
Learn a lot.


00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.728
There will be a test tonight!


00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.092
Morning.


00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:52.037
- Hi.
- Good morning.


00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.469
- Morning.
- Morning.


00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.423
How's the coffee today, Shorty?


00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.534
Editorial in two.


00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.666
Good morning, gentlemen.


00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:37.003
- Good morning.
- Good morning.


00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:39.043
Well, Stanton, tell Mr. Howe


00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:41.636
the draft board piece
was damn near perfect.


00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.315
Mr. Graysmith.


00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:47.250
Horrid.


00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:48.411
Horrid.


00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:50.716
Not so horrid.


00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:52.586
Horrid.
I'm thinking we go with not so horrid.


00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:58.957
Paul, what's on the crime beat?


00:09:59.065 --> 00:10:03.195
Janice in Datebook left the fondue party
before everyone got naked.


00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:04.997
That's a crime.


00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:07.231
Have you seen her? Wouldn't kid you.


00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.070
It may be the beginning of a crime wave.


00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.441
You need to see this.


00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.681
Go get the publisher.


00:10:19.785 --> 00:10:20.877
"Dear Editor,


00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:22.045
"This is the murderer


00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:24.213
"of the two teenagers
last Christmas at Lake Herman


00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:27.486
"and the girl on the Fourth of July
near the golf course in Vallejo.


00:10:27.593 --> 00:10:28.651
"To prove I killed them,


00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:32.458
"I shall state some facts
which only I and the police know.


00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:35.898
"Christmas,
brand name of ammo, Super-X.


00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:38.269
"Ten shots were fired.


00:10:38.371 --> 00:10:41.169
"The boy was on his back
with his feet to the car.


00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:42.535
"The girl..."


00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:47.803
Would you read that, please?


00:10:49.048 --> 00:10:51.539
"The girl was on her right side,
feet to the west.


00:10:51.651 --> 00:10:53.312
"Fourth of July.


00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:56.286
"One, girl was
wearing patterned slacks.


00:10:56.389 --> 00:10:58.448
"The boy was also shot in the knee.


00:10:58.557 --> 00:11:00.889
"Brand name of ammo was Western.


00:11:01.594 --> 00:11:03.357
"Here is part of a cipher.


00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:06.954
"The other two parts of this cipher
are being mailed to the editors of


00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:09.899
"the <i>Vallejo Times</i> and <i>S.F. Examiner.</i>


00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:13.802
"I want you to print this cipher
on the front page of your paper.


00:11:13.906 --> 00:11:16.306
"In this cipher is my identity.


00:11:16.409 --> 00:11:18.900
"If you do not print this cipher
by the afternoon of Fry,"


00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:25.007
F-R-Y, "First of Aug '69
I will go on a kill rampage Fry night.


00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:29.417
"I will cruise around all weekend
killing Ione people in the night


00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:30.955
"then move on to kill again


00:11:31.057 --> 00:11:34.788
"until I end up with
a dozen people over the weekend."


00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:37.362
It's unsigned except for a symbol.


00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:41.725
Is it me,
or does that look like a gunsight?


00:11:43.302 --> 00:11:45.167
Today's August first.


00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:46.898
He wants his code
in the afternoon edition.


00:11:47.006 --> 00:11:49.736
If the <i>Examiner</i> doesn't have
the balls to run it, we scoop the Bay.


00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:51.867
Al, this man is talking about
shooting 12 people.


00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:53.774
And not running this
might make him do that.


00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:56.347
If we run it, we might be setting
a very dangerous precedent.


00:11:56.449 --> 00:11:57.882
Oh, come on, now, it's newsworthy.


00:11:57.983 --> 00:12:00.213
Well, giving some sick bastard
a soapbox,


00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:01.343
what does that say to people?


00:12:01.454 --> 00:12:04.651
Back up. Is this Vallejo story true?
Do we know that?


00:12:04.757 --> 00:12:07.726
- Paul?
- What? I cover crime in Vallejo?


00:12:08.928 --> 00:12:10.862
Yeah, I cover crime in Vallejo.
Ten minutes.


00:12:10.963 --> 00:12:13.261
Let's shoot the code and call SFPD.


00:12:13.365 --> 00:12:17.165
If it turns out to be real,
at least we'll have the material.


00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:18.967
All right.


00:12:19.772 --> 00:12:22.036
Graysmith,
don't you have that cartoon to finish?


00:12:22.141 --> 00:12:23.369
Oh, yeah.


00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:32.145
Hi, this is Paul Avery
from the <i>San Francisco Chronicle.</i>


00:12:32.251 --> 00:12:35.277
I'm looking for someone to
shed some light on a letter we received.


00:12:35.387 --> 00:12:36.411
Thank you.


00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.714
Sergeant Mulanax.


00:12:38.824 --> 00:12:40.587
<i>Sergeant, Paul Avery from</i>
<i>the</i> San Francisco Chronicle.


00:12:40.693 --> 00:12:41.717
I just wanted to check


00:12:41.827 --> 00:12:43.624
if you had an unsolved
firearm-related homicide


00:12:43.729 --> 00:12:46.630
on Christmas and
maybe one on July fourth.


00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:47.892
Shit.


00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:49.799
You guys got one, too?


00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:54.033
Confirmed.
VPD, they confirmed the shootings.


00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:55.198
Al's on the phone with the <i>Examiner.</i>


00:12:55.307 --> 00:12:56.706
They got the same letter
with a different code.


00:12:56.809 --> 00:12:57.867
So did <i>Times-Herald.</i>


00:12:57.977 --> 00:13:00.343
Christmas, two teenagers
on lover's lane. Both DOA.


00:13:00.446 --> 00:13:02.038
David Faraday and Betty Jensen.


00:13:02.148 --> 00:13:04.708
July fourth,
Darlene Ferrin and Michael...


00:13:04.817 --> 00:13:06.682
I think it's "Mayhew."
Anyway, he lived, she didn't.


00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:07.844
The murder weapons?


00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:10.854
Ballistics, everything he said
in the letters matched.


00:13:10.956 --> 00:13:14.016
I mean, I think the <i>Times-Herald's</i>
gonna go with it.


00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:16.993
<i>The Examiner's</i> going,
but won't go front page.


00:13:17.096 --> 00:13:21.294
I say let's go front page.
If he kills 12 people, it's not our fault.


00:13:21.867 --> 00:13:24.427
Robert! We need the cartoon.


00:13:26.338 --> 00:13:29.501
- You're not finished?
- No, I'm finished, Carol. I'm finished.


00:13:29.608 --> 00:13:31.303
Thieriot's still here.


00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.570
Really?


00:13:33.045 --> 00:13:36.310
The first edition
is off the floor in 10, Charles.


00:13:39.785 --> 00:13:41.252
Give us a sec.


00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:45.680
Okay, re-plate.


00:13:46.158 --> 00:13:48.683
We'll go on page... Page four.


00:13:50.563 --> 00:13:53.691
What do you say, 20 bucks
whoever cracks the psycho's name?


00:13:53.799 --> 00:13:55.664
He won't give his name.


00:13:56.936 --> 00:13:58.665
Morti's? Anyone?


00:13:58.771 --> 00:14:01.001
- That's where I'm heading.
- All right.


00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:30.364
Put those on my desk. Turn on the light.


00:14:41.347 --> 00:14:42.871
Grab your book.


00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:47.910
Now go get your jammies on.


00:14:50.823 --> 00:14:52.313
<i>All right, people, listen up.</i>


00:14:52.725 --> 00:14:57.788
The cipher's broken into three sections,
each with eight lines and 17 symbols.


00:14:57.897 --> 00:15:00.422
No breaks between the symbols
denoting different words.


00:15:00.532 --> 00:15:02.898
No numbers or clues
to substitution keys.


00:15:03.002 --> 00:15:05.061
And you got symbols
from at least seven different sources.


00:15:06.405 --> 00:15:11.035
Greek, Morse code, Navy semaphore,
weather symbols, astrological signs.


00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:20.045
- Hey, take a gander at this code thing.
- Okay.


00:15:25.391 --> 00:15:26.983
You wanna give it a go?


00:15:29.061 --> 00:15:32.030
Guy who used to sit there
was a great cartoonist. Bob Bastian.


00:15:32.131 --> 00:15:32.765
Now he's doing public television.
For some reason.


00:15:32.765 --> 00:15:35.427
Now he's doing public television.
For some reason.


00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:38.367
Paul Avery.


00:15:39.838 --> 00:15:42.807
Robert Graysmith.
I've been here nine months.


00:15:45.844 --> 00:15:48.108
You were right, by the way.
He didn't give his name.


00:15:48.213 --> 00:15:49.180
Who cracked it?


00:15:49.281 --> 00:15:51.511
A history teacher
and his wife in Salinas.


00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:54.711
"I like killing people
because it is so much fun.


00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:58.847
"It is more fun
than killing wild game in the forest


00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:03.486
"because man is the most
dangerous animal of all to kill.


00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:06.257
"Something gives me
the most thrilling experience.


00:16:06.365 --> 00:16:10.324
"It is even better
than getting your rocks off with a girl.


00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:14.065
"The best part of it is that when I die,


00:16:14.173 --> 00:16:17.142
"I will be reborn in paradise.


00:16:17.242 --> 00:16:20.609
"And all that I have killed
will become my slaves.


00:16:20.713 --> 00:16:24.479
"I will not give you my name
because you will try to slow down


00:16:24.583 --> 00:16:27.780
"or stop my collecting of slaves
for my afterlife."


00:16:27.886 --> 00:16:29.751
Methinks our friend's
a tad bit fuckered in the head.


00:16:29.855 --> 00:16:34.019
I heard he even sent Vallejo
a code key, just to help.


00:16:34.126 --> 00:16:36.492
- What is that at the bottom?
- Leftovers.


00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:38.187
Maybe an anagram.


00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.114
How does one do that?


00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.111
I like puzzles. I do them a lot.


00:17:01.487 --> 00:17:04.513
How did you know
he wasn't gonna give his name?


00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.717
Dangerous animal.


00:17:07.593 --> 00:17:09.185
Dangerous animal.


00:17:10.129 --> 00:17:12.996
What dangerous animal?
How do I know that?


00:17:20.372 --> 00:17:21.964
- Paul.
- Yes, Templeton.


00:17:22.074 --> 00:17:24.133
- Editorial, now.
- Very well.


00:17:26.311 --> 00:17:27.869
Another letter.


00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.279
More of the same.
Details about the murders.


00:17:32.418 --> 00:17:36.320
He taped a flashlight to the gun.
That's how he hit them in the dark.


00:17:36.422 --> 00:17:38.481
And he gave himself a name.


00:17:59.645 --> 00:18:02.739
You know this used to be
the town of Montecello?


00:18:02.848 --> 00:18:04.179
But at some point,


00:18:04.283 --> 00:18:07.446
the county decided that the land
would work better as a lake.


00:18:07.553 --> 00:18:09.248
So they flooded it.


00:18:10.722 --> 00:18:14.488
- But there's an entire...
- Hidden city under the water.


00:18:14.593 --> 00:18:16.686
We were here last spring, remember?


00:18:16.795 --> 00:18:18.194
Oh, yeah.


00:18:24.403 --> 00:18:26.132
Somebody else is here.


00:18:26.238 --> 00:18:27.967
It is a public park.


00:18:30.642 --> 00:18:32.735
I think he's watching us.


00:18:32.845 --> 00:18:35.075
Well, we're very good-Iooking.


00:18:40.752 --> 00:18:42.219
Where'd he go?


00:18:44.957 --> 00:18:46.618
He went behind that tree.


00:18:46.725 --> 00:18:49.091
All right. So he's taking a leak.


00:18:56.101 --> 00:18:57.966
He's coming towards us.


00:19:00.072 --> 00:19:02.040
Oh, my God, he has a gun.


00:19:02.841 --> 00:19:04.308
Don't move.


00:19:04.409 --> 00:19:07.276
- I want your money and your car keys.
- Okay.


00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.572
We're not gonna do anything, okay?


00:19:09.681 --> 00:19:13.378
We're gonna cooperate.
Just tell me what you want us to do.


00:19:17.055 --> 00:19:18.113
Here.


00:19:20.492 --> 00:19:22.983
You're welcome to everything I have.


00:19:26.565 --> 00:19:28.999
If there's anything else
I could do for you...


00:19:29.101 --> 00:19:31.399
Maybe I could write you a check?


00:19:33.972 --> 00:19:36.566
Okay, I could give you
my phone number.


00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:39.872
You know, I might be able to help you.


00:19:39.978 --> 00:19:42.071
Even more than you might think.


00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.240
He's a sociology major.


00:19:45.784 --> 00:19:48.378
Pre-law, actually.


00:19:50.522 --> 00:19:51.989
Oh, keys.


00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.217
You know, I'm sorry, I don't know exactly
where I put my keys.


00:19:54.326 --> 00:19:57.295
They might be on the blanket.
Is it okay if...


00:20:02.067 --> 00:20:03.625
Here's the keys.


00:20:05.103 --> 00:20:06.934
Don't get up.


00:20:07.039 --> 00:20:09.030
I want her to tie you up.


00:20:13.212 --> 00:20:14.304
Okay.


00:20:34.066 --> 00:20:37.092
You know, if he comes any closer,
I might be able to get that gun.


00:20:37.202 --> 00:20:39.397
- Don't get any ideas.
- I'm not.


00:20:39.504 --> 00:20:42.098
I killed a guard
escaping from prison in Montana.


00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:44.175
I'm not doing anything, okay?


00:20:44.276 --> 00:20:46.437
I'm not afraid to kill again.


00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.277
Look away.


00:20:56.555 --> 00:20:58.921
What was the name of that prison?


00:21:02.728 --> 00:21:05.288
Hey, you said it was in Montana, right?


00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:08.092
I'm taking your car.


00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.100
I'm going to Mexico.


00:21:10.202 --> 00:21:12.261
We didn't complain
when you tied our hands.


00:21:12.371 --> 00:21:14.339
Okay, you have everything that I have.


00:21:14.439 --> 00:21:17.272
We have done everything
that you've asked.


00:21:17.376 --> 00:21:18.707
It's okay. It's okay.


00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:21.074
She tied you loose, didn't she?


00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:26.342
Get on your stomach
so I can tie your feet.


00:21:26.451 --> 00:21:28.919
Okay.
It gets really cold out here at night.


00:21:29.021 --> 00:21:30.579
We could freeze.


00:21:38.997 --> 00:21:40.692
Okay, you all done?


00:21:42.734 --> 00:21:44.429
You know,
just because people are gonna ask,


00:21:44.536 --> 00:21:46.595
was that thing even loaded?


00:21:57.582 --> 00:21:58.879
It's okay.


00:21:59.618 --> 00:22:01.643
This is all gonna be okay.


00:22:30.649 --> 00:22:34.278
<i>Dispatch, this is 43L2,</i>
<i>heading south on Knoxville Road.</i>


00:22:34.386 --> 00:22:38.083
<i>I've got an abandoned white</i>
<i>VW Karmann-Ghia...</i>


00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:53.967
<i>Napa Police Department.</i>


00:22:54.072 --> 00:22:58.304
<i>I want to report a murder.</i>
<i>No, a double murder.</i>


00:22:59.845 --> 00:23:03.144
<i>They are two miles north</i>
<i>of park headquarters.</i>


00:23:03.248 --> 00:23:06.809
<i>They were in a white</i>
<i>Volkswagen Karmann-Ghia.</i>


00:23:08.387 --> 00:23:10.446
<i>I'm the one that did it.</i>


00:23:10.555 --> 00:23:12.614
<i>43L2 has a male victim with him.</i>


00:23:12.724 --> 00:23:15.318
<i>Piner's ambulance</i>
<i>has been dispatched.</i>


00:23:16.294 --> 00:23:18.455
Boy lived, the girl didn't. Again.


00:23:18.563 --> 00:23:20.929
God, can you imagine
surviving something like that?


00:23:21.032 --> 00:23:22.431
Writing the dates on the side of the car.


00:23:22.534 --> 00:23:25.628
We got two Vallejo killings,
now there's one in Napa. Why Napa?


00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:27.637
What the hell is he doing out of Vallejo?


00:23:27.739 --> 00:23:31.197
Sweet mother of Christ,
what are you drawing?


00:23:31.309 --> 00:23:32.799
Kid at the lake.


00:23:32.911 --> 00:23:34.708
This is what he said
the Zodiac was wearing.


00:23:34.813 --> 00:23:36.041
God, that's a hell of a get-up.


00:23:36.148 --> 00:23:38.742
- Paul, what are you doing?
- Hyman, I wrote it. It's done.


00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:39.908
Now I just got to type it up.


00:23:40.018 --> 00:23:42.145
Type it up?
It's not finished until you type it up.


00:23:42.254 --> 00:23:44.017
We've got to read it.


00:23:46.658 --> 00:23:49.456
- What's that?
- That's the Zodiac at the lake.


00:23:49.561 --> 00:23:50.994
What's the story with the kid?


00:23:51.096 --> 00:23:53.462
He seems a little touched
or medicated or...


00:23:53.565 --> 00:23:54.691
- Graysmith?
- Yeah, what is it?


00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:56.290
He's a fucking boy scout.


00:23:56.401 --> 00:23:58.596
He doesn't smoke,
he doesn't drink, he doesn't curse.


00:23:58.703 --> 00:24:00.136
- And he's back.
- I knew it.


00:24:00.238 --> 00:24:01.569
"Man is the most
dangerous animal of all."


00:24:01.673 --> 00:24:02.765
I knew that
I heard that from somewhere.


00:24:02.874 --> 00:24:05.172
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>


00:24:05.277 --> 00:24:08.246
It's a movie about a Count
who hunts people for sport.


00:24:08.346 --> 00:24:09.370
People.


00:24:09.481 --> 00:24:11.449
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>


00:24:12.217 --> 00:24:14.651
- Who's that?
- That's Count Zaroff.


00:24:14.753 --> 00:24:16.846
Zaroff? With a "Z"?


00:24:19.524 --> 00:24:21.253
<i>And that will be</i>
<i>all for the news on the 20.</i>


00:24:21.359 --> 00:24:23.850
<i>We've got curfews in effect tonight</i>
<i>for the following counties,</i>


00:24:23.962 --> 00:24:27.898
<i>Napa, Solano, Contra Costa,</i>
<i>Alameda, Marin, and San Mateo.</i>


00:24:27.999 --> 00:24:30.126
<i>So please, everyone, stay safe.</i>


00:24:30.235 --> 00:24:33.534
<i>Vic in San Francisco, you're on the line.</i>
<i>You're not scared of the Zodiac?</i>


00:24:33.638 --> 00:24:36.698
<i>Heck no,</i>
<i>he's only shooting those farm kids.</i>


00:24:36.808 --> 00:24:39.402
<i>What scares me</i>
<i>is those hippies out in the Haight</i>


00:24:39.511 --> 00:24:41.376
<i>with their free love and weird clothes.</i>


00:24:41.480 --> 00:24:43.471
<i>We've got Alfred from Vacaville.</i>


00:24:43.582 --> 00:24:45.846
<i>You know, I think</i>
<i>that was really offensive.</i>


00:24:45.951 --> 00:24:47.578
<i>It's not just farm kids.</i>


00:24:47.686 --> 00:24:49.551
<i>These are nice, clean-cut young people.</i>


00:24:49.654 --> 00:24:52.088
<i>Hey, nobody's downplaying</i>
<i>the loss of human life here, Alfred.</i>


00:24:52.190 --> 00:24:54.181
<i>Well, that last guy was.</i>


00:24:54.292 --> 00:24:57.125
<i>We have good solid communities</i>
<i>out here in the North Bay.</i>


00:24:57.229 --> 00:25:00.756
<i>Unlike in the city where you have</i>
<i>Satanists running around.</i>


00:25:00.866 --> 00:25:04.324
<i>Well, you bring up a good question.</i>
<i>Is the Zodiac a Satanist?</i>


00:25:04.436 --> 00:25:06.131
<i>Amber from Oakland,</i>
<i>what do you think?</i>


00:25:06.238 --> 00:25:07.432
<i>I don't really know,</i>


00:25:07.539 --> 00:25:10.633
<i>but I thought that code</i>
<i>they printed didn't look very Christian.</i>


00:25:10.742 --> 00:25:13.438
<i>But I think the bigger problem</i>
<i>is that the papers shouldn't have printed</i>


00:25:13.545 --> 00:25:15.376
<i>anything that the Zodiac</i>
<i>has been doing.</i>


00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:18.608
<i>That they're just printing</i>
<i>all that stuff to sell more newspapers.</i>


00:25:18.717 --> 00:25:20.878
<i>Well, the Zodiac did demand</i>
<i>they print his letters</i>


00:25:20.986 --> 00:25:22.578
<i>or he'd kill more people.</i>


00:25:22.687 --> 00:25:23.984
<i>Yeah, but he would have</i>
<i>done it anyway,</i>


00:25:24.089 --> 00:25:25.647
<i>whether they printed it or not, I think.</i>


00:25:25.757 --> 00:25:27.190
<i>An interesting point.</i>


00:25:27.292 --> 00:25:29.453
<i>So, what do you think he'll do next?</i>


00:25:50.181 --> 00:25:53.548
- <i>San Francisco Police Department.</i>
- <i>Yes. There's a fight in a cab!</i>


00:25:53.652 --> 00:25:54.880
<i>What is your location?</i>


00:25:54.986 --> 00:25:57.955
<i>3398 Washington,</i>
<i>at the corner of Cherry.</i>


00:25:58.056 --> 00:25:59.785
<i>One's drunk and</i>
<i>we think he's robbing him.</i>


00:25:59.891 --> 00:26:03.224
- <i>Is the crime still in progress?</i>
- <i>Yes, please hurry.</i>


00:26:04.729 --> 00:26:06.321
Oh, my God, look!


00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:30.448
Nuts!


00:26:33.758 --> 00:26:35.555
Whoever this is,
you owe me a new lamp.


00:26:35.660 --> 00:26:38.288
<i>Cabbie's been shot</i>
<i>three blocks from the Presidio.</i>


00:26:38.396 --> 00:26:40.591
Well, it wasn't me.
I've been with my bride all night.


00:26:40.699 --> 00:26:43.668
- She can vouch.
- Go put on the Folgers.


00:26:43.768 --> 00:26:45.167
<i>You'll pick me up?</i>


00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.101
Let me just describe
the lamp you're gonna buy me.


00:26:55.947 --> 00:26:58.882
- I just got to sleep.
- Suspect's Negro, male adult.


00:26:58.984 --> 00:27:01.885
Walt's on scene, locked up the cab
and secured the crowd.


00:27:01.987 --> 00:27:04.478
Seriously, dead asleep.
I lost feeling in my arm and everything.


00:27:04.589 --> 00:27:05.886
Crackers.


00:27:09.761 --> 00:27:11.752
You ever try Japanese food?


00:27:11.863 --> 00:27:14.525
- What do you mean, like teriyaki?
- No, like the urchin.


00:27:14.633 --> 00:27:16.999
- Raw fish.
- I'm eating here, Bill.


00:27:18.370 --> 00:27:21.339
- I always wanted to try it.
- So, why don't you?


00:27:21.439 --> 00:27:23.407
Haven't got around to it.


00:27:39.024 --> 00:27:42.152
Evening, gents. What a lovely night
for a botched robbery.


00:27:42.260 --> 00:27:44.820
Yeah, third this week.
Must be end of summer rush.


00:27:44.929 --> 00:27:48.057
I got foot patrols going through the park,
dogs are on the way.


00:27:48.166 --> 00:27:52.466
The victim's name is Paul Stine.
Dousette pronounced him at 10:10.


00:27:52.570 --> 00:27:54.663
Suspect fired one shot
to the back of the head.


00:27:54.773 --> 00:27:56.673
Driver's wallet
and car keys are missing.


00:27:56.775 --> 00:27:57.799
How'd you know his name?


00:27:57.909 --> 00:28:00.844
Leroy, there, came down
from Yellow Cab to ID him.


00:28:00.945 --> 00:28:02.503
Neighborhood's pretty high-end
for this kind of thing,


00:28:02.614 --> 00:28:04.809
so I already set up transpo for the cab.


00:28:04.916 --> 00:28:06.383
- Coroner's here.
- Any witnesses?


00:28:06.484 --> 00:28:09.920
Kids who called it in
saw the suspect from that window.


00:28:10.021 --> 00:28:11.511
- Did they hear a shot?
- No.


00:28:11.623 --> 00:28:12.715
They first saw him in the front seat,


00:28:12.824 --> 00:28:14.724
thought he was a drunk
fighting with the driver.


00:28:14.826 --> 00:28:17.795
Oldest kid ran downstairs to get
a better look from the dining room,


00:28:17.896 --> 00:28:19.693
described him as a white male, glasses,


00:28:19.798 --> 00:28:21.993
crew-cut, stocky,
and wearing a dark jacket.


00:28:22.100 --> 00:28:23.897
Wait, I thought someone said
he was black.


00:28:24.002 --> 00:28:25.902
That's the description
that went out to radio cars.


00:28:26.004 --> 00:28:28.939
- We already corrected it.
- Oh, well, that's good.


00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:31.406
- You guys need anything else?
- No. Get out of here.


00:28:31.509 --> 00:28:33.443
Thanks. Happy Birthday.


00:28:33.545 --> 00:28:36.241
- Wait, it's your birthday?
- Yep.


00:28:36.347 --> 00:28:38.474
- That's great. Happy birthday.
- Thanks.


00:28:38.583 --> 00:28:41.575
- Body or scene?
- It's your birthday, I'll take the body.


00:28:41.686 --> 00:28:43.813
Dave, looks like he
wiped the cab down pretty good.


00:28:43.922 --> 00:28:46.322
- We got some blood over here.
- Prints?


00:28:46.424 --> 00:28:48.289
Could very well be.
We'll dust it at the Hall.


00:28:48.393 --> 00:28:51.123
The odd thing is, we also got gloves.


00:28:51.229 --> 00:28:53.629
- Suspect's?
- There's blood on them.


00:28:55.066 --> 00:28:56.260
- Hey, Pete?
- Yeah, Dave.


00:28:56.367 --> 00:28:57.527
You through over there,
can I get in there?


00:28:57.635 --> 00:28:59.262
Yeah, I'm all set.


00:29:00.238 --> 00:29:02.229
- Who rolled him?
- Stewarts.


00:29:09.147 --> 00:29:11.138
I got a single 9mm casing.


00:29:15.653 --> 00:29:17.018
Yeah, Luger.


00:29:17.622 --> 00:29:19.453
Nothing from the crowd.


00:29:19.557 --> 00:29:22.424
Okay.
I'm your shooter, Negro male adult,


00:29:22.527 --> 00:29:25.860
who also happens to be
a stocky, crew-cut Caucasian.


00:29:25.964 --> 00:29:28.489
I flag a cab. I give him this address.


00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:31.364
Did I give him this address?
Who's got the fare book?


00:29:31.469 --> 00:29:32.800
Right here.


00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:38.007
Washington and Maple.
That's one block east.


00:29:59.130 --> 00:30:00.290
Lighting's the same over here,


00:30:00.398 --> 00:30:02.832
so maybe I see
someone walking their dog.


00:30:02.934 --> 00:30:05.767
You don't want any witnesses
so you tell him to go down a block.


00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:06.928
He pulls over.


00:30:07.038 --> 00:30:08.972
I wait for him to put it in park
because I'm smart


00:30:09.073 --> 00:30:10.370
and I don't want him
hitting the accelerator


00:30:10.475 --> 00:30:11.737
when I shoot him. May I?


00:30:11.843 --> 00:30:14.209
He stops, puts it in park, boom.


00:30:14.312 --> 00:30:17.008
I shoot him on the right side,
he slumps right?


00:30:17.115 --> 00:30:19.106
Maybe you've got your hand
on his collar when you shoot.


00:30:19.217 --> 00:30:20.377
All right. So, either way,


00:30:20.485 --> 00:30:22.180
I just dumped a quart of blood
in the front seat.


00:30:22.287 --> 00:30:25.415
- So, why do you get in the front seat?
- For the money.


00:30:25.523 --> 00:30:26.547
But he's dead.


00:30:26.658 --> 00:30:28.353
You could just reach over the seat,
pull out his wallet.


00:30:28.459 --> 00:30:30.620
You don't have to go
anywhere near the blood.


00:30:30.728 --> 00:30:33.196
So, why'd he get in the front seat?


00:30:33.731 --> 00:30:35.323
- I'm an idiot.
- But you're not an idiot.


00:30:35.433 --> 00:30:37.162
You waited for him to put it in park.


00:30:37.268 --> 00:30:39.463
- Right. Thank you.
- Yeah, sure.


00:30:41.206 --> 00:30:43.037
- Can I see that?
- Yeah.


00:30:43.575 --> 00:30:46.840
I am an idiot.
I just killed a man for $8.25.


00:30:46.945 --> 00:30:51.245
It's his third fare of the night.
Does anyone have any animal crackers?


00:30:51.783 --> 00:30:53.978
- Animal crackers?
- They're in the car.


00:30:54.085 --> 00:30:56.280
I'm saving those for later.


00:30:56.387 --> 00:30:57.547
Fine.


00:31:02.026 --> 00:31:05.723
- Are you a reporter?
- No, I'm Inspector Dave Toschi, SFPD.


00:31:05.830 --> 00:31:08.355
Sir, I was wondering
if I'd be able to talk to your children,


00:31:08.466 --> 00:31:10.696
one at a time and preferably alone?


00:31:10.802 --> 00:31:13.066
They just saw a man murdered.


00:31:13.171 --> 00:31:14.263
I understand.


00:31:14.639 --> 00:31:16.300
It looked like
they were drunk and fighting.


00:31:16.407 --> 00:31:17.704
Yeah, and he had a rag.


00:31:17.809 --> 00:31:20.175
He came around the side of the car
and he was wiping stuff.


00:31:20.278 --> 00:31:23.611
- Did you get a chance to see his face?
- I did.


00:31:23.715 --> 00:31:25.205
Well, sort of.


00:31:26.484 --> 00:31:28.975
Did you remember what he looked like?


00:31:30.488 --> 00:31:32.479
- Normal.
- Yeah.


00:31:32.590 --> 00:31:33.887
"Normal?"


00:31:56.614 --> 00:31:58.172
<i>"This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


00:31:58.283 --> 00:32:00.649
<i>"I am the murderer of the taxi driver</i>


00:32:00.752 --> 00:32:04.188
"over by Washington Street
and Maple Street last night.


00:32:04.289 --> 00:32:06.723
"To prove this, here is
a blood-stained piece of his shirt.


00:32:06.824 --> 00:32:11.761
"I am the same man who did in
the people in the North Bay Area.


00:32:11.863 --> 00:32:14.423
"The S.F. Police could have
caught me last night


00:32:14.532 --> 00:32:16.056
"if they had searched the park properly


00:32:16.167 --> 00:32:19.432
"instead of holding road races
with their motorcicles."


00:32:19.537 --> 00:32:21.027
- Gentlemen.
- Dave.


00:32:21.139 --> 00:32:23.073
Paul. Where's the shirt?


00:32:24.509 --> 00:32:26.170
Right there, boss.


00:32:27.312 --> 00:32:28.870
There's your rag the kids talked about.


00:32:28.980 --> 00:32:30.971
So he got in the front seat
to tear off a piece of the shirt.


00:32:31.082 --> 00:32:33.482
- Is this on the record?
- Well, what do you think?


00:32:33.584 --> 00:32:35.609
He confirms
the Vallejo and Napa killings.


00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:37.278
Gets worse.


00:32:37.388 --> 00:32:39.413
Robert, do you have a deadline?


00:32:39.524 --> 00:32:41.651
What does he mean, it gets worse?


00:32:41.759 --> 00:32:43.158
Read the last part.


00:32:43.261 --> 00:32:45.491
"School children make nice targets.


00:32:45.596 --> 00:32:47.894
"I think I shall wipe out
a school bus some morning.


00:32:47.999 --> 00:32:49.660
"Just shoot out the front tire


00:32:49.767 --> 00:32:52.167
"and then pick off the kiddies
as they come bouncing out."


00:32:52.270 --> 00:32:54.795
Jesus Christ, who's got school buses?
Department of Transportation?


00:32:54.906 --> 00:32:56.806
- School board.
- All right.


00:32:56.908 --> 00:32:59.172
I'm gonna need elimination prints
from your staff.


00:32:59.277 --> 00:33:02.007
Has anyone here
didn't touch this letter?


00:33:06.250 --> 00:33:08.411
On my way back to my desk.
They have phones, if you want.


00:33:08.519 --> 00:33:10.111
We need to get matches
on blood and fabric.


00:33:10.221 --> 00:33:11.381
I'll call Napa and Vallejo,


00:33:11.489 --> 00:33:13.286
get the letters up to Sherwood
in Sacramento.


00:33:13.391 --> 00:33:16.792
Dave, just one thing.
Is it true they got a print off the cab?


00:33:16.894 --> 00:33:19.226
Yeah, we got a partial in blood.


00:33:20.098 --> 00:33:23.226
- But that is not for publication.
- Hey, hey, come on.


00:33:23.334 --> 00:33:25.564
Hey, it's me.


00:33:25.670 --> 00:33:27.763
Did he say they got a print?


00:33:28.873 --> 00:33:30.067
Partial.


00:33:31.075 --> 00:33:32.133
Whoa.


00:33:33.511 --> 00:33:34.876
Dude, he wears his gun like Bullitt.


00:33:34.979 --> 00:33:37.470
No, McQueen got that from Toschi.


00:33:37.582 --> 00:33:39.345
Does he think that Zodiac's
gonna send another code?


00:33:39.450 --> 00:33:41.247
'Cause I think Zodiac's
gonna send another code.


00:33:41.352 --> 00:33:43.377
Jesus Harold Christ
on rubber crutches, Bobby.


00:33:43.488 --> 00:33:44.512
What are you doing?


00:33:44.622 --> 00:33:45.919
You're doing that thing,
the thing we discussed,


00:33:46.024 --> 00:33:48.515
the thing that I don't like.
Starts with an "L."


00:33:48.626 --> 00:33:50.526
- Oh, looming.
- Yeah.


00:33:50.628 --> 00:33:53.529
In cooperation with SFPD,
we will run the Zodiac letter


00:33:53.631 --> 00:33:56.293
without including the threat
on school children.


00:33:56.401 --> 00:33:58.062
We don't want to start a city-wide panic


00:33:58.169 --> 00:34:01.661
so I'm asking all of you
to please keep this confidential.


00:34:01.773 --> 00:34:03.968
Just go about your daily business.


00:34:04.075 --> 00:34:05.406
Thank you.


00:34:21.125 --> 00:34:24.117
I packed you your carrots
and your soda and peanut butter, okay?


00:34:24.228 --> 00:34:27.220
- Dad, you don't have to wait with me.
- I know.


00:34:34.572 --> 00:34:38.372
You know what? You know what?
I'm gonna drive him today, okay?


00:34:38.876 --> 00:34:40.070
Come on.


00:34:58.129 --> 00:34:59.790
What's that?


00:34:59.897 --> 00:35:02.422
Similarities in the lowercase "r's."


00:35:11.609 --> 00:35:12.735
And that?


00:35:12.844 --> 00:35:14.812
It is you waiting in the hall
if you speak again.


00:35:14.912 --> 00:35:16.743
I have to concentrate.


00:35:17.148 --> 00:35:18.240
Sorry.


00:35:18.349 --> 00:35:20.476
"Sorry" counts as speaking.


00:35:31.229 --> 00:35:34.198
There are similarities
in the lowercase "r's."


00:35:38.269 --> 00:35:40.703
We have to release the bus threat.


00:35:41.305 --> 00:35:43.933
- It'll screw us.
- We're already screwed.


00:35:44.041 --> 00:35:46.271
We just went from
"Routine Cabbie Shooting"


00:35:46.377 --> 00:35:48.538
to "Mass Murderer Targets Kids."


00:35:56.354 --> 00:35:59.414
<i>The Zodiac Killer</i>
<i>has come to San Francisco.</i>


00:35:59.524 --> 00:36:00.513
<i>Confirmation tonight,</i>


00:36:00.625 --> 00:36:02.559
<i>from the San Francisco</i>
<i>Police Department</i>


00:36:02.660 --> 00:36:04.594
<i>that in his latest haunting letter,</i>


00:36:04.695 --> 00:36:07.892
<i>which takes credit for the murder</i>
<i>of cab driver Paul Stine,</i>


00:36:07.999 --> 00:36:11.366
<i>the Zodiac has threatened to,</i>
<i>"Wipe out a school bus</i>


00:36:11.469 --> 00:36:14.802
<i>"and pick off the kiddies</i>
<i>as they come bouncing out."</i>


00:36:18.276 --> 00:36:20.938
<i>If you think you might know</i>
<i>who the Zodiac is,</i>


00:36:21.045 --> 00:36:25.175
<i>you can call the San Francisco</i>
<i>Police Department's newest tip line.</i>


00:36:48.339 --> 00:36:51.570
Press conference is at 4:00.
We got to give them something.


00:36:51.676 --> 00:36:53.109
We're coordinating
with the school board,


00:36:53.211 --> 00:36:55.076
and we expect
a break in the case very soon.


00:36:55.179 --> 00:36:56.942
- What do we really got?
- We're swamped.


00:36:57.048 --> 00:36:58.413
When they can't get anyone
on the tip line


00:36:58.516 --> 00:37:00.211
they call the switchboard
and keep getting put through.


00:37:00.318 --> 00:37:01.307
You got any hard suspects?


00:37:01.419 --> 00:37:04.115
About 90 an hour. I'm up to around 500.


00:37:04.222 --> 00:37:05.348
Well, can't you narrow it down?


00:37:05.456 --> 00:37:07.617
I would love to,
if I could get out of this...


00:37:07.725 --> 00:37:11.217
- Homicide, please hold.
- Yeah, hold, please.


00:37:11.329 --> 00:37:13.024
We're gonna need to tell them
we got the entire force on this.


00:37:13.130 --> 00:37:14.427
How many men can you give me?


00:37:14.532 --> 00:37:16.523
Well, right now, it's you and Bill
and Monday's a school day.


00:37:16.634 --> 00:37:18.534
Yeah, I know, Chief.
I have three daughters of my own.


00:37:18.636 --> 00:37:20.570
Yeah, I know. Where's Armstrong?


00:37:20.671 --> 00:37:22.138
He's on the phone with Vallejo.


00:37:22.240 --> 00:37:24.174
We're playing catch up, Jack.


00:37:24.275 --> 00:37:26.766
I'd like to set up a meeting
with your survivor, Michael Mageau.


00:37:26.877 --> 00:37:28.469
I can't. He skipped town.


00:37:28.579 --> 00:37:31.207
The only guy who's seen Zodiac
without a mask is missing?


00:37:31.315 --> 00:37:34.443
When he was still in the hospital
we could show him lineups all day long.


00:37:34.552 --> 00:37:35.951
As soon as he got out, he split.


00:37:36.053 --> 00:37:37.077
<i>Really? Why?</i>


00:37:37.188 --> 00:37:39.383
I don't think he wanted
to have anything to do with this.


00:37:39.490 --> 00:37:41.651
<i>Can you send us everything</i>
<i>that you have?</i>


00:37:41.759 --> 00:37:44.489
Well, the road goes both ways.


00:37:44.595 --> 00:37:47.723
Now, we need that print
you lifted from the cab


00:37:47.832 --> 00:37:49.766
<i>and we should have been in</i>
<i>on the handwriting.</i>


00:37:49.867 --> 00:37:52.131
I apologize.
Things have been moving fast.


00:37:52.236 --> 00:37:54.966
<i>Who should I talk to in Napa</i>
<i>so we can coordinate?</i>


00:37:55.072 --> 00:37:56.198
Talk to Ken Narlow.


00:37:56.307 --> 00:37:58.172
We really should have been in
on the handwriting.


00:37:58.276 --> 00:38:00.744
<i>I apologize.</i>
<i>Things have been moving fast.</i>


00:38:00.845 --> 00:38:02.278
<i>Listen, we're gonna need</i>
<i>your scene photos.</i>


00:38:02.380 --> 00:38:03.404
Can't help you.


00:38:03.514 --> 00:38:05.448
<i>Ken, I don't want to get into</i>
<i>a jurisdictional thing here.</i>


00:38:05.549 --> 00:38:08.143
No, no, no, no, no.
We didn't have a crime scene.


00:38:08.252 --> 00:38:11.483
The ranger that found the kids literally
swept everything into a picnic blanket.


00:38:11.589 --> 00:38:13.284
<i>All we have are the Wing Walker prints.</i>


00:38:13.391 --> 00:38:14.483
The what?


00:38:14.592 --> 00:38:16.287
Boot prints to and from the crime scene


00:38:16.394 --> 00:38:17.986
were made by size
10-and-a-half Wing Walkers,


00:38:18.095 --> 00:38:21.553
military-style boots
sold only at military PXs


00:38:22.066 --> 00:38:23.863
designed to walk
on the wings of planes.


00:38:23.968 --> 00:38:26.698
<i>And you can't buy at a PX</i>
<i>without a military ID,</i>


00:38:26.804 --> 00:38:28.738
so our suspect could be military.


00:38:28.839 --> 00:38:30.602
Did you guys narrow your list off of this?


00:38:30.708 --> 00:38:32.801
- Yeah.
- <i>Did Vallejo?</i>


00:38:32.910 --> 00:38:35.003
I don't know. I don't work in Vallejo.
I work here.


00:38:35.112 --> 00:38:37.239
Great. I'm gonna need photos
of those boot prints.


00:38:37.348 --> 00:38:39.316
<i>Sure, if you send me the handwriting.</i>


00:38:39.417 --> 00:38:41.009
I thought Questioned Documents
already did.


00:38:41.118 --> 00:38:42.608
Nope. Vallejo's got them, not us.


00:38:42.720 --> 00:38:44.711
All right.
I'll have Questioned Documents...


00:38:44.822 --> 00:38:46.722
Forget it. I'll telefax it to you.


00:38:46.824 --> 00:38:48.291
We don't have telefax yet.


00:38:48.392 --> 00:38:50.986
- Okay, I'll put it in the mail.
- <i>We'll mail ours, too.</i>


00:38:51.095 --> 00:38:52.756
And call Mulanax in Vallejo.


00:38:52.863 --> 00:38:54.956
- Maybe he can get you a mimeo.
- Right.


00:38:55.066 --> 00:38:57.432
Why don't you just get a photo
off the original plaster cast?


00:38:57.535 --> 00:38:59.628
We'd have to wait,
because they don't have a fax.


00:38:59.737 --> 00:39:01.170
<i>We don't have a fax, either.</i>


00:39:01.272 --> 00:39:03.001
Look, I'm just trying
to get us coordinated.


00:39:03.107 --> 00:39:04.574
Have you called Solano Sheriff's Office?


00:39:04.675 --> 00:39:06.302
Why would I call Solano?


00:39:06.410 --> 00:39:10.005
<i>Because the two kids that got killed</i>
<i>last Christmas were Solano's.</i>


00:39:10.114 --> 00:39:11.308
I thought they were Vallejo.


00:39:11.415 --> 00:39:12.712
No, they were over the county line


00:39:12.817 --> 00:39:15.012
so you're gonna need
to coordinate with them, too.


00:39:15.119 --> 00:39:16.552
Okay.


00:39:16.654 --> 00:39:17.746
Bill.


00:39:18.456 --> 00:39:20.321
Can I have a word with you?


00:39:23.260 --> 00:39:25.353
Where did you see this guy?


00:39:26.163 --> 00:39:28.597
We got the call to circle the scene
and look for a Negro male adult.


00:39:28.699 --> 00:39:30.166
Where was he?


00:39:30.267 --> 00:39:32.701
On Jackson. Heading east.
About the middle of the block.


00:39:32.803 --> 00:39:33.237
And this is three minutes
after the shooting?


00:39:33.237 --> 00:39:34.829
And this is three minutes
after the shooting?


00:39:34.939 --> 00:39:36.099
Give or take. Yeah.


00:39:36.207 --> 00:39:38.437
- And you were heading east or west?
- We were going west.


00:39:38.542 --> 00:39:40.772
All right, so you're
on Jackson going west.


00:39:40.878 --> 00:39:44.006
So the cab was one block
catty-corner southwest?


00:39:44.115 --> 00:39:45.776
- Correct.
- Did you slow down?


00:39:45.883 --> 00:39:47.612
- Of course we slowed down.
- All right.


00:39:47.718 --> 00:39:49.948
Listen, Dispatch said
it was a Negro male.


00:39:50.054 --> 00:39:51.316
That was corrected.


00:39:51.422 --> 00:39:54.084
No, but at the time
they hadn't changed it.


00:39:54.191 --> 00:39:56.250
This guy was white.


00:39:56.360 --> 00:39:58.191
Right, not in a hurry.
Kind of lumbering along like...


00:39:58.295 --> 00:40:01.093
Lumbering?
What do you mean, "lumbering"?


00:40:02.199 --> 00:40:04.895
- Shuffling.
- Stocky? Had a crew cut?


00:40:05.870 --> 00:40:08.100
Yeah, that's all correct.


00:40:08.205 --> 00:40:09.934
Listen, it was dark.


00:40:10.875 --> 00:40:12.900
The guy was wearing a dark jacket.
There's no way...


00:40:13.010 --> 00:40:15.501
He would have been covered in blood.


00:40:17.114 --> 00:40:18.706
Did you stop him?


00:40:20.785 --> 00:40:22.548
Did you talk to him?


00:40:23.154 --> 00:40:25.088
- Yes? No?
- No.


00:40:25.990 --> 00:40:27.480
You need to get with a sketch artist.


00:40:27.591 --> 00:40:30.583
We have to put out
a new composite right away.


00:40:33.697 --> 00:40:36.632
<i>Five persons have been murdered</i>
<i>in the San Francisco area,</i>


00:40:36.734 --> 00:40:38.133
<i>and in each case the killer...</i>


00:40:38.235 --> 00:40:40.726
<i>"I shall wipe out a school bus</i>
<i>some morning..."</i>


00:40:40.838 --> 00:40:42.465
<i>San Francisco police...</i>


00:40:44.341 --> 00:40:46.866
<i>... to see the Stones in concert</i>
<i>this Sunday.</i>


00:40:47.178 --> 00:40:49.237
<i>The new letters</i>
<i>from the Zodiac Killer were sent to</i>


00:40:49.346 --> 00:40:51.371
<i>the City room of the</i>
San Francisco Chronicle.


00:40:51.482 --> 00:40:52.642
<i>One of the letters was...</i>


00:40:52.750 --> 00:40:55.275
Looming. No looming.


00:40:55.386 --> 00:40:58.480
- Have you considered the water theory?
- What?


00:40:58.589 --> 00:41:01.422
Geographically, every attack
takes place near a body of water


00:41:01.525 --> 00:41:02.651
- or a water-based name.
- This is your water theory?


00:41:02.760 --> 00:41:05.194
Lake Berryessa. Blue Rock Springs.


00:41:05.296 --> 00:41:07.924
- Lake Herman.
- Wash-ington and Cherry?


00:41:09.433 --> 00:41:11.025
You think?


00:41:11.135 --> 00:41:12.159
No.


00:41:12.269 --> 00:41:13.668
I'm reading this book,


00:41:13.771 --> 00:41:15.398
<i>Homicide Investigation</i>
by Lemoyne Snyder...


00:41:15.506 --> 00:41:16.905
- "Leymone."
...and he says you look for patterns,


00:41:17.007 --> 00:41:19.100
- so I'm looking for patterns.
- No.


00:41:19.210 --> 00:41:21.542
You can't think of this case
in normal police terms.


00:41:21.645 --> 00:41:23.806
- Why not?
- You got four crime scenes.


00:41:23.914 --> 00:41:26.815
Solano, Vallejo, Berryessa, and here.


00:41:26.917 --> 00:41:30.614
Not a single usable print
at the first three or in any of the letters?


00:41:31.088 --> 00:41:34.546
How does our master criminal come
to the city and leave a bloody latent?


00:41:34.658 --> 00:41:37.218
I mean, assuming the gloves are his,


00:41:37.328 --> 00:41:39.023
he shoots the cabbie
and then takes them off?


00:41:39.129 --> 00:41:40.289
<i>So it's not his print?</i>


00:41:40.397 --> 00:41:42.160
Maybe, maybe not.
You're missing the point.


00:41:42.266 --> 00:41:44.860
- The point is the first attack...
- David Faraday and Betty Jensen.


00:41:44.969 --> 00:41:46.527
They both die.


00:41:46.637 --> 00:41:49.105
From there on out,
he only manages to kill the girls.


00:41:49.206 --> 00:41:51.140
- Not for lack of trying.
- Not for lack of trying.


00:41:51.242 --> 00:41:54.769
Mageau lives, Ferrin dies.
Hartnell lives, Shepard dies.


00:41:54.879 --> 00:41:58.246
He gets so caught up with the women
he forgets to finish off the men.


00:41:58.349 --> 00:42:00.681
Plus, they're all couples
and all on lover's lanes.


00:42:00.784 --> 00:42:02.615
- Paul Stine is not.
- Exactly.


00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:04.915
Single, male cab driver
on Washington and Cherry doesn't fit.


00:42:05.022 --> 00:42:06.387
Doesn't fit.


00:42:07.291 --> 00:42:09.555
So, why does Zodiac kill him?


00:42:12.396 --> 00:42:14.387
He's breaking the pattern.


00:42:23.607 --> 00:42:24.631
Yeah?


00:42:24.742 --> 00:42:28.439
<i>Someone claiming to be Zodiac</i>
<i>called Oakland PD a half-hour ago.</i>


00:42:28.546 --> 00:42:31.811
<i>He says he's gonna call in on Jim</i>
<i>Dunbar's morning show in three hours.</i>


00:42:31.916 --> 00:42:32.974
On television?


00:42:33.083 --> 00:42:35.142
<i>He wants Melvin Belli on</i>
<i>to counsel him.</i>


00:42:35.252 --> 00:42:37.345
All right. All right.
Let's go wake up Melvin.


00:42:39.823 --> 00:42:41.688
Animal crackers?


00:42:41.792 --> 00:42:43.089
Glove box.


00:42:43.193 --> 00:42:44.888
Are these windows bulletproof?


00:42:44.995 --> 00:42:47.520
Yes, Melvin.
You don't have to lie down back there.


00:42:47.631 --> 00:42:48.825
This man is a marksman,


00:42:48.933 --> 00:42:51.766
could snuff me out
at a moment's notice.


00:42:51.869 --> 00:42:53.234
Are you sure you're up for this?


00:42:53.337 --> 00:42:57.774
Don't you worry about me, Inspector.
I'll be fine when the lights are on.


00:42:57.875 --> 00:42:59.604
This man has asked for my help.


00:42:59.710 --> 00:43:01.769
The man you're worrying about
snuffing you out?


00:43:01.879 --> 00:43:03.813
What are these, cookies?


00:43:05.549 --> 00:43:07.642
Dear Lord, do you ever clean this car?


00:43:07.952 --> 00:43:11.388
- Shit.
- KGO must have tipped other stations.


00:43:20.965 --> 00:43:23.900
<i>Get him talking.</i>
<i>Convince him to meet you somewhere.</i>


00:43:24.001 --> 00:43:25.263
If you see an opportunity,


00:43:25.369 --> 00:43:28.133
we want you to suggest
Old St. Mary's Church in Chinatown.


00:43:28.238 --> 00:43:29.398
You'll be tracing the call?


00:43:29.506 --> 00:43:32.600
Pacific Telephone says you need to
keep him on the line for 15 minutes.


00:43:32.710 --> 00:43:34.940
We can do that, can't we, Jim?


00:43:37.314 --> 00:43:39.646
Fifteen seconds. Clear the set.


00:43:46.023 --> 00:43:48.218
Here you go, you drunken reprobate.


00:43:48.325 --> 00:43:52.125
<i>We interrupt our regular program</i>
<i>to bring you this news bulletin.</i>


00:43:52.229 --> 00:43:54.197
<i>Welcome to this special edition</i>
<i>of our show</i>


00:43:54.298 --> 00:43:56.163
<i>in which we are joined</i>
<i>by attorney Melvin Belli</i>


00:43:56.266 --> 00:43:59.633
<i>who the Zodiac Killer</i>
<i>personally requested to appear.</i>


00:43:59.737 --> 00:44:01.568
Finish up, buddy, and put it in the sink.


00:44:01.672 --> 00:44:04.664
- <i>Good morning, Melvin.</i>
- <i>Good morning, Jim.</i>


00:44:04.775 --> 00:44:08.006
<i>So, the phone lines are open.</i>
<i>Mr. Belli is here.</i>


00:44:08.112 --> 00:44:09.136
<i>Here to help, Jim.</i>


00:44:09.246 --> 00:44:11.077
<i>Yes. Here to help.</i>


00:44:11.181 --> 00:44:15.880
<i>And we ask the public not to call in,</i>
<i>so that the Zodiac himself can reach us.</i>


00:44:24.962 --> 00:44:28.363
I saw your <i>Star Trek,</i> by the way.
It was excellent.


00:44:28.465 --> 00:44:30.399
A shame about the show.


00:44:30.501 --> 00:44:31.968
Good people.


00:44:32.069 --> 00:44:35.800
You know, I've often thought of
becoming an actor full-time.


00:44:35.906 --> 00:44:37.168
What was your character's name?


00:44:37.274 --> 00:44:39.469
- <i>Gorgon.</i>
- <i>Gorgon. That's right.</i>


00:44:41.011 --> 00:44:42.911
Roll the tape. Get the tape.


00:44:43.013 --> 00:44:45.641
Jim, we have a call. We're going live.


00:44:46.917 --> 00:44:48.111
Hello?


00:44:51.655 --> 00:44:53.816
Hello? This is Melvin Belli.


00:44:55.025 --> 00:44:57.050
Who am I speaking with?


00:44:57.161 --> 00:44:59.561
<i>This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


00:45:02.700 --> 00:45:06.568
Is there something I can call you
that's a little less ominous?


00:45:08.572 --> 00:45:09.596
<i>Sam.</i>


00:45:10.207 --> 00:45:12.175
Sam.


00:45:12.509 --> 00:45:16.138
Is there somewhere we can meet, Sam,
and talk about this?


00:45:16.580 --> 00:45:19.845
<i>Meet me on top of the Fairmont Hotel.</i>


00:45:19.950 --> 00:45:21.713
<i>Without anyone else or I'll jump...</i>


00:45:21.819 --> 00:45:23.616
Have a unit go to the Fairmont Hotel.


00:45:23.721 --> 00:45:25.951
- <i>Sam.</i>
- <i>Yes?</i>


00:45:26.623 --> 00:45:30.081
Do you think you need medical care?


00:45:30.194 --> 00:45:32.059
<i>Medical, not mental.</i>


00:45:32.162 --> 00:45:34.460
Do you have health problems?


00:45:34.565 --> 00:45:36.294
<i>I'm sick. I have headaches.</i>


00:45:36.400 --> 00:45:38.129
Headaches?


00:45:38.235 --> 00:45:39.566
I have headaches, too,


00:45:39.670 --> 00:45:42.366
but a chiropractor stopped them
a week ago.


00:45:42.473 --> 00:45:44.270
I think I can help you, Sam.


00:45:46.710 --> 00:45:47.972
Sam?


00:45:49.913 --> 00:45:52.381
He knows they're tracing his calls.


00:45:56.053 --> 00:46:00.080
<i>Sam, we'd like you to know</i>
<i>that we are not tracing these calls.</i>


00:46:00.190 --> 00:46:04.422
<i>It's a long, difficult process</i>
<i>and ineffective with these short calls.</i>


00:46:09.933 --> 00:46:10.991
Sam?


00:46:13.270 --> 00:46:16.364
We're not tracing these calls.
You have my word.


00:46:17.274 --> 00:46:18.434
<i>Okay.</i>


00:46:18.942 --> 00:46:22.207
<i>Sam, you need to tell me</i>
<i>what your problem is.</i>


00:46:22.312 --> 00:46:24.177
<i>I don't want to go to the gas chamber.</i>


00:46:24.281 --> 00:46:26.772
<i>I have headaches.</i>
<i>I kill, I don't get them.</i>


00:46:26.884 --> 00:46:28.215
That is fucked up!


00:46:28.318 --> 00:46:31.776
<i>You want to live, don't you?</i>
<i>Well, this is your passport.</i>


00:46:31.889 --> 00:46:33.288
<i>How long have you been</i>
<i>having these headaches?</i>


00:46:33.390 --> 00:46:35.381
<i>Since I killed a kid.</i>


00:46:36.360 --> 00:46:38.555
- Do you have blackouts?
- <i>Yes.</i>


00:46:38.662 --> 00:46:42.359
- Do you have fits?
- <i>No. I just have headaches.</i>


00:46:42.499 --> 00:46:44.091
Did you attempt to call one other time


00:46:44.201 --> 00:46:46.795
when F. Lee Bailey was with us
two or three weeks ago?


00:46:46.904 --> 00:46:47.893
<i>Yes.</i>


00:46:48.005 --> 00:46:49.836
And why did you want
to talk to Mr. Bailey?


00:46:49.940 --> 00:46:52.875
Why do you wanna talk to me, Sam?


00:46:52.976 --> 00:46:54.603
- <i>I don't want to be hurt.</i>
- Why is he calling?


00:46:54.711 --> 00:46:56.679
- Hey, just a second, buddy.
- <i>I don't wanna go to the gas chamber.</i>


00:46:56.780 --> 00:46:58.441
<i>You won't get hurt if you talk to me.</i>


00:46:58.549 --> 00:47:01.541
And you're not going
to the gas chamber.


00:47:01.652 --> 00:47:04.018
I wouldn't think they would ask
for capital punishment.


00:47:04.121 --> 00:47:06.282
<i>We should ask the District Attorney.</i>


00:47:06.390 --> 00:47:08.449
<i>Do you want me to do that, Sam?</i>


00:47:08.559 --> 00:47:11.255
<i>Do you want me to talk</i>
<i>to the District Attorney?</i>


00:47:15.165 --> 00:47:16.894
What was that, Sam?


00:47:17.868 --> 00:47:19.961
<i>I did not say anything.</i>


00:47:20.070 --> 00:47:21.970
<i>We heard a scream.</i>


00:47:22.773 --> 00:47:24.900
<i>That was my headache.</i>


00:47:25.709 --> 00:47:28.678
You sound like you're in
a great deal of pain.


00:47:29.446 --> 00:47:32.472
<i>My head aches. I'm so sick.</i>


00:47:34.351 --> 00:47:35.841
<i>I'm gonna kill them.</i>


00:47:35.953 --> 00:47:38.786
- Oh, okay.
- <i>I'm gonna kill those kids!</i>


00:47:38.889 --> 00:47:40.481
Fantastic.


00:47:43.060 --> 00:47:44.459
<i>Sam?</i>


00:47:45.996 --> 00:47:50.228
- <i>Let's meet and talk. Just us.</i>
- <i>Okay.</i>


00:47:50.367 --> 00:47:53.029
<i>How about Old St. Mary's Church</i>
<i>in Chinatown?</i>


00:47:53.136 --> 00:47:54.433
<i>No.</i>


00:47:54.538 --> 00:47:58.406
<i>In front of the Daly City</i>
<i>St. Vincent de Paul at 10:30.</i>


00:47:58.508 --> 00:48:00.237
I'll see you there.


00:48:02.012 --> 00:48:03.946
Take care of yourself, Sam.


00:48:28.272 --> 00:48:29.466
My, my, my.


00:48:29.573 --> 00:48:33.270
You fellows certainly know
how to put on a secret meeting.


00:48:35.646 --> 00:48:37.136
<i>You know, the problem is,</i>


00:48:37.247 --> 00:48:40.080
<i>I don't want to go to the gas chamber.</i>
<i>I have headaches.</i>


00:48:40.183 --> 00:48:42.208
<i>I kill, I don't get them.</i>


00:48:42.319 --> 00:48:43.946
No, it's not him.


00:48:45.022 --> 00:48:48.150
It's the voice.
The voice is too high. It's too young.


00:48:48.258 --> 00:48:50.488
All right.
Thanks for coming down, Bryan.


00:48:50.594 --> 00:48:51.856
<i>Do you have blackouts?</i>


00:48:51.962 --> 00:48:53.793
That's okay. I got it.


00:49:00.003 --> 00:49:01.027
They pulled off the trace.


00:49:01.138 --> 00:49:04.403
Our Daly City no-show
called from a mental institution.


00:49:04.508 --> 00:49:06.373
Oakland PD's operator is sure


00:49:06.476 --> 00:49:08.944
the man she talked to
had a deeper voice.


00:49:09.046 --> 00:49:10.206
Calmer.


00:49:11.048 --> 00:49:13.209
Might have actually been him.


00:49:19.456 --> 00:49:22.619
"So I shall change
my way of collecting slaves.


00:49:22.726 --> 00:49:26.218
"I shall no longer announce to anyone
when I commit my murders.


00:49:26.330 --> 00:49:29.527
"They shall look like routine robberies,
killings of anger


00:49:29.633 --> 00:49:32.602
"and a few fake accidents, et cetera.


00:49:32.703 --> 00:49:33.761
"The police shall never catch me


00:49:33.870 --> 00:49:36.270
"because I have been
too clever for them.


00:49:36.373 --> 00:49:39.900
"I look like the description passed out
only when I do my thing.


00:49:40.010 --> 00:49:43.036
"The rest of the time
I look entirely different.


00:49:43.146 --> 00:49:47.640
"I shall not tell you what
my disguise consists of when I kill.


00:49:48.251 --> 00:49:50.776
"As of yet I have left no
fingerprints behind me,


00:49:50.887 --> 00:49:53.378
"contrary to what the police say.


00:49:53.490 --> 00:49:55.856
"I wear transparent fingertips.


00:49:56.827 --> 00:50:01.560
"All it is is two coats of airplane cement
coated on my fingertips.


00:50:01.665 --> 00:50:06.125
"I enjoy needling the blue pigs.
Hey, blue pig, I was in the park.


00:50:06.236 --> 00:50:11.697
"You were using fire trucks to mask
the sound of your cruising prowl cars.


00:50:11.808 --> 00:50:13.241
"Hey, pig, doesn't it rile you up


00:50:13.343 --> 00:50:16.437
"to have your nose
rubbed in your booboos?


00:50:16.546 --> 00:50:19.606
"If you cops think I am going to take
on a bus the way I stated I was,


00:50:19.716 --> 00:50:22.913
"you deserve to have holes
in your heads."


00:50:24.888 --> 00:50:27.049
And you need to look at this.


00:50:29.926 --> 00:50:32.292
"Take one bag of
ammonium nitrate fertilizer,


00:50:32.396 --> 00:50:34.057
"one gallon of stove oil,


00:50:34.164 --> 00:50:36.291
"and dump a few bags
of gravel on top..."


00:50:36.400 --> 00:50:38.129
- Okay.
- It's a bomb.


00:50:38.235 --> 00:50:39.998
Okay. We gotta call the Army
and see if this


00:50:40.103 --> 00:50:42.833
science experiment could actually work.


00:50:42.939 --> 00:50:44.463
Another cipher.


00:50:46.710 --> 00:50:49.372
- When did these arrive?
- They arrived this morning.


00:50:49.479 --> 00:50:50.878
Are you planning to publish?


00:50:50.981 --> 00:50:52.175
Robert.


00:50:53.683 --> 00:50:55.617
We should have a drink.


00:50:59.790 --> 00:51:01.155
Thank you.


00:51:02.993 --> 00:51:05.223
So, tell me about yourself.


00:51:05.328 --> 00:51:08.820
- You married?
- Divorced. Two kids.


00:51:09.866 --> 00:51:11.731
What do you do for fun?


00:51:13.270 --> 00:51:14.897
I love to read.


00:51:15.839 --> 00:51:18.307
- I enjoy books.
- Those are the same things.


00:51:18.408 --> 00:51:20.899
Why you been going through my trash?


00:51:23.780 --> 00:51:25.645
I'll come back to that.


00:51:26.183 --> 00:51:27.844
How did you know
he was gonna send another code?


00:51:27.951 --> 00:51:29.680
I just guessed.


00:51:29.786 --> 00:51:31.947
- Just guessed.
- The first one seemed too easy.


00:51:32.055 --> 00:51:34.387
All right, this can no longer be ignored.


00:51:34.491 --> 00:51:38.086
- What is that you're drinking?
- It's an Aqua Velva.


00:51:38.195 --> 00:51:41.096
You wouldn't make fun of it
if you tried it.


00:51:50.607 --> 00:51:53.007
But who actually cracked the code?


00:51:53.810 --> 00:51:56.040
A married couple who like puzzles.


00:51:56.146 --> 00:51:58.307
So what's that tell us about the Zodiac?


00:51:58.415 --> 00:51:59.712
- He's no expert.
- Right.


00:51:59.816 --> 00:52:01.477
It's just a simple substitution code


00:52:01.585 --> 00:52:03.780
like the one that
we used to do as boy scouts.


00:52:03.887 --> 00:52:05.514
"A" is one, "B" is two.


00:52:05.622 --> 00:52:06.953
We weren't all boy scouts, Robert.


00:52:07.057 --> 00:52:10.584
Well, it's not that hard.
You just got to know where to start.


00:52:10.694 --> 00:52:12.457
In the first cipher...


00:52:12.562 --> 00:52:13.790
You actually carry that around with you?


00:52:13.897 --> 00:52:15.592
- Why?
- No reason.


00:52:16.733 --> 00:52:20.169
What's the most common double
consonant in the English language?


00:52:20.270 --> 00:52:21.362
Consonant?


00:52:21.471 --> 00:52:22.768
- The double "L."
- Double "L."


00:52:22.873 --> 00:52:26.707
And what's the one word that we know
that he'll use in here, at least once?


00:52:26.810 --> 00:52:27.868
- "Kill."
- Right, "kill."


00:52:27.978 --> 00:52:29.445
So the Hardens start looking
for double symbols,


00:52:29.546 --> 00:52:31.514
which they find here, here, and here.


00:52:31.615 --> 00:52:34.049
Each with the same
two symbols preceding them.


00:52:34.151 --> 00:52:36.085
So now they've got
a repeating four-letter word


00:52:36.186 --> 00:52:38.211
ending with two symbols
that they assume stand for "L."


00:52:38.321 --> 00:52:39.754
And since they think the whole word
is "kill" then...


00:52:39.856 --> 00:52:43.223
Then you got your "K," you got your "I,"
and you're on your way.


00:52:43.326 --> 00:52:45.191
But how do you go
from "A" is one and "B" is two


00:52:45.295 --> 00:52:46.660
to figuring out this whole code?


00:52:46.763 --> 00:52:49.630
Well, same way I did.
You go to the library.


00:52:52.969 --> 00:52:54.869
In this book,


00:52:54.971 --> 00:52:59.067
the author presents a very simple
substitution code in the preface.


00:52:59.176 --> 00:53:02.111
Eight of the 26 symbols that
he suggests are found in this cipher.


00:53:02.212 --> 00:53:03.474
Yeah, but there are non-letter symbols


00:53:03.580 --> 00:53:04.979
because there's all
these medieval ones.


00:53:05.081 --> 00:53:07.606
I thought they looked medieval, too.


00:53:08.518 --> 00:53:10.315
But then I found a code
written in the Middle Ages.


00:53:10.420 --> 00:53:11.444
Guess what it's called?


00:53:12.255 --> 00:53:14.018
The Zodiac Alphabet.


00:53:15.992 --> 00:53:17.186
Jesus.


00:53:18.361 --> 00:53:19.794
What do you want out of this?


00:53:19.896 --> 00:53:21.386
- What?
- What's your angle?


00:53:21.498 --> 00:53:24.331
This is good business
for everyone but you.


00:53:27.504 --> 00:53:29.267
How do you mean "business"?


00:53:32.342 --> 00:53:34.674
Hey. Come to bed.


00:53:34.778 --> 00:53:38.043
I'll be up in a minute.
I need to make a phone call.


00:53:49.659 --> 00:53:51.320
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Bill?


00:53:52.195 --> 00:53:54.561
There's not many basements
in California.


00:53:54.664 --> 00:53:56.825
<i>"Basement for future use."</i>


00:53:56.933 --> 00:53:58.423
That's right.


00:53:58.535 --> 00:54:02.164
<i>I'll have Vallejo and Napa</i>
<i>check with their city planners.</i>


00:54:02.272 --> 00:54:04.467
- <i>Get some sleep.</i>
- Yeah, sure.


00:54:17.420 --> 00:54:20.253
<i>"Dear Melvin,</i>
<i>this is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


00:54:20.357 --> 00:54:22.518
<i>"I wish you a happy Christmas.</i>


00:54:22.626 --> 00:54:26.062
<i>"The one thing I ask of you is this.</i>
<i>Please help me.</i>


00:54:26.162 --> 00:54:29.563
"I cannot reach out for help
because this thing in me won't let me."


00:54:29.666 --> 00:54:30.997
Thank you.


00:54:31.101 --> 00:54:34.298
"I am finding it extremely difficult
to hold it in check


00:54:34.404 --> 00:54:37.032
"and I am afraid I will lose control again


00:54:37.140 --> 00:54:39.938
"and take my ninth
and possibly tenth victim."


00:54:40.043 --> 00:54:42.341
Melvin, he's reaching out to you.


00:54:42.445 --> 00:54:43.776
Absolutely.


00:54:43.880 --> 00:54:47.407
Inspectors, he sent this letter
directly to my residence.


00:54:47.517 --> 00:54:50.543
It is a cry for help,
intended as a private communiqué.


00:54:50.654 --> 00:54:52.781
Which is why
you contacted the <i>Chronicle.</i>


00:54:52.889 --> 00:54:55.881
The people have a right to know.
Toddy?


00:54:55.992 --> 00:54:59.052
- When did the letter arrive?
- In the middle of last week.


00:54:59.162 --> 00:55:01.562
I was away on safari.


00:55:01.665 --> 00:55:03.428
What did you gentlemen
do for Christmas?


00:55:03.533 --> 00:55:05.831
- You're looking at it.
- You must see Africa.


00:55:05.935 --> 00:55:11.134
Cradle of civilization.
Fascinating people. Beautiful. Savage.


00:55:11.241 --> 00:55:15.007
- Back to the killer who wrote to you.
- Yes. Of course.


00:55:15.111 --> 00:55:17.011
It is my belief
that he only penned this letter


00:55:17.113 --> 00:55:20.139
because he couldn't get through to me
on the Dunbar show or here.


00:55:20.250 --> 00:55:22.775
- He tried to contact you here?
- Several times.


00:55:22.886 --> 00:55:25.013
I was out,
but he spoke with my housekeeper.


00:55:25.121 --> 00:55:26.179
Didn't leave a number.


00:55:26.289 --> 00:55:28.814
He's kind of crafty like that.
Do you mind if I speak to her?


00:55:28.925 --> 00:55:32.019
Not at all. But the real story is the letter.


00:55:32.128 --> 00:55:34.187
- I'll be back.
- Yeah.


00:55:34.297 --> 00:55:35.423
She's right this way.


00:55:35.532 --> 00:55:40.868
Inspector Toschi, it is my belief
this is a window into this man's soul.


00:55:40.970 --> 00:55:42.665
Killing is his compulsion.


00:55:42.772 --> 00:55:45.366
Even though he tries to ignore it,
it drives him.


00:55:45.475 --> 00:55:46.499
It's in his blood.


00:55:46.609 --> 00:55:49.669
Could be.
Or maybe he just likes the attention.


00:56:33.523 --> 00:56:38.790
I didn't mean to scare you,
but your right rear wheel is loose.


00:56:38.895 --> 00:56:39.919
Really?


00:56:40.029 --> 00:56:43.521
If you like,
I could tighten the lugs up for you.


00:56:46.136 --> 00:56:47.262
If you don't mind.


00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:49.838
Well, you can't be too careful.


00:57:24.274 --> 00:57:26.674
- All done.
- Thank you.


00:57:26.776 --> 00:57:29.006
No problem. Have a good night.


00:57:33.983 --> 00:57:35.280
It's okay.


00:58:29.639 --> 00:58:31.266
Are you okay?


00:58:32.775 --> 00:58:35.437
Yeah. Yeah, we're fine.


00:58:36.279 --> 00:58:38.713
Must have been worse than I thought.


00:58:38.815 --> 00:58:41.682
I can give you a lift to a service station.


00:58:43.920 --> 00:58:45.012
Okay.


00:58:51.361 --> 00:58:53.386
It's okay. Come on.


00:59:01.104 --> 00:59:03.265
I didn't know you had a baby.


00:59:04.974 --> 00:59:06.635
Oh, is that okay?


00:59:08.211 --> 00:59:10.008
The more the merrier.


00:59:19.556 --> 00:59:22.184
You shouldn't smoke. It's a bad habit.


00:59:28.665 --> 00:59:32.294
- I think we just passed a filling station.
- It was closed.


00:59:37.774 --> 00:59:40.834
Do you always go around
helping people in the night?


00:59:40.944 --> 00:59:44.209
When I'm done with them,
they don't need much help.


00:59:47.083 --> 00:59:48.846
It's okay.


00:59:48.952 --> 00:59:50.943
Before I kill you,


00:59:51.054 --> 00:59:53.887
I'm gonna throw your baby
out the window.


01:00:07.403 --> 01:00:10.566
No! Help! Please! No!


01:00:17.513 --> 01:00:20.414
She was on the side of the road.
She flagged me down.


01:00:20.516 --> 01:00:22.143
- What happened to her?
- She said she jumped from a car.


01:00:22.251 --> 01:00:24.082
I found her like this.


01:00:24.187 --> 01:00:27.088
- What is it?
- Please, he said...


01:00:27.190 --> 01:00:30.023
- It'll be okay.
- Tried to kill me.


01:00:30.126 --> 01:00:31.616
My baby!


01:00:31.728 --> 01:00:35.129
- Where's her baby?
- She didn't have one when I stopped.


01:00:35.231 --> 01:00:36.858
Where's your baby?


01:00:43.373 --> 01:00:44.567
Jesus.


01:00:52.281 --> 01:00:54.715
- You hid it?
- In case he came back.


01:01:09.632 --> 01:01:10.894
<i>"This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


01:01:11.567 --> 01:01:14.866
<i>"By the way, have you cracked</i>
<i>the last cipher I sent you?</i>


01:01:14.971 --> 01:01:18.702
<i>"I'm mildly curious as to how much</i>
<i>money you have on my head now.</i>


01:01:18.808 --> 01:01:22.574
<i>"I hope you do not think I was the one</i>
<i>who wiped out that blue meanie</i>


01:01:22.679 --> 01:01:24.670
<i>"with a bomb at the cop station,</i>


01:01:24.781 --> 01:01:27.249
<i>"even though I talked about</i>
<i>killing children with one."</i>


01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:28.783
<i>"This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


01:01:28.885 --> 01:01:32.150
<i>"I'd like to see some nice Zodiac</i>
<i>buttons wandering around town.</i>


01:01:32.955 --> 01:01:34.445
<i>"Everyone else has these buttons</i>


01:01:34.557 --> 01:01:38.015
<i>"like peace, black power,</i>
<i>and Melvin eats blubber, et cetera.</i>


01:01:38.261 --> 01:01:39.592
<i>"It would cheer me up considerably</i>


01:01:39.696 --> 01:01:42.062
<i>"if I saw a lot of people</i>
<i>wearing my button.</i>


01:01:42.165 --> 01:01:44.861
- <i>"Please no nasty ones."</i>
- <i>"This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


01:01:44.967 --> 01:01:47.868
<i>"I shot a man</i>
<i>sitting in a parked car with a.38.</i>


01:01:47.970 --> 01:01:51.235
<i>"Zodiac 12, SFPD zero."</i>


01:01:51.340 --> 01:01:54.707
<i>"The map coupled with this code</i>
<i>will tell you where the bomb is set.</i>


01:01:54.811 --> 01:01:57.507
<i>"You have until next fall to dig it up."</i>


01:02:00.016 --> 01:02:01.483
<i>"This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


01:02:01.584 --> 01:02:03.347
<i>"I'm rather unhappy because you people</i>


01:02:03.453 --> 01:02:05.250
<i>"will not wear</i>
<i>some nice Zodiac buttons.</i>


01:02:05.354 --> 01:02:07.788
"So, I now have a little list,
starting with the woman and her baby


01:02:07.890 --> 01:02:09.289
"that I gave a rather interesting ride


01:02:09.392 --> 01:02:11.622
"for a couple of hours one evening,
a few months back,


01:02:11.728 --> 01:02:13.958
"that ended in my burning her car
where I found them."


01:02:14.063 --> 01:02:16.258
We're really not gonna run
any more of his letters?


01:02:16.365 --> 01:02:18.925
The new policy. Our brothers in blue
want us to hold back


01:02:19.035 --> 01:02:20.593
and see how he reacts.


01:02:20.703 --> 01:02:22.796
Four letters in three months,


01:02:22.905 --> 01:02:25.897
and this is the first mention
of Kathleen Johns. That's very weird.


01:02:26.008 --> 01:02:29.307
That's because he's full of shit.


01:02:30.613 --> 01:02:32.240
What do you mean?


01:02:33.516 --> 01:02:34.676
You don't know?


01:02:36.385 --> 01:02:41.152
Welcome. Please put your stuff down.
You're going down five rows and left.


01:02:41.257 --> 01:02:43.851
Looking for the <i>Modesto Bee</i>
from March.


01:02:43.960 --> 01:02:46.986
I'm going to stand here
and attempt not to vomit.


01:02:47.096 --> 01:02:49.064
- Left.
- Left.


01:02:50.099 --> 01:02:52.590
- What am I looking for?
- Kathleen Johns.


01:02:52.702 --> 01:02:53.896
Also probably you wanna
pull the <i>Chron</i> from...


01:02:54.003 --> 01:02:57.131
You know, never mind. I'll see to that.


01:02:58.307 --> 01:03:00.673
Okay, look at this letter again.
The part about Kathleen Johns.


01:03:00.777 --> 01:03:02.642
Tell me what facts he gives.


01:03:02.745 --> 01:03:05.908
- A woman and her baby abducted.
- Fact.


01:03:08.117 --> 01:03:10.278
- The car on fire.
- Okay, now,


01:03:11.754 --> 01:03:14.154
look at the article from the <i>Bee.</i>


01:03:14.857 --> 01:03:16.415
Seen it yet?


01:03:16.526 --> 01:03:18.426
Everything in the letter
already appeared in the article.


01:03:18.528 --> 01:03:20.462
And he's done it before.


01:03:21.664 --> 01:03:24.292
Officer Richard Radetich,
shot sitting in his car.


01:03:24.400 --> 01:03:26.561
Zodiac claimed that he shot someone
in their car.


01:03:26.669 --> 01:03:30.161
Couple days after this article came out.


01:03:30.273 --> 01:03:31.934
The police already had somebody
in custody.


01:03:32.041 --> 01:03:34.601
Zodiac didn't do it,
but took credit for it anyway


01:03:34.710 --> 01:03:37.008
because he's in it for the press.


01:03:37.113 --> 01:03:38.478
He even stole his symbol.


01:03:38.581 --> 01:03:40.845
- What?
- Yeah. Shit.


01:03:40.950 --> 01:03:42.611
If I show you something,
you promise not to tell anyone?


01:03:42.718 --> 01:03:45.983
- Who would I tell?
- Okay. Totally solid point. Okay.


01:03:53.830 --> 01:03:55.525
That's the only place
that word and that symbol


01:03:55.631 --> 01:03:58.065
ever appeared together
before the letters.


01:03:58.167 --> 01:03:59.691
The guy stole his logo off a watch.


01:03:59.802 --> 01:04:01.099
How can somebody
who's killed 13 people do...


01:04:01.204 --> 01:04:02.432
He claims he's killed 13 people,


01:04:02.538 --> 01:04:04.028
but which ones
can we actually confirm?


01:04:04.140 --> 01:04:08.167
There's three in Vallejo,
one in Berryessa, the cabbie. That's it.


01:04:09.812 --> 01:04:12.303
Bobby, you almost look disappointed.


01:04:13.216 --> 01:04:15.684
Chief's pulling everybody off buses.


01:04:16.319 --> 01:04:17.877
Business as usual.


01:04:17.987 --> 01:04:19.648
Something'll shake loose.


01:04:19.755 --> 01:04:21.950
Not a peep in four months.


01:04:22.058 --> 01:04:24.492
First he won't shut up and now...


01:04:24.594 --> 01:04:26.858
Maybe we drove him underground.


01:04:27.530 --> 01:04:29.122
Maybe he's gone.


01:04:30.199 --> 01:04:33.225
<i>311 at 582 Haight, cross at Biltmore.</i>
<i>There's a male...</i>


01:04:33.336 --> 01:04:35.531
- Happy birthday, Bill.
- Thanks.


01:04:45.781 --> 01:04:48.045
Does it ever bother you
that people call you Shorty?


01:04:48.150 --> 01:04:50.641
Does it bother you
that people call you a retard?


01:04:50.753 --> 01:04:53.551
- Nobody calls me that.
- Right.


01:04:53.656 --> 01:04:57.217
<i>As governor,</i>
<i>I pledge to use all my influence</i>


01:04:57.326 --> 01:05:01.956
<i>to make sure that Darlene Ferrin's killer</i>
<i>is brought to justice.</i>


01:05:02.064 --> 01:05:06.626
<i>I believe some clues were overlooked</i>
<i>in the murder of Darlene Ferrin.</i>


01:05:06.736 --> 01:05:08.567
- <i>I believe her murder was premeditated.</i>
- Who is that?


01:05:08.671 --> 01:05:11.663
Florence Douglas, mayor of Vallejo.
She's running for governor.


01:05:11.774 --> 01:05:14.607
<i>I believe that the police department</i>
<i>either did not have the money, the time</i>


01:05:14.710 --> 01:05:16.735
<i>or, yes, the inclination...</i>


01:05:16.846 --> 01:05:20.213
<i>Sayonara,</i> police endorsement.
Good work, Flo.


01:05:20.316 --> 01:05:22.910
Does anyone ever call me names, or...


01:05:24.020 --> 01:05:25.885
You mean like retard?


01:05:25.988 --> 01:05:27.216
Yeah.


01:05:28.190 --> 01:05:29.248
No.


01:05:33.562 --> 01:05:37.589
Shit. Fuck. Oh, my God. Jesus.


01:05:41.837 --> 01:05:43.702
Tell me that's not a piece
of bloody shirt!


01:05:43.806 --> 01:05:45.296
Fuck! Holy fucking crap!


01:05:45.408 --> 01:05:47.774
"I feel it in my bones,
you ache to know my name


01:05:48.010 --> 01:05:50.342
"and so I'll clue you in.


01:05:50.446 --> 01:05:53.540
"But then, why spoil the game?
Happy Halloween."


01:05:55.051 --> 01:05:58.817
Paul, you did call him
a latent homosexual


01:05:58.921 --> 01:06:00.218
in at least one of your articles.


01:06:00.323 --> 01:06:02.814
Dave. I want a gun.


01:06:05.528 --> 01:06:06.825
A gun?


01:06:11.434 --> 01:06:13.026
You're in Herb Caen.


01:06:13.135 --> 01:06:15.626
"Paul Avery's investigation
has won him the accolade


01:06:15.738 --> 01:06:18.730
"of a message from the Zodiac warning,
'You are doomed.'


01:06:18.841 --> 01:06:22.140
"As a result, several crime newsmen
are wearing lapel buttons reading,


01:06:22.244 --> 01:06:24.337
"'I am not Paul Avery."'


01:06:24.447 --> 01:06:26.574
You should sell these.
You could do well.


01:06:26.682 --> 01:06:29.310
It's been a windfall, since
they published the threat on my life.


01:06:29.418 --> 01:06:31.079
I got the leads
coming out of the woodwork.


01:06:31.187 --> 01:06:34.122
There's one guy down in Riverside.


01:06:34.223 --> 01:06:35.349
I'm gonna drive down
and see him tonight.


01:06:35.458 --> 01:06:39.155
- You wanna tag along?
- No, I have a date.


01:06:39.829 --> 01:06:42.127
- Really?
- Who is this guy?


01:06:42.231 --> 01:06:45.792
He wishes to remain anonymous.
I wish to remain infamous.


01:06:45.901 --> 01:06:50.201
So we're going to get along great.


01:06:56.979 --> 01:06:59.607
Hi. Good evening. Hi.
I'm looking for a Melanie.


01:06:59.715 --> 01:07:01.580
Yes.
It's the young lady sitting by herself.


01:07:01.684 --> 01:07:03.015
Thank you.


01:07:09.392 --> 01:07:10.689
You must be Melanie.


01:07:10.793 --> 01:07:12.693
- Which would make you Robert.
- It would.


01:07:12.795 --> 01:07:15.992
Glynnis told me lots about you.


01:07:16.098 --> 01:07:17.793
- And you have wine, great.
- I do.


01:07:17.900 --> 01:07:19.800
Great. How late am I?


01:07:21.704 --> 01:07:24.229
Just a few minutes, really.
I just got here myself.


01:07:24.340 --> 01:07:27.400
Traffic's bumper to bumper.
I was at the gun range.


01:07:27.510 --> 01:07:30.570
- Glynnis said you were a cartoonist.
- Oh, yeah.


01:07:30.679 --> 01:07:32.510
Well, what're you doing at a gun range?


01:07:32.615 --> 01:07:34.173
Reading.


01:07:34.283 --> 01:07:37.184
Get some more...
You need some more napkins.


01:07:38.487 --> 01:07:40.682
So, you work with Glynnis.


01:07:40.790 --> 01:07:42.724
- For her, actually.
- For her?


01:07:42.825 --> 01:07:44.452
Oh, well...


01:07:46.328 --> 01:07:48.387
My children are terrified of Glynnis.


01:07:48.497 --> 01:07:49.759
Me, too.


01:07:53.169 --> 01:07:54.295
So, the gun range?


01:07:54.403 --> 01:07:57.372
We're... I'm working on...
Do you know the Zodiac?


01:07:57.473 --> 01:07:58.770
- Yeah.
- I'm working with...


01:07:58.874 --> 01:08:01.342
- Do you know who Paul Avery is?
- Sounds kind of familiar.


01:08:01.444 --> 01:08:03.173
He's the writer
that the Zodiac threatened.


01:08:03.279 --> 01:08:04.473
Oh, yeah, I saw that on TV.


01:08:04.580 --> 01:08:07.708
Well, I work near him
and he's going down tonight


01:08:07.817 --> 01:08:10.980
to track an anonymous tipster
down in Riverside.


01:08:12.154 --> 01:08:14.213
Where is Riverside?


01:08:14.323 --> 01:08:15.790
It's near L.A.


01:08:15.891 --> 01:08:19.486
Oh, wow. I don't think Paul knows
that it's that far away.


01:08:21.697 --> 01:08:23.688
Sounds kind of dangerous.


01:08:24.967 --> 01:08:27.868
Yeah. How do you mean?


01:08:27.970 --> 01:08:30.370
Well, you said it was
an anonymous tip, right?


01:08:30.473 --> 01:08:31.906
Yeah.


01:08:32.007 --> 01:08:35.534
So it could be an ambush.
I mean, it could be the Zodiac.


01:08:37.079 --> 01:08:39.479
Don't you think it's kind of stupid?


01:08:39.582 --> 01:08:42.210
Yeah, yeah. Well, Paul has a gun.


01:08:46.055 --> 01:08:48.523
So, do you know what's good here?


01:08:50.359 --> 01:08:52.486
I've never been here before.


01:08:54.630 --> 01:08:56.598
The pasta, spaghetti?


01:08:58.334 --> 01:09:00.393
Are you ready to order yet?


01:09:01.470 --> 01:09:04.268
Yeah, I'll have the penne vodka.
But could you do it in a cream sauce?


01:09:04.373 --> 01:09:05.670
Of course.


01:09:10.646 --> 01:09:12.841
Maybe give us another minute?


01:09:14.717 --> 01:09:16.651
Do you have any change?


01:09:16.752 --> 01:09:18.913
Oh, wait, no wait, hold on.


01:09:19.021 --> 01:09:20.545
Nope. That's a penny.


01:09:20.656 --> 01:09:22.055
Do you have to make a phone call?


01:09:22.158 --> 01:09:25.616
Yeah, you know,
when you were saying that the Zodiac...


01:09:26.228 --> 01:09:27.889
You know, when you said it
was dangerous, I just thought


01:09:27.997 --> 01:09:30.022
- that it is dangerous, and it's...
- Stupid?


01:09:30.132 --> 01:09:31.724
Stupid. And I just thought that


01:09:31.834 --> 01:09:35.565
I should call his wife
and just see if she's heard from him.


01:09:37.907 --> 01:09:39.340
I have some change.


01:09:58.561 --> 01:10:01.826
Okay. Well, she said
she'd call when she heard from him.


01:10:01.931 --> 01:10:03.364
- Good.
- Yeah.


01:10:04.767 --> 01:10:08.203
Melanie, I should really go home
and wait for the call.


01:10:11.340 --> 01:10:14.798
Is this some sleazy plan
to get me to go home with you?


01:10:15.511 --> 01:10:16.978
What? No.


01:10:19.481 --> 01:10:21.449
I'll get the food to go.


01:10:23.152 --> 01:10:24.278
Hello!


01:10:40.502 --> 01:10:43.335
Hi! I'm supposed
to meet somebody here.


01:11:01.590 --> 01:11:02.989
Anything?


01:11:06.629 --> 01:11:07.891
You don't have to stay.


01:11:07.997 --> 01:11:09.430
Are you kidding?


01:11:09.531 --> 01:11:12.625
This is the most interesting date
I've ever had.


01:11:16.905 --> 01:11:17.997
- <i>Paul?</i>
- Robert?


01:11:18.107 --> 01:11:18.474
- Yes.
- You sitting down?


01:11:18.474 --> 01:11:19.668
- Yes.
- You sitting down?


01:11:19.775 --> 01:11:20.867
<i>Yes.</i>


01:11:20.976 --> 01:11:22.773
You're not gonna believe this.


01:11:22.878 --> 01:11:23.867
Dave!


01:11:23.979 --> 01:11:26.573
<i>In a bizarre twist,</i>
<i>the hunted has become hunter.</i>


01:11:26.682 --> 01:11:30.448
San Francisco Chronicle <i>reporter</i>
<i>and Zodiac target Paul Avery</i>


01:11:30.552 --> 01:11:32.611
<i>claims to have uncovered</i>
<i>new information</i>


01:11:32.721 --> 01:11:37.181
<i>regarding the only unsolved homicide</i>
<i>in Riverside County's history,</i>


01:11:37.293 --> 01:11:40.456
<i>a 1966 Southern California murder,</i>


01:11:40.562 --> 01:11:43.531
<i>that Avery now believes</i>
<i>was the Zodiac's first victim.</i>


01:11:43.632 --> 01:11:44.621
What?


01:11:44.733 --> 01:11:45.893
- He didn't call you about this?
- Hang on!


01:11:46.001 --> 01:11:47.491
<i>The Riverside killer</i>
<i>wrote to the press letters</i>


01:11:47.603 --> 01:11:51.437
<i>that I then took personally to</i>
<i>the Office of Questioned Documents.</i>


01:11:51.540 --> 01:11:53.701
<i>And what did this expert tell you?</i>


01:11:53.809 --> 01:11:55.333
<i>What I knew in my gut, Ron.</i>


01:11:55.444 --> 01:11:57.878
<i>The handwriting matches Zodiac's.</i>


01:11:57.980 --> 01:12:00.312
How'd he get the evidence
out of Riverside?


01:12:00.416 --> 01:12:02.611
He took it to Sherwood
without telling us, the son of a bitch.


01:12:02.718 --> 01:12:03.912
You know how bad this looks?


01:12:04.019 --> 01:12:06.214
Hey, how do we know
that this lead is real?


01:12:06.322 --> 01:12:08.586
It's very real. You know how I know?


01:12:08.691 --> 01:12:10.556
Because I saw it on TV.


01:12:16.598 --> 01:12:17.565
Excuse me.


01:12:17.666 --> 01:12:18.792
Dave.


01:12:19.201 --> 01:12:20.293
Hi.


01:12:20.402 --> 01:12:22.529
Dave, you know Mel Nicolai.
He's working the case for Justice.


01:12:22.638 --> 01:12:23.798
Good to see you, Mel.


01:12:23.906 --> 01:12:25.771
All due respect,
can someone explain to me


01:12:25.874 --> 01:12:27.501
why I'm reading
about breaks in this case


01:12:27.609 --> 01:12:29.440
in the <i>Chronicle</i> instead
of getting calls from you?


01:12:29.545 --> 01:12:30.603
We got screwed.


01:12:30.713 --> 01:12:31.873
Dave, come on.


01:12:31.980 --> 01:12:33.948
You do get your name in the paper a lot.
People talk.


01:12:34.049 --> 01:12:36.916
I don't ever talk about an open
investigation, period. Okay, Ken?


01:12:37.019 --> 01:12:39.783
Dave? Hey. Hi.


01:12:39.888 --> 01:12:42.448
Paul Avery. Can I catch a ride
with you gents when we get there?


01:12:42.558 --> 01:12:44.389
Not a good idea, Paul.


01:12:45.260 --> 01:12:48.161
He's gonna make me take a cab
when we're going to the same place.


01:12:48.263 --> 01:12:50.823
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>
<i>thank you for choosing PSA.</i>


01:12:50.933 --> 01:12:53.026
- Fair enough. Fair enough.
- <i>Please take your seats at this time.</i>


01:12:53.135 --> 01:12:56.263
<i>Remember, smoking is</i>
<i>in the last six aisles only.</i>


01:12:56.372 --> 01:12:57.999
<i>Enjoy your flight.</i>


01:13:01.877 --> 01:13:03.936
- Cross? Hi.
- Yeah.


01:13:04.046 --> 01:13:06.310
- Detective David Toschi, SFPD.
- How are you doing?


01:13:06.415 --> 01:13:07.905
Great. Thanks for having us
down today.


01:13:08.016 --> 01:13:10.507
Not at all.
I hear you have some files for us.


01:13:10.619 --> 01:13:12.109
I'll show you mine. You show me yours.


01:13:12.221 --> 01:13:14.587
- Frisco huh?
- That's right. San Francisco.


01:13:15.224 --> 01:13:16.691
- Ken Narlow from Napa.
- Ken.


01:13:16.792 --> 01:13:18.487
- Mel Nicolai, Justice.
- Mel.


01:13:18.594 --> 01:13:19.561
Here's what we know.


01:13:19.661 --> 01:13:22.221
Cheri Jo Bates attended
Riverside Community College.


01:13:22.331 --> 01:13:26.597
She studies in the library
the night of October 30th, 1966.


01:13:26.702 --> 01:13:30.502
She leaves with an unidentified male
at closing, 9:00 p.m.


01:13:30.606 --> 01:13:34.303
Her body's found the next morning
in a parking lot, stabbed to death.


01:13:34.410 --> 01:13:35.707
Her car is disabled.


01:13:35.811 --> 01:13:38.780
Someone cut the coil in the distributor,
the battery died.


01:13:38.881 --> 01:13:41.281
The someone comes back,
offers to help.


01:13:41.383 --> 01:13:43.510
- Like Kathleen Johns.
- Who?


01:13:43.619 --> 01:13:46.281
A woman outside of Modesto,
might be a Zodiac victim.


01:13:46.388 --> 01:13:49.880
Might. Might be.
I have her comp right here in this file.


01:13:49.992 --> 01:13:51.186
Okay.


01:13:51.293 --> 01:13:54.387
A typewritten confession was sent
to the <i>Riverside Press Enterprise</i>


01:13:54.496 --> 01:13:57.260
on November 29th,
a month after Bates's murder.


01:13:57.366 --> 01:13:58.765
They ran it.


01:14:01.036 --> 01:14:03.732
"I'm not sick. I am insane.
But that will not stop the game.


01:14:03.839 --> 01:14:06.000
"This letter should be published
for all to read."


01:14:06.108 --> 01:14:07.473
He wants to be published.
He calls it a game.


01:14:07.576 --> 01:14:08.941
I mean, this could be our boy.


01:14:09.044 --> 01:14:12.343
Six months later, the police,
the girl's father, and the paper,


01:14:12.448 --> 01:14:14.382
they all received these.


01:14:19.221 --> 01:14:21.018
Double postage, just like Zodiac.


01:14:22.624 --> 01:14:25.491
These are what Sherwood Morrill
matched to the Zodiac letters?


01:14:25.594 --> 01:14:27.619
These and the desktop. Don.


01:14:27.729 --> 01:14:32.029
This was found a couple of months later
by a janitor in RCC storage.


01:14:41.009 --> 01:14:43.603
Sherwood got
a handwriting match off wood?


01:14:45.547 --> 01:14:47.811
Who etches in their own handwriting?


01:14:47.916 --> 01:14:49.042
To be honest with you,


01:14:49.151 --> 01:14:51.517
our letters and your letters,
I don't see it.


01:14:51.620 --> 01:14:54.180
How did Paul Avery
get his hands on the exemplars?


01:14:54.289 --> 01:14:55.620
I gave them to him.


01:14:55.724 --> 01:14:57.589
We talked on the phone the other day
for about an hour.


01:14:57.693 --> 01:14:59.160
And I told him you were gonna be here.


01:14:59.261 --> 01:15:00.922
- You told him we were meeting?
- Yeah.


01:15:01.029 --> 01:15:03.224
I also told him
we don't think this is Zodiac.


01:15:03.332 --> 01:15:05.391
Okay, wait a minute.


01:15:05.501 --> 01:15:08.561
- You don't think this is Zodiac?
- We got a guy we like for it.


01:15:08.670 --> 01:15:10.228
We don't have enough
to pin it on him yet,


01:15:10.339 --> 01:15:11.567
but we're pretty sure it's him.


01:15:11.673 --> 01:15:14.540
If you don't think this is Zodiac,
then why give anything to Avery?


01:15:14.643 --> 01:15:16.270
I'm trying to cooperate.


01:15:16.378 --> 01:15:19.176
Oh, that's how you cooperate?
By giving information to reporters?


01:15:19.341 --> 01:15:20.865
Look, I don't know
about the handwriting,


01:15:20.976 --> 01:15:22.204
but Sherwood says it's a match, right?


01:15:22.311 --> 01:15:24.711
So, let's just say
that your guy did Cheri Jo.


01:15:24.813 --> 01:15:25.939
He types the confession.


01:15:26.048 --> 01:15:29.176
Zodiac reads it in the paper,
and he writes a letter taking credit for it.


01:15:29.284 --> 01:15:30.808
Now, that's something he's done before.


01:15:30.919 --> 01:15:33.513
Look, now you have everything we have.


01:15:33.622 --> 01:15:36.921
But, in my opinion,
you guys came south for nothing.


01:15:37.025 --> 01:15:39.118
FUBAR, gentlemen, FUBAR.


01:15:39.227 --> 01:15:41.957
I don't care what he says.
This still could be Z.


01:15:42.064 --> 01:15:45.261
The problem is
the entire state already thinks it is.


01:15:45.367 --> 01:15:48.700
Well, there's your press agent.
Talk to him about it.


01:15:51.239 --> 01:15:53.173
I come in peace.
I don't want any trouble.


01:15:53.275 --> 01:15:55.243
I really don't want to talk to you
right now, Paul. Not now.


01:15:55.344 --> 01:15:59.280
- Just trying to do my job.
- Oh, really? Well, now I can't do mine.


01:15:59.381 --> 01:16:01.406
We're already screwed with
the amount of tips we got on this thing,


01:16:01.516 --> 01:16:03.211
and you just freaked out the entire state.


01:16:03.318 --> 01:16:06.617
I have got Napa, Vallejo, and DOJ
looking at me sideways


01:16:06.722 --> 01:16:09.520
and Riverside's telling me
I'm on a snipe hunt!


01:16:09.625 --> 01:16:12.253
Jesus. Hey, Cheri Jo Bates was a gift.
I gave that to you.


01:16:12.361 --> 01:16:13.919
You and Armstrong
never would have found her.


01:16:14.029 --> 01:16:16.293
This may not be Zodiac.
Does that matter to you?


01:16:16.398 --> 01:16:17.729
- What if it is?
- Does it matter that Riverside may not


01:16:17.833 --> 01:16:19.892
be able to make a case
against their suspect because of you?


01:16:20.002 --> 01:16:21.902
Tell it to Sherwood.
I'm out here, beating the bushes,


01:16:22.004 --> 01:16:23.562
trying to draw him out.
We're in this together.


01:16:23.672 --> 01:16:25.037
No, we're not in anything together, Paul,


01:16:25.140 --> 01:16:27.005
because I'm not interested
in upping my circulation.


01:16:27.109 --> 01:16:29.976
Oh, boy. He wrote me.
He threatened my life.


01:16:30.078 --> 01:16:31.670
Hey, Bullitt!


01:16:31.780 --> 01:16:35.739
Been a year-and-a-half,
you gonna catch this fucking guy or not?


01:16:37.886 --> 01:16:40.252
- Go fuck yourself.
- Happily.


01:16:40.355 --> 01:16:42.346
You should have called me, Paul.


01:16:47.929 --> 01:16:49.123
Thank you.


01:17:02.411 --> 01:17:04.140
- Did you see this?
- Unfortunately, yes.


01:17:04.246 --> 01:17:06.908
Here comes every lunatic in California.


01:17:07.783 --> 01:17:09.080
I'm the Zodiac.


01:17:09.184 --> 01:17:10.742
And how did you kill your victims?


01:17:10.852 --> 01:17:13.480
With a gun. No, with a hammer.


01:17:13.588 --> 01:17:14.885
All I'm authorized to tell you


01:17:14.990 --> 01:17:16.548
is that he's still under
government employment.


01:17:16.658 --> 01:17:19.718
- And who authorized you to tell me this?
- That's all I'm authorized to say.


01:17:19.828 --> 01:17:21.955
<i>Only a little rat bastard like Andre</i>


01:17:22.064 --> 01:17:24.624
could have done something
like cut off all the victims' hands.


01:17:24.733 --> 01:17:27.099
Zodiac didn't cut off
any of the victims' hands.


01:17:27.202 --> 01:17:28.931
- Are you sure?
- Yes, sir.


01:17:29.037 --> 01:17:31.562
Travis and I worked here
side by side for 10 years.


01:17:31.673 --> 01:17:35.734
His foot gets crushed in an accident
and the killings begin.


01:17:35.844 --> 01:17:37.334
- Coincidence?
- I don't know.


01:17:37.446 --> 01:17:39.311
You're a cop, man. Do the math.


01:17:43.719 --> 01:17:46.950
Have you considered
the killer might be Paul Avery?


01:17:47.055 --> 01:17:48.215
Frequently.


01:17:48.824 --> 01:17:50.189
He was drinking Coors,
getting a load on.


01:17:50.759 --> 01:17:54.388
Starts talking about hunting people.
Like that book.


01:17:54.496 --> 01:17:56.657
Says how you can put a light
at the end of a gun


01:17:56.765 --> 01:17:58.289
to use as a sight in the dark.


01:17:58.400 --> 01:18:00.163
- He said that?
- Yeah.


01:18:00.268 --> 01:18:03.135
So I asked him,
"How would you get away with it?"


01:18:03.405 --> 01:18:05.134
And he said, "It would be easy


01:18:05.240 --> 01:18:07.674
"'cause there'd be no real motive
to the thing."


01:18:07.776 --> 01:18:09.641
Then he said he'd write letters
to the police


01:18:09.745 --> 01:18:11.542
and call himself Zodiac
to mess with them.


01:18:11.646 --> 01:18:13.238
Leigh liked messing with people.


01:18:13.348 --> 01:18:16.340
- You're positive he said "Zodiac"?
- Yeah.


01:18:16.451 --> 01:18:19.545
I thought it was a stupid name.
So I told him.


01:18:19.654 --> 01:18:23.090
He got up all upset and said,
"I don't care what you think.


01:18:23.191 --> 01:18:25.819
"I've thought about it a long time
and that's the name I'm gonna use."


01:18:25.927 --> 01:18:29.260
Did you feel like he'd been
thinking about it a long time?


01:18:29.364 --> 01:18:32.595
He was raw about losing his job
at the school.


01:18:32.701 --> 01:18:35.693
He talked about shooting out
the tires of a school bus


01:18:35.804 --> 01:18:38.204
and picking off the little darlings.


01:18:38.306 --> 01:18:42.367
- He actually used those words?
- That's what made me remember.


01:18:42.477 --> 01:18:44.911
Afterwards, I told my wife
I didn't wanna see him again.


01:18:45.013 --> 01:18:46.742
And I haven't since.


01:18:46.848 --> 01:18:49.339
Other thing is, Leigh's into skin diving.


01:18:49.451 --> 01:18:51.510
I know he's been up to that lake
a bunch of times.


01:18:51.620 --> 01:18:53.986
Lake Berryessa?
Did you ever go with him?


01:18:54.089 --> 01:18:58.048
Couple times. We went fishing
by Putah Creek near there.


01:18:58.160 --> 01:18:59.627
Tell him when you put it together.


01:18:59.728 --> 01:19:04.427
About a year ago, in the paper,
there was a story about the Zodiac.


01:19:04.533 --> 01:19:07.627
And it all comes back.
I tried to call the local cops.


01:19:07.736 --> 01:19:09.328
They blew him off.
Thought he was a nut.


01:19:09.437 --> 01:19:13.237
And you're sure
the conversation you had about Zodiac


01:19:13.341 --> 01:19:17.107
took place on January 1st, 1968?


01:19:17.212 --> 01:19:18.941
It couldn't have been any later.


01:19:19.047 --> 01:19:21.948
I started a new job in L.A.
On January 20th.


01:19:22.484 --> 01:19:23.951
I had to move.


01:19:24.052 --> 01:19:26.520
- <i>This is my problem. This guy...</i>
- <i>Arthur Leigh Allen?</i>


01:19:26.621 --> 01:19:29.215
This guy, Leigh,
just lays out his entire evil plan


01:19:29.324 --> 01:19:30.814
to a fishing buddy on New Year's Day?


01:19:30.926 --> 01:19:33.724
I don't know.
He's angry, he's been drinking,


01:19:33.829 --> 01:19:35.956
been thinking about it for a while.
I can buy that.


01:19:36.064 --> 01:19:38.396
So why didn't Cheney
contact us sooner?


01:19:38.500 --> 01:19:39.933
I checked. He did.


01:19:40.035 --> 01:19:43.027
First recorded contact
with the police department about Allen


01:19:43.138 --> 01:19:45.936
was in Pomona. January 10th, 1970.


01:19:46.041 --> 01:19:47.133
He just got lost in the shuffle.


01:19:47.242 --> 01:19:48.903
Did Cheney have anything
against Allen?


01:19:49.010 --> 01:19:50.307
Did Allen screw his wife or anything?


01:19:50.412 --> 01:19:52.107
We're gonna do
a full background check.


01:19:52.214 --> 01:19:54.876
But I got to tell you, I like this guy.


01:19:55.917 --> 01:19:57.817
So, let's pull
some handwriting samples.


01:19:59.554 --> 01:20:02.455
Hi. I talked to Sherwood.
He got the samples.


01:20:02.557 --> 01:20:04.491
- What are you having?
- BLT.


01:20:07.128 --> 01:20:09.653
So, the check stubs are a wash.
There's not enough handwriting.


01:20:09.764 --> 01:20:12.289
The application's got more,
but it doesn't look like Z's,


01:20:12.400 --> 01:20:14.698
so he can't rule him in.
But he can't rule him out, either.


01:20:14.803 --> 01:20:17.670
- Well, that's vague.
- He needs more samples.


01:20:18.740 --> 01:20:20.833
Also, our guy is a pervert.


01:20:21.910 --> 01:20:23.775
When Mel got the application
from Valley Springs,


01:20:23.879 --> 01:20:26.143
they told him that
Allen had been fired for touching kids.


01:20:26.248 --> 01:20:28.375
- Touching?
- Polite euphemism.


01:20:30.051 --> 01:20:33.179
- So what do you want to do?
- Make some phone calls.


01:20:33.288 --> 01:20:35.916
- Are you done with the fries?
- Go ahead.


01:20:36.024 --> 01:20:37.457
<i>Did you and Mr. Cheney have a chance</i>


01:20:37.559 --> 01:20:39.754
<i>to look at the copies</i>
<i>of the Zodiac letters we sent you?</i>


01:20:39.861 --> 01:20:42.557
Yeah.
Some of this stuff is pretty creepy.


01:20:42.664 --> 01:20:45.758
- <i>Yeah, we know that.</i>
- I mean, creepy like Leigh.


01:20:46.134 --> 01:20:48.625
He misspells words like that.
He thinks it's funny.


01:20:48.737 --> 01:20:50.534
What about the handwriting?


01:20:50.639 --> 01:20:53.574
<i>I don't know.</i>
<i>Don't you have experts for that stuff?</i>


01:20:53.675 --> 01:20:56.769
Our man at Questioned Documents
says it's inconclusive.


01:20:56.878 --> 01:20:58.709
Maybe he did it with his other hand.


01:20:58.813 --> 01:21:00.075
<i>The letters are a little too neat</i>


01:21:00.181 --> 01:21:02.581
<i>for someone to have written</i>
<i>with the wrong hand.</i>


01:21:02.684 --> 01:21:04.413
But not for Leigh, right.


01:21:04.519 --> 01:21:06.419
- What do you mean?
- <i>He's ambidextrous.</i>


01:21:06.521 --> 01:21:09.922
<i>He can write with either hand.</i>
<i>Didn't you guys know that?</i>


01:21:10.025 --> 01:21:12.823
In everyday life, Allen uses his left hand.


01:21:12.928 --> 01:21:15.362
Job applications,
letters to friends, et cetera.


01:21:15.463 --> 01:21:18.091
But he writes the Zodiac letters
with his right hand


01:21:18.199 --> 01:21:21.965
producing a different handwriting
that he can't be linked to.


01:21:22.437 --> 01:21:23.768
We got to see this guy, Chief.


01:21:23.872 --> 01:21:25.066
- Where is he?
- Vallejo.


01:21:25.173 --> 01:21:28.233
He works at Union Oil in Pinole.
His brother's up there, too.


01:21:28.343 --> 01:21:29.776
See them both.


01:21:29.878 --> 01:21:32.346
Make sure you call Mulanax.
It is his backyard.


01:21:32.447 --> 01:21:35.610
Oh, right, because that
worked so well for us in Riverside.


01:21:35.717 --> 01:21:38.277
Cooperation, that's us, at all costs.


01:21:47.896 --> 01:21:51.923
You can talk to him in here.
Coke machine's busted, by the way.


01:21:53.101 --> 01:21:55.035
I'll go get him for you.


01:21:56.538 --> 01:21:58.665
So how do you guys wanna do this?


01:21:58.773 --> 01:22:02.402
Well, Bill talked to the informants.
He leads, we follow?


01:22:02.510 --> 01:22:04.102
It's okay by me.


01:22:18.026 --> 01:22:20.586
Mr. Allen, I'm Inspector Bill Armstrong.


01:22:20.695 --> 01:22:23.596
This is Inspector Dave Toschi
and Sergeant Jack Mulanax.


01:22:23.698 --> 01:22:28.067
We're investigating the Zodiac murders
in San Francisco and Vallejo.


01:22:28.169 --> 01:22:29.761
Please, sit down.


01:22:38.646 --> 01:22:41.114
The informant notified us
that you made certain statements


01:22:41.216 --> 01:22:43.776
11 months prior
to the first Zodiac murder.


01:22:43.885 --> 01:22:46.911
If they're true,
they're quite incriminating.


01:22:47.022 --> 01:22:49.252
Do you recall
having any such conversation?


01:22:49.357 --> 01:22:50.449
- No.
- Have you ever read


01:22:50.558 --> 01:22:52.526
or heard anything about the Zodiac?


01:22:52.627 --> 01:22:53.855
When it was first in the paper.


01:22:53.962 --> 01:22:56.021
But I didn't follow it
after those first reports.


01:22:56.131 --> 01:22:58.622
- Why not?
- Too morbid. I...


01:22:59.634 --> 01:23:02.432
I told all this to the other officer.


01:23:02.537 --> 01:23:05.005
- Which other officer?
- From Vallejo.


01:23:06.441 --> 01:23:07.874
Do you remember his name?


01:23:07.976 --> 01:23:11.673
No, but it was right after
the murder at the lake.


01:23:11.780 --> 01:23:14.248
And what did you tell this officer?


01:23:15.850 --> 01:23:20.048
I told him that I'd gone to Salt Point
that weekend to skin dive.


01:23:20.155 --> 01:23:22.953
That I was alone
but I met a couple there.


01:23:24.159 --> 01:23:26.286
I have their names at home
if you want them.


01:23:26.394 --> 01:23:28.021
That would be great, Arthur.


01:23:28.129 --> 01:23:29.994
- Leigh.
- What?


01:23:30.899 --> 01:23:33.390
Leigh. Nobody calls me Arthur.


01:23:35.170 --> 01:23:38.571
Also, that day when I came home,
my neighbor saw me.


01:23:38.673 --> 01:23:42.439
It was around 4:00.
But I forgot to tell the other officer that.


01:23:42.544 --> 01:23:44.705
- Neighbor's name?
- Bill White.


01:23:46.548 --> 01:23:48.311
He died a week or so afterwards.


01:23:48.416 --> 01:23:51.817
Heart attack.
So I didn't think to call to follow up.


01:23:53.988 --> 01:23:56.081
The knives I had in my car
with the blood on them,


01:23:56.191 --> 01:23:59.718
that blood came from a chicken
that I killed for dinner.


01:24:02.530 --> 01:24:05.328
- What?
- I had knives in my car that weekend.


01:24:05.433 --> 01:24:09.699
Maybe Bill saw them
and called the other officer on me.


01:24:10.338 --> 01:24:13.398
Well, we'll be checking in on that.


01:24:13.508 --> 01:24:14.941
Well, let me ask you something else.


01:24:15.043 --> 01:24:18.979
Were you ever in Southern California
at any time in 1966?


01:24:20.014 --> 01:24:22.505
- Is this about the Riverside killing?
- Yes.


01:24:23.651 --> 01:24:25.881
Well, I guess I was there
around that time.


01:24:25.987 --> 01:24:29.320
I used to go down there a lot.
I like the auto races.


01:24:33.661 --> 01:24:36.095
Informant says that
you're ambidextrous?


01:24:36.197 --> 01:24:38.131
No, that's untrue.


01:24:38.233 --> 01:24:40.531
You can't write with both hands?


01:24:41.703 --> 01:24:44.763
My teachers tried to make me
when I was a kid, but I couldn't.


01:24:44.873 --> 01:24:46.966
I'm left-handed.


01:24:47.075 --> 01:24:51.239
He also said that you made statements
about killing school children.


01:24:51.946 --> 01:24:53.436
That is...


01:24:53.548 --> 01:24:56.813
That is horrible. That is...
That's a horrible thing to say.


01:24:56.918 --> 01:25:00.115
So, you weren't angry
about being fired from Valley Springs


01:25:00.221 --> 01:25:02.416
for touching your students?


01:25:11.699 --> 01:25:13.394
I'm not the Zodiac.


01:25:14.369 --> 01:25:17.338
And if I was, I certainly wouldn't tell you.


01:25:19.607 --> 01:25:21.404
That's a nice watch.


01:25:23.244 --> 01:25:24.268
Thank you.


01:25:24.379 --> 01:25:25.812
May I see it?


01:25:27.749 --> 01:25:29.182
May I see it?


01:25:41.029 --> 01:25:42.087
Where'd you get it?


01:25:42.297 --> 01:25:45.027
It was a Christmas gift
from my mother two years ago.


01:25:45.133 --> 01:25:47.260
That's very sweet.


01:25:47.368 --> 01:25:49.962
So, tell me something, Arthur.


01:25:50.071 --> 01:25:51.095
You don't remember anyone


01:25:51.206 --> 01:25:55.040
you might have had a conversation with
regarding the Zodiac?


01:25:56.211 --> 01:26:01.615
Maybe Ted Kidder or Phil Tucker
at Vallejo Recreation.


01:26:02.917 --> 01:26:04.748
But I couldn't be positive.


01:26:04.852 --> 01:26:06.979
I used to work there when...


01:26:10.658 --> 01:26:12.717
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>


01:26:14.028 --> 01:26:15.120
What?


01:26:15.230 --> 01:26:18.393
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>
That's why you're here, isn't it?


01:26:18.499 --> 01:26:20.228
It was my favorite book in high school.


01:26:20.335 --> 01:26:23.793
It's about this man who waits for people
to get shipwrecked on this island.


01:26:23.905 --> 01:26:25.304
Because he was
tired of hunting animals,


01:26:25.406 --> 01:26:26.998
he hunted the people for the challenge.


01:26:27.108 --> 01:26:31.238
And man is the most
dangerous animal of all?


01:26:31.346 --> 01:26:33.837
That's the whole point of the story.


01:26:34.549 --> 01:26:35.880
Great book.


01:26:37.118 --> 01:26:39.746
Or, at least, that's what I told Phil.


01:26:45.360 --> 01:26:46.588
May I go?


01:26:50.231 --> 01:26:51.289
Sure.


01:26:56.170 --> 01:27:00.436
- Thanks for your time.
- I'm willing to help in any way possible.


01:27:00.541 --> 01:27:02.600
I look forward to the day


01:27:02.710 --> 01:27:06.168
when police officers
are no longer referred to as pigs.


01:27:07.181 --> 01:27:08.341
Thanks.


01:27:09.484 --> 01:27:11.111
We'll be in touch.


01:27:22.897 --> 01:27:26.993
So does anyone think this suspect
warrants further investigation?


01:27:27.101 --> 01:27:30.036
These are copies of some
of the Zodiac letters that were sent.


01:27:30.605 --> 01:27:33.904
We'd like you to take a look at them.


01:27:34.008 --> 01:27:35.873
You think my brother's the Zodiac.


01:27:35.977 --> 01:27:37.945
Well, we're looking at him.


01:27:38.046 --> 01:27:39.411
Are you going to arrest him?


01:27:39.514 --> 01:27:43.450
Mrs. Allen, we don't arrest people
just because we're interested in them.


01:27:43.551 --> 01:27:44.984
Well, Leigh's always been troubled.


01:27:45.086 --> 01:27:47.281
Is it true about the children?


01:27:47.855 --> 01:27:49.288
Unfortunately.


01:27:49.390 --> 01:27:51.984
We don't see him much anymore
since we found out.


01:27:52.093 --> 01:27:54.118
What are your feelings
about Don Cheney?


01:27:54.228 --> 01:27:56.526
Don Cheney? My old roommate?


01:27:56.631 --> 01:27:59.600
- Was he the one who contacted you?
- That's confidential.


01:27:59.701 --> 01:28:01.225
Well, Don's a very reliable guy.


01:28:01.336 --> 01:28:04.396
If he were to tell you something,
I'd believe it to be true.


01:28:04.505 --> 01:28:05.665
- This one.
- What about it?


01:28:05.773 --> 01:28:07.900
Here, where he spells
"Christmas" with two "S's."


01:28:08.009 --> 01:28:09.943
We got a Christmas card from Leigh
a couple years ago.


01:28:10.044 --> 01:28:13.070
He spelled it the exact same way.
Christ-mass.


01:28:13.181 --> 01:28:15.911
- Would you still have that?
- I can look for it.


01:28:16.017 --> 01:28:18.110
Thank you. That'd be great.


01:28:19.253 --> 01:28:21.278
Is there anything else
we can do to help?


01:28:21.389 --> 01:28:23.016
<i>The brother said</i>
<i>he would search Leigh's apartment</i>


01:28:23.124 --> 01:28:24.352
next time he went out of town.


01:28:24.459 --> 01:28:26.689
- That gets you around a warrant.
- For the time being.


01:28:26.794 --> 01:28:30.025
If we do find something,
Mulanax will go to the DA in Vallejo,


01:28:30.131 --> 01:28:31.860
and we could search the place properly.


01:28:31.966 --> 01:28:33.433
Now I got a chance to talk to the cop


01:28:33.534 --> 01:28:36.401
who interviewed Leigh Allen
two days after the Berryessa murders.


01:28:36.504 --> 01:28:38.199
Doesn't remember how he got onto him,


01:28:38.306 --> 01:28:41.298
but didn't think he looked like a killer
so he didn't like him for Z.


01:28:41.409 --> 01:28:44.242
- But you do?
- I wish I could've taken the guy in there.


01:28:44.345 --> 01:28:47.280
Take it slow, Dave.
Try and find more stuff for Sherwood.


01:28:47.382 --> 01:28:49.407
A match'll get us farther
on the warrants.


01:28:49.517 --> 01:28:52.611
- Avery's on two.
- Tell him to screw.


01:28:52.720 --> 01:28:57.020
You want me to communicate that
verbatim or can I spice it up a little?


01:29:06.834 --> 01:29:08.267
Christ, kid.


01:29:09.937 --> 01:29:10.869
Yeah.


01:29:10.972 --> 01:29:13.270
- Paul, I've been thinking...
- Oh, God save us all.


01:29:13.374 --> 01:29:14.739
The letter to Melvin Belli


01:29:14.842 --> 01:29:17.777
was sent exactly one year
after the Lake Herman Road murder.


01:29:17.879 --> 01:29:19.608
And the one to Cheri Jo Bates' father


01:29:19.714 --> 01:29:22.080
was sent exactly six months
after her death.


01:29:22.183 --> 01:29:24.481
- She was killed a day before Halloween.
- Yeah.


01:29:24.585 --> 01:29:26.075
And you received a Halloween card...


01:29:26.187 --> 01:29:28.781
You know, these are all fascinating
pieces of news, Robert,


01:29:28.890 --> 01:29:30.824
it's a bit early in the day.


01:29:30.925 --> 01:29:33.758
Paul, it's 11:00 and we missed Editorial.


01:29:38.366 --> 01:29:40.391
- I'm sorry. I didn't mean to wake you up.
- No, no, no.


01:29:40.501 --> 01:29:41.695
- I just thought that...
- No, no, no.


01:29:47.337 --> 01:29:49.669
This suspect is not your Zodiac.


01:29:51.775 --> 01:29:54.300
This sample matches the canceled
checks and the application?


01:29:54.411 --> 01:29:55.400
Perfectly.


01:29:55.512 --> 01:29:58.709
So we've just retested the left hand.
I mean, we know he's ambidextrous.


01:29:58.815 --> 01:30:02.046
In 38 years, I've never seen anyone
that ambidextrous.


01:30:02.152 --> 01:30:04.643
Both hands would have commonalities.


01:30:05.021 --> 01:30:06.283
I'm sorry.


01:30:06.790 --> 01:30:08.519
Just not gonna work.


01:30:10.460 --> 01:30:12.860
- <i>Homicide, Toschi.</i>
- Dave, it's Jack Mulanax.


01:30:12.963 --> 01:30:15.090
Hey. Mulanax. Yeah.


01:30:15.198 --> 01:30:16.597
<i>We struck out with the judge.</i>


01:30:16.700 --> 01:30:18.327
<i>He won't sign off on a warrant</i>
<i>for Allen's house.</i>


01:30:18.435 --> 01:30:20.460
- Why not?
- Said it wasn't enough.


01:30:20.570 --> 01:30:22.902
Now, unless we bring him a handwriting
match or some evidence that...


01:30:23.006 --> 01:30:25.372
How are we gonna get evidence
if we can't toss the house?


01:30:25.475 --> 01:30:26.908
<i>I don't know.</i>


01:30:27.477 --> 01:30:30.378
- I truly am sorry.
- <i>No, no. Thank you, Jack.</i>


01:30:32.282 --> 01:30:33.340
What do you wanna do?


01:30:33.450 --> 01:30:34.781
Don't know what I can do
without Vallejo.


01:30:34.884 --> 01:30:37.717
We need Allen's right hand.
We can't get it without a warrant.


01:30:37.821 --> 01:30:39.914
Are there other guys
you should be looking at?


01:30:40.023 --> 01:30:41.957
Only, what?


01:30:42.058 --> 01:30:43.958
Twenty-three hundred?


01:30:44.060 --> 01:30:45.391
Okay, then.


01:30:48.565 --> 01:30:49.896
Okay, then.


01:31:17.827 --> 01:31:20.489
Paul, you wrote the Justice Department


01:31:20.597 --> 01:31:23.930
asking to be put in charge
of the Zodiac investigation?


01:31:25.969 --> 01:31:27.869
I merely suggested...


01:31:27.971 --> 01:31:29.165
On our letterhead?


01:31:29.272 --> 01:31:31.297
...that those with intimate knowledge
of the case


01:31:31.408 --> 01:31:33.342
create an information clearinghouse


01:31:33.443 --> 01:31:35.570
to promote an exchange
and free flow of ideas.


01:31:35.678 --> 01:31:38.738
- And that you run it.
- Well, who better than me?


01:31:39.816 --> 01:31:41.340
The marked man.


01:31:42.085 --> 01:31:44.019
Paul, if you want to work here,
I need three things.


01:31:44.120 --> 01:31:45.587
One, stop boozing.


01:31:45.688 --> 01:31:48.851
Two, stop doing
whatever else it is you're doing.


01:31:48.958 --> 01:31:52.450
And three, cut this nonsense out.


01:31:52.562 --> 01:31:55.622
Sweetest of Templetons, if at any time


01:31:55.732 --> 01:32:00.931
you feel my excellent work is no longer
in step with this trashy provincial rag,


01:32:01.037 --> 01:32:02.698
I'll more than happily...


01:32:02.806 --> 01:32:06.264
More than happily
decamp for greener pastures.


01:32:06.376 --> 01:32:07.968
Paul, I mean it!


01:32:18.188 --> 01:32:20.053
- Paul?
- Yep.


01:32:20.156 --> 01:32:23.353
- What was that?
- An editorial tete-a-tete.


01:32:24.527 --> 01:32:26.620
- Wanna grab a drink?
- It's 10:00 in the morning.


01:32:26.729 --> 01:32:28.526
Late breakfast?


01:32:29.566 --> 01:32:31.659
- Early lunch, or...
- Paul.


01:32:34.170 --> 01:32:35.603
Are you okay?


01:32:36.473 --> 01:32:37.497
No.


01:32:40.944 --> 01:32:42.741
Thank you for asking.


01:32:44.981 --> 01:32:47.108
Shorty! Let's go out for one.


01:32:47.217 --> 01:32:49.208
Paul, where are you going?


01:32:51.287 --> 01:32:52.845
<i>So, you moved off my brother-in-law?</i>


01:32:53.857 --> 01:32:55.791
We couldn't get a warrant.


01:32:57.460 --> 01:33:00.861
Last year we arranged for Leigh
to get help from a social worker.


01:33:00.964 --> 01:33:02.591
He only went twice.


01:33:02.699 --> 01:33:05.668
We saw him recently for
the first time in nine months.


01:33:05.768 --> 01:33:08.896
My mother-in-law brought him by
to see the new baby.


01:33:09.005 --> 01:33:12.304
After he left,
I went to see that social worker.


01:33:12.408 --> 01:33:15.741
He couldn't talk about a former patient,
so I just asked him straight out


01:33:15.845 --> 01:33:18.006
if he thought Leigh
was capable of killing people.


01:33:18.114 --> 01:33:21.345
- Because of patient confidentiality...
- The man said yes.


01:33:23.186 --> 01:33:25.347
Why hadn't you seen him
in nine months?


01:33:25.455 --> 01:33:27.355
He's going to school in Santa Rosa.


01:33:27.457 --> 01:33:30.790
- Santa Rosa? Where is he living?
- In his trailer.


01:33:30.894 --> 01:33:32.919
- In Santa Rosa?
- Sonoma County.


01:33:33.029 --> 01:33:35.224
We wouldn't have to go
through the Vallejo DA.


01:33:35.331 --> 01:33:36.821
It's been 11 months
since you talked to this guy,


01:33:36.933 --> 01:33:38.457
and now you wanna search his trailer?


01:33:38.568 --> 01:33:40.331
If we find something, great.


01:33:40.436 --> 01:33:43.599
If not, we get his prints and
handwriting samples from both hands.


01:33:43.706 --> 01:33:46.072
I thought Sherwood shut you down.


01:33:46.809 --> 01:33:49.277
What if I can get a second opinion?


01:33:50.446 --> 01:33:52.437
I don't wanna step on Sherwood's toes.
He trained me at this.


01:33:52.549 --> 01:33:55.313
Terry, all I need to know
is if the suspect is ambidextrous.


01:33:55.418 --> 01:33:59.377
Could he possibly have written
those letters with his other hand?


01:34:01.090 --> 01:34:02.455
Between you and me?


01:34:02.559 --> 01:34:05.995
Because there are differing
schools of thought on this.


01:34:07.197 --> 01:34:11.634
Get the samples of his other hand.
If he's the Zodiac, you'll get a match.


01:34:11.734 --> 01:34:14.294
<i>That's the current thinking,</i>
<i>according to Terry Pascoe.</i>


01:34:14.404 --> 01:34:17.669
Meanwhile, I spoke to a psychologist
who'd be willing to testify


01:34:17.774 --> 01:34:20.743
that someone who undergoes
a personality change like Zodiac


01:34:20.843 --> 01:34:23.778
would manifest it physically,
altering his handwriting.


01:34:23.880 --> 01:34:27.475
Which is why Sherwood couldn't
get a match from Allen's samples.


01:34:27.584 --> 01:34:29.814
We got Terry Pascoe,
this psychology guy,


01:34:29.919 --> 01:34:31.250
coupled with Cheney...


01:34:31.354 --> 01:34:32.821
It could be enough for a warrant.


01:34:32.922 --> 01:34:34.048
Get Cheney on the record.


01:34:34.324 --> 01:34:37.384
"And that he would call himself Zodiac."


01:34:38.494 --> 01:34:39.518
Yes.


01:34:39.629 --> 01:34:43.190
And you're willing to swear
to this, under oath, in Superior Court?


01:34:43.299 --> 01:34:44.698
Without any hesitation.


01:34:44.801 --> 01:34:46.962
Thank you very much, Mr. Cheney.
Thank you very much for your time.


01:34:47.070 --> 01:34:48.059
Thank you.


01:34:48.171 --> 01:34:49.968
Suspect is Arthur Leigh Allen.


01:34:50.073 --> 01:34:53.804
Lives in Sunset Trailer Court
in Santa Rosa, California.


01:34:53.910 --> 01:34:55.502
Physical description.


01:34:55.612 --> 01:34:57.807
Allen is similar in height,
weight and build


01:34:57.914 --> 01:35:01.008
to a man seen at Lake Berryessa
on the day of the stabbings.


01:35:01.117 --> 01:35:03.915
<i>I understand he doesn't look</i>
<i>much like the San Francisco composite.</i>


01:35:04.020 --> 01:35:05.544
True. Height and weight are sketchy,


01:35:05.655 --> 01:35:07.850
but lumbering Caucasian
with a crew cut is right on.


01:35:07.957 --> 01:35:10.255
We never had much confidence
in the composite from the kids.


01:35:10.360 --> 01:35:12.351
The patrolman
who saw Zodiac that night


01:35:12.462 --> 01:35:13.929
said he didn't look much like the sketch.


01:35:14.030 --> 01:35:15.497
Military boot prints.


01:35:15.598 --> 01:35:18.328
Allen was in the Navy.
Wears a size 10-and-a-half.


01:35:18.434 --> 01:35:20.868
Same size as the prints
found at Berryessa.


01:35:20.970 --> 01:35:22.665
<i>What about gun?</i>


01:35:22.772 --> 01:35:27.334
Cheney says Allen owns several
firearms. We'll list them in the warrant.


01:35:27.443 --> 01:35:30.207
- <i>And the ciphers.</i>
- Could be code training in the Navy,


01:35:30.313 --> 01:35:33.009
and people have seen Allen
with ciphers in the past.


01:35:33.116 --> 01:35:34.140
<i>Really? Who?</i>


01:35:34.250 --> 01:35:37.048
That would be his sister-in-law
and a man named Phil Tucker


01:35:37.153 --> 01:35:39.451
that he worked with
at a public pool in Vallejo.


01:35:39.555 --> 01:35:43.013
And Phil Tucker told us about
a conversation that he had with Allen


01:35:43.126 --> 01:35:45.822
about how to attach a flashlight
to the barrel of a gun.


01:35:45.928 --> 01:35:49.159
That gives us two sources
on the ciphers and two on the flashlight.


01:35:49.265 --> 01:35:51.256
<i>What about his threats on children?</i>


01:35:51.367 --> 01:35:53.130
Suspect worked for elementary schools


01:35:53.236 --> 01:35:56.433
and was fired for molestation
in March, April '68.


01:35:56.539 --> 01:35:59.167
- Could give him motive.
- At the very least, it's home turf.


01:35:59.275 --> 01:36:01.334
He'd have knowledge of bus routes,


01:36:01.444 --> 01:36:03.878
which the two major threats
centered around.


01:36:03.980 --> 01:36:05.675
<i>What about the bomb?</i>


01:36:07.116 --> 01:36:09.084
Allen works as a chemist.


01:36:09.185 --> 01:36:10.618
Take him through the geography.


01:36:10.720 --> 01:36:12.187
Vallejo murders.


01:36:12.288 --> 01:36:15.780
Allen lives in Vallejo
with his mother in her basement.


01:36:15.892 --> 01:36:19.055
Berryessa murder. On the day
that the two kids were stabbed


01:36:19.162 --> 01:36:21.824
his neighbor saw bloody knives
in his truck


01:36:21.931 --> 01:36:24.832
which he claimed were used
to kill a chicken.


01:36:24.934 --> 01:36:26.765
<i>Does he have any alibis?</i>


01:36:26.869 --> 01:36:29.531
He claimed he did, but he's been unable
to produce the names


01:36:29.639 --> 01:36:32.904
of the couple he supposedly met
on the day of Berryessa.


01:36:33.009 --> 01:36:35.375
The bottom line is that Allen
can't alibi up on anything.


01:36:35.478 --> 01:36:37.275
Riverside, Vallejo, the lake or us.


01:36:37.380 --> 01:36:39.575
- You want to tell me about the name?
- <i>What name?</i>


01:36:39.682 --> 01:36:40.774
Zodiac.


01:36:40.883 --> 01:36:44.751
Allen wears a watch that bears
both the word and crosshair symbol.


01:36:44.854 --> 01:36:46.219
And he mentioned Zodiac to Cheney


01:36:46.322 --> 01:36:48.847
a year and a half
before it appeared in any letter.


01:36:52.061 --> 01:36:54.495
- John...
- <i>That's pretty good, guys.</i>


01:36:54.597 --> 01:36:57.566
- We think so, too.
- <i>Let's take it to a judge.</i>


01:37:17.787 --> 01:37:19.049
Mr. Allen?


01:37:19.155 --> 01:37:21.146
This is the
Santa Rosa Police Department.


01:37:21.257 --> 01:37:24.055
We have a warrant
to search your residence.


01:37:35.104 --> 01:37:36.230
Hello?


01:37:44.981 --> 01:37:47.211
I'll check with the neighbors.


01:37:48.518 --> 01:37:49.542
Close the door.


01:37:49.652 --> 01:37:52.678
Close the door,
there's rodents running around.


01:38:05.067 --> 01:38:07.558
Neighbor said he tore out of here
about a half-hour ago.


01:38:07.670 --> 01:38:11.970
- You think somebody tipped him?
- We're not leaving till he comes back.


01:38:17.847 --> 01:38:19.576
I'll check the back.


01:38:32.328 --> 01:38:33.317
Jesus.


01:38:33.429 --> 01:38:35.021
- What?
- Squirrels.


01:38:37.200 --> 01:38:39.134
Piece of work, this guy.


01:38:46.075 --> 01:38:48.737
Not one, but two blue windbreakers.


01:38:48.845 --> 01:38:52.508
- Like the Stine scene?
- We'll have those checked for blood.


01:38:53.015 --> 01:38:55.916
And a pair of black gloves.


01:38:57.286 --> 01:39:00.551
Men's seven,
just like the ones we found in the cab.


01:39:00.656 --> 01:39:03.181
Well, he's got the same size shoes
and gloves as Z.


01:39:03.292 --> 01:39:05.726
Probably just a coincidence.


01:39:05.828 --> 01:39:09.662
Dave, I got a gun.
Check that. Two guns.


01:39:10.867 --> 01:39:14.098
They're both.22s.
One automatic, one revolver.


01:39:14.203 --> 01:39:15.693
Well, that's interesting.


01:39:15.805 --> 01:39:18.933
Because he happens to have
an M-1 rifle here in the closet.


01:39:19.041 --> 01:39:21.635
For little darlings bouncing off buses.


01:39:23.145 --> 01:39:24.635
Someone's here.


01:39:31.621 --> 01:39:34.021
Hello, Arthur. Remember us?


01:39:56.612 --> 01:39:57.670
No.


01:39:57.780 --> 01:39:58.838
On the handwriting?


01:39:58.948 --> 01:40:02.440
Ballistics, no match.
Prints, no match. Writing, no match.


01:40:02.552 --> 01:40:04.281
On both hands, right?


01:40:04.387 --> 01:40:06.184
Because we got handwriting
from both his hands.


01:40:06.289 --> 01:40:07.620
And neither hand matches.


01:40:07.723 --> 01:40:09.350
Forget Sherwood.
Let's get another opinion.


01:40:09.458 --> 01:40:11.449
Fellas, he's not your guy.


01:40:18.167 --> 01:40:19.361
Damn it.


01:40:26.542 --> 01:40:27.566
Hey.


01:40:28.444 --> 01:40:31.004
What do you want? Time off?


01:40:33.215 --> 01:40:34.341
A hug?


01:40:35.251 --> 01:40:37.185
Do you know what
the worst part of this is?


01:40:37.286 --> 01:40:39.186
I can't tell if I wanted it
to be Allen so bad


01:40:39.288 --> 01:40:42.553
because I actually thought it was him,
or I just want all this to be over.


01:40:42.658 --> 01:40:44.558
It's because you thought it was him.


01:40:44.660 --> 01:40:46.150
And I did, too.


01:40:48.998 --> 01:40:50.397
You know what? Take some time off.


01:40:50.499 --> 01:40:53.764
Spend some time with your wife
and the kids.


01:40:53.869 --> 01:40:56.394
Go to Candlestick. See a movie.


01:40:57.740 --> 01:41:03.042
<i>"To the city of San Francisco,</i>
<i>I will enjoy killing one person every day</i>


01:41:03.145 --> 01:41:05.545
<i>"until you pay me $100,000.</i>


01:41:06.549 --> 01:41:09.245
<i>"If you agree, say so tomorrow morning</i>


01:41:10.086 --> 01:41:13.021
<i>"in the personal column</i>
San Francisco Chronicle,


01:41:13.122 --> 01:41:15.090
<i>"and I will set up meeting.</i>


01:41:15.191 --> 01:41:16.783
<i>"If I do not hear from you,</i>


01:41:16.892 --> 01:41:19.861
<i>"it will be my next pleasure</i>
<i>to kill a Catholic priest or a...</i>


01:41:23.299 --> 01:41:24.732
<i>"...Scorpio."</i>


01:41:27.136 --> 01:41:28.603
<i>Who's out of their minds?</i>


01:41:28.704 --> 01:41:30.763
I've got to get out of here.


01:41:30.873 --> 01:41:34.138
<i>Where the hell does he expect me</i>
<i>to find $100,000?</i>


01:41:34.243 --> 01:41:36.609
<i>You're not thinking of paying him,</i>
<i>are you, Mr. Mayor?</i>


01:41:36.712 --> 01:41:41.012
<i>The city of San Francisco does not</i>
<i>pay criminals not to commit a crime.</i>


01:42:03.973 --> 01:42:06.441
The killer gets shot in the chest.


01:42:06.542 --> 01:42:08.806
That's how it ends.


01:42:09.278 --> 01:42:10.870
Do I know you?


01:42:10.980 --> 01:42:13.744
I'm Robert Graysmith.
I work at the <i>Chronicle</i> with Paul Avery.


01:42:13.849 --> 01:42:15.407
Dave Toschi. Nice to meet you.


01:42:15.518 --> 01:42:18.009
Dave! That Harry Callahan
did a hell of a job with your case.


01:42:18.120 --> 01:42:20.714
Yeah. No need for due process, right?


01:42:25.061 --> 01:42:27.052
- What do you do at the <i>Chronicle?</i>
- I'm a cartoonist.


01:42:27.163 --> 01:42:28.460
That's nice.


01:42:28.564 --> 01:42:30.464
You're gonna catch him.


01:42:32.134 --> 01:42:34.932
Pal, they're already
making movies about it.


01:42:42.712 --> 01:42:45.647
<i>We today have concluded</i>
<i>an agreement</i>


01:42:45.748 --> 01:42:49.343
<i>to end the war and bring peace</i>
<i>with honor in Vietnam.</i>


01:42:49.452 --> 01:42:52.512
<i>... Charles Manson for</i>
<i>the Tate-La Bianca mass murders...</i>


01:42:52.621 --> 01:42:54.885
<i>Guilty in the Chowchilla</i>
<i>kidnapping case.</i>


01:42:54.990 --> 01:42:57.254
<i>In the murder trial of one...</i>


01:42:57.359 --> 01:42:59.156
<i>Chairman Mao died today...</i>


01:42:59.261 --> 01:43:01.627
<i>... an absolute pardon</i>
<i>unto Richard Nixon...</i>


01:43:01.731 --> 01:43:04.700
- <i>No, I'm not a crook...</i>
- <i>... Generation of hostility...</i>


01:43:06.902 --> 01:43:09.871
<i>... has now led to the death</i>
<i>of 50,000 Americans</i>


01:43:09.972 --> 01:43:12.907
<i>and several</i>
<i>hundred thousand Vietnamese...</i>


01:43:13.008 --> 01:43:15.704
<i>Patricia Hearst is kidnapped</i>
<i>by the Symbionese Liberation Army...</i>


01:43:15.811 --> 01:43:19.144
<i>All of us should stand up together</i>
<i>and say, "No more."</i>


01:43:20.750 --> 01:43:23.378
<i>Your Declaration of Independence</i>
<i>spreads that...</i>


01:43:23.486 --> 01:43:26.080
<i>Americans admire</i>
<i>the United Kingdom...</i>


01:43:26.188 --> 01:43:28.213
<i>Mr. Hoffa has disappeared.</i>


01:43:28.324 --> 01:43:31.816
<i>If we despise our own government...</i>


01:43:31.927 --> 01:43:35.090
<i>... that the police have captured a man</i>


01:43:35.197 --> 01:43:36.824
<i>whom they believe</i>
<i>to be the "Son of Sam..."</i>


01:43:52.314 --> 01:43:54.441
Hi. We haven't met.


01:43:54.550 --> 01:43:56.518
I'm Robert Graysmith.


01:43:56.619 --> 01:43:58.484
I'm Duffy Jennings.


01:43:58.587 --> 01:44:01.681
- Nice to meet you.
- Good to meet you, man.


01:44:01.791 --> 01:44:02.883
You got a great desk.


01:44:02.992 --> 01:44:05.017
Guy who used to work here
was a great reporter.


01:44:05.127 --> 01:44:06.389
Oh, yeah. Oh, I'm sure he was.


01:44:06.495 --> 01:44:08.963
I mean, it's a honor
to leave the <i>Chronicle</i>


01:44:09.064 --> 01:44:11.862
and go work for the <i>Sacramento Bee.</i>


01:44:11.967 --> 01:44:14.128
Dare to dream, right, Robert?


01:44:17.807 --> 01:44:20.674
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you, too.


01:44:20.776 --> 01:44:22.869
I'm just right down there
at the Art department


01:44:22.978 --> 01:44:25.446
- if you need anything, Duffy.
- Yeah.


01:44:28.984 --> 01:44:30.186
- You sure you don't want the car, Bill?
- It's your turn.


01:44:30.186 --> 01:44:31.653
- You sure you don't want the car, Bill?
- It's your turn.


01:44:31.754 --> 01:44:34.917
You could just drop me off at my place
and take the car.


01:44:35.024 --> 01:44:36.958
You should keep the car.


01:44:37.726 --> 01:44:38.784
Yeah?


01:44:39.361 --> 01:44:41.420
I'm not coming in tomorrow.


01:44:43.399 --> 01:44:44.889
Why? What's up?


01:44:46.135 --> 01:44:47.363
I'm done.


01:44:48.904 --> 01:44:50.838
I put in for a transfer.


01:44:56.879 --> 01:44:58.107
Where?


01:44:58.547 --> 01:45:00.139
Looking at Fraud.


01:45:02.384 --> 01:45:04.443
I can't be on call anymore.


01:45:07.256 --> 01:45:09.520
I wanna see these kids grow up.


01:45:10.693 --> 01:45:12.923
Hey, good for you, Bill.


01:45:14.830 --> 01:45:17.321
- You'll be okay.
- Yeah. I'll be fine.


01:45:19.401 --> 01:45:20.425
Hey,


01:45:21.537 --> 01:45:24.938
I'm not leaving you
holding the bag on anything, am I?


01:45:26.642 --> 01:45:27.666
No.


01:45:30.045 --> 01:45:31.103
Okay.


01:45:31.780 --> 01:45:33.475
Hey, you know what?


01:45:34.116 --> 01:45:38.314
Maybe you'll have a chance
to try your Japanese food, the raw stuff.


01:45:39.321 --> 01:45:40.379
Yeah.


01:46:12.388 --> 01:46:14.083
I'm not Paul Avery.


01:46:16.992 --> 01:46:19.927
The boys need to be tucked in, please,
and the baby needs changing.


01:46:20.029 --> 01:46:22.327
- I'll flip you for it.
- You wish.


01:46:25.801 --> 01:46:28.463
Nobody has more Zodiac crap
than you do.


01:47:13.182 --> 01:47:15.377
- Are you kidding me?
- Hi, Paul.


01:47:17.152 --> 01:47:19.814
Permission to come aboard.
It's right there.


01:47:19.922 --> 01:47:22.390
Anyway, you got shoes on.
This is perfect right here.


01:47:22.491 --> 01:47:24.391
- That's the one.
- Okay.


01:47:26.128 --> 01:47:28.926
- See that? Mesmerizing.
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.


01:47:29.031 --> 01:47:31.659
My own kids
would kill me for one of those.


01:47:33.535 --> 01:47:35.765
- How are you?
- Fantastic.


01:47:35.871 --> 01:47:37.998
I mean, admittedly,


01:47:38.107 --> 01:47:40.439
the <i>Bee</i> ain't exactly
the <i>Chron,</i> but fuck it, right?


01:47:40.542 --> 01:47:43.443
Do you want a drink?
I don't have anything blue, but I got...


01:47:43.545 --> 01:47:45.513
Don't worry about that.
Don't worry about it.


01:47:45.614 --> 01:47:49.175
It's no bother at all.
Nobody comes by from the old days.


01:47:49.585 --> 01:47:50.609
Cheers.


01:47:51.387 --> 01:47:53.514
To your health and mine.


01:47:55.457 --> 01:47:56.822
Mostly mine.


01:48:02.031 --> 01:48:03.521
So,


01:48:05.734 --> 01:48:07.065
what's new?


01:48:09.104 --> 01:48:11.004
- I've been thinking.
- Yeah.


01:48:11.106 --> 01:48:12.232
Somebody should write a book.


01:48:12.341 --> 01:48:15.276
Somebody should write a fucking book,
that's for sure.


01:48:15.377 --> 01:48:17.504
- About what?
- About Zodiac.


01:48:19.148 --> 01:48:20.547
It's not new.


01:48:20.649 --> 01:48:25.279
I've been thinking that
if you put all the information together,


01:48:25.387 --> 01:48:26.945
maybe you could jog something loose.


01:48:27.056 --> 01:48:29.547
And then I was thinking that
nobody knows the case better than you.


01:48:29.658 --> 01:48:30.682
Yeah. That's true.


01:48:30.793 --> 01:48:33.785
You know all the players,
and you have all the files.


01:48:33.896 --> 01:48:35.193
Lost them.


01:48:35.531 --> 01:48:36.589
You lost them?


01:48:36.698 --> 01:48:39.963
Or I tossed them. I don't know.
I moved onto a boat.


01:48:40.402 --> 01:48:42.461
You know that we work
in the daily business, right?


01:48:42.571 --> 01:48:43.833
As in, today.


01:48:43.939 --> 01:48:46.703
What do you think
we were doing back then?


01:48:47.709 --> 01:48:49.836
Do you know that more people die
in the East Bay commute


01:48:49.945 --> 01:48:52.243
every three months
than that idiot ever killed?


01:48:52.347 --> 01:48:53.507
He offed a few citizens,


01:48:53.615 --> 01:48:56.948
he wrote a few letters,
and he faded into a footnote.


01:49:02.458 --> 01:49:05.450
Not that I haven't been sitting here idly


01:49:05.561 --> 01:49:09.520
waiting for you to drop by
and reinvigorate my sense of purpose.


01:49:11.867 --> 01:49:14.995
It was four years ago. Let it fucking go.


01:49:15.104 --> 01:49:17.800
You're wrong. It was important.


01:49:19.074 --> 01:49:21.565
Then, what did you ever do about it?


01:49:22.444 --> 01:49:24.571
If it was so fucking important,
what did you ever do?


01:49:24.680 --> 01:49:27.513
You hovered over my desk,
you stole from wastebaskets.


01:49:27.616 --> 01:49:29.243
Am I being unkind?


01:49:30.419 --> 01:49:33.684
Oh, that's right, I forgot.
You went to the library.


01:49:36.492 --> 01:49:38.460
I'm sorry I bothered you.


01:50:00.582 --> 01:50:02.607
- Hey, hi.
- Hi.


01:50:02.718 --> 01:50:05.152
- Where you been?
- The library.


01:50:36.818 --> 01:50:38.115
Thank you!


01:50:53.869 --> 01:50:57.236
- Inspector Toschi?
- Yeah? One moment, please.


01:51:01.610 --> 01:51:02.804
- Hi.
- Hi.


01:51:04.112 --> 01:51:06.103
We met at the movies once.


01:51:06.615 --> 01:51:07.980
It must have been magical.


01:51:08.083 --> 01:51:09.812
I'm Robert Graysmith.
I work at the <i>Chronicle.</i>


01:51:09.918 --> 01:51:11.887
I was wondering if I could buy you lunch.


01:51:11.887 --> 01:51:12.683
I was wondering if I could buy you lunch.


01:51:14.423 --> 01:51:16.084
Sure, why not?


01:51:16.191 --> 01:51:18.557
So, you're a friend of Paul Avery's?


01:51:18.660 --> 01:51:21.060
He's actually the reason I'm here.


01:51:22.798 --> 01:51:25.164
I wanted to ask you about Zodiac.


01:51:25.634 --> 01:51:28.865
Well, I appreciate the interest,
but we don't discuss open cases.


01:51:28.971 --> 01:51:31.496
Oh, well, what's going on with it,
day to day?


01:51:31.607 --> 01:51:33.268
We're actively pursuing all leads.


01:51:33.375 --> 01:51:35.935
And you're the only one on it, right?


01:51:37.112 --> 01:51:38.579
Mr. Graysmith,


01:51:39.715 --> 01:51:41.683
Zodiac hasn't written in three years.


01:51:41.783 --> 01:51:44.513
You know how many murders
we've had in San Francisco since then?


01:51:44.620 --> 01:51:46.110
- No.
- Over 200.


01:51:46.221 --> 01:51:49.520
That's a lot of dead people
and grieving families that need our help.


01:51:49.625 --> 01:51:51.217
So, nobody cares.


01:51:51.360 --> 01:51:53.794
Excuse me? I care.


01:51:56.498 --> 01:51:58.762
Okay. Can I show you something?


01:52:01.670 --> 01:52:04.833
I've been doing research
on the first cipher.


01:52:04.940 --> 01:52:06.703
Everything an amateur
would need to create it


01:52:06.808 --> 01:52:09.777
can be found in these books.


01:52:09.878 --> 01:52:13.211
Now, I started thinking
that if you can track these books,


01:52:13.315 --> 01:52:15.715
then maybe you can track the man.


01:52:16.251 --> 01:52:19.084
So, I remember you thought
that Zodiac was military,


01:52:19.187 --> 01:52:22.850
so I went to every base library
and I got a list of every person


01:52:22.958 --> 01:52:26.894
who's ever checked out these books
and that's when I found this.


01:52:31.633 --> 01:52:34.124
- Missing.
- It means they were stolen.


01:52:34.936 --> 01:52:38.497
So, almost every book on ciphers
was stolen from the Presidio Library?


01:52:38.607 --> 01:52:41.201
And the Oakland Army Terminal Library.


01:52:44.012 --> 01:52:48.449
Somebody didn't want a record
of ever having checked out these books.


01:52:48.550 --> 01:52:50.177
Who are you again?


01:52:52.287 --> 01:52:53.914
I just wanna help.


01:52:57.125 --> 01:52:59.389
I can't allow you to help.


01:52:59.494 --> 01:53:01.257
I can't discuss the case with you.


01:53:01.363 --> 01:53:03.797
I can't give you information,
and I certainly couldn't tell you


01:53:03.899 --> 01:53:06.094
to go see Ken Narlow in Napa.


01:53:06.668 --> 01:53:08.033
N-A-R-L-O-W.


01:53:18.046 --> 01:53:22.710
I'm sorry, Mr. Graysmith,
but we don't cooperate with writers.


01:53:22.818 --> 01:53:25.582
Well, I'm not a writer, I'm a cartoonist.


01:53:26.521 --> 01:53:28.716
- And Dave Toschi sent you?
- Yes.


01:53:28.824 --> 01:53:30.792
- Why?
- Maybe he...


01:53:30.892 --> 01:53:33.690
Maybe he thought
that I could do some good.


01:53:34.429 --> 01:53:38.593
- What are you, some kind of boy scout?
- Eagle Scout, actually, first class.


01:53:39.568 --> 01:53:42.731
Well, if you wanna do this,
don't let me stop you.


01:53:44.039 --> 01:53:46.098
Better start with Vallejo, Jack Mulanax.


01:53:47.075 --> 01:53:49.475
I understand what you're trying to do.


01:53:49.578 --> 01:53:51.773
But this is an open police investigation.


01:53:51.880 --> 01:53:53.973
I'm a friend of Dave Toschi's.


01:53:54.082 --> 01:53:57.347
And he said
that you might be able to help.


01:53:57.452 --> 01:54:00.353
I mean, the case is dead.
Zodiac's long gone.


01:54:01.289 --> 01:54:03.450
He's yesterday's news, right?


01:54:04.526 --> 01:54:06.289
That's what they say.


01:54:07.229 --> 01:54:09.060
So, what's the harm?


01:54:09.164 --> 01:54:10.597
<i>No pens, no paper.</i>


01:54:11.166 --> 01:54:13.828
Anything that you see that's relevant,
you got to remember in your head.


01:54:13.935 --> 01:54:14.993
Okay.


01:54:17.239 --> 01:54:18.536
Okay, here we go.


01:54:18.640 --> 01:54:20.699
- Which one?
- All of them.


01:54:20.809 --> 01:54:23.505
And there's more in the next room.
They're all marked with these numbers.


01:54:23.612 --> 01:54:24.806
243-146.


01:54:24.913 --> 01:54:26.744
You don't smoke, do you?


01:54:26.848 --> 01:54:28.941
Once. In high school.


01:54:32.354 --> 01:54:33.719
What's this?


01:54:34.656 --> 01:54:35.953
Thank you.


01:55:04.186 --> 01:55:06.177
<i>Man, you really creeped us out.</i>


01:55:12.060 --> 01:55:14.051
<i>"Nine millimeter.</i>


01:55:15.630 --> 01:55:18.155
<i>"Said nothing and began firing."</i>


01:55:26.975 --> 01:55:28.272
"Most Dangerous Game.


01:55:28.376 --> 01:55:31.140
<i>"Do not eliminate this suspect</i>
<i>because of handwriting.</i>


01:55:31.246 --> 01:55:33.339
<i>"Not because of handwriting.</i>


01:55:33.915 --> 01:55:35.883
"Darlene's sister, Linda.


01:55:35.984 --> 01:55:38.646
"It was all just deep breathing. George.


01:55:39.287 --> 01:55:42.051
"It was a strange man. George.
Strange man."


01:55:43.024 --> 01:55:44.651
Thank you so much.


01:55:46.561 --> 01:55:48.552
Oh, briefcase. Oh, thanks.


01:55:51.266 --> 01:55:53.791
- Hey, Jack.
- Hey, Bawart.


01:55:53.902 --> 01:55:55.733
- Who's that?
- That's Graysmith.


01:55:55.837 --> 01:55:59.102
Some cartoonist.
Thinks he's gonna solve the Zodiac.


01:56:00.809 --> 01:56:02.106
Well, good for him.


01:56:32.574 --> 01:56:34.838
- Thank you for meeting me, Inspector.
- No. We're not meeting, Robert.


01:56:34.943 --> 01:56:36.467
We're just two guys
who happen to be sitting


01:56:36.578 --> 01:56:37.738
on the same bench at the same time.


01:56:37.846 --> 01:56:40.246
I've got five minutes.
I've got to get back to the Hall.


01:56:40.348 --> 01:56:43.078
Okay. As far as you know,
did anyone ever get in touch


01:56:43.184 --> 01:56:44.879
with Mike Mageau
during your investigation


01:56:44.986 --> 01:56:47.454
- and show him suspect photos?
- Why?


01:56:47.556 --> 01:56:49.990
Well, he's the only surviving victim
who ever saw Zodiac without a mask.


01:56:50.091 --> 01:56:51.422
No, I mean, why are you asking me?


01:56:51.526 --> 01:56:53.391
Mageau and Darlene,
that's Vallejo's case.


01:56:53.495 --> 01:56:56.259
Paul Stine is mine.
You've got four minutes now.


01:56:56.364 --> 01:56:58.662
Darlene Ferrin was being followed.


01:56:58.767 --> 01:57:00.530
Now, I know Mulanax says
that they already found this guy,


01:57:00.635 --> 01:57:01.624
a George Waters?


01:57:01.736 --> 01:57:03.533
But he also said
that she had a lot of admirers


01:57:03.638 --> 01:57:05.265
who would come to
the restaurant where she worked.


01:57:05.373 --> 01:57:06.965
- She was popular.
- Very.


01:57:07.075 --> 01:57:08.702
Yeah. So...


01:57:08.810 --> 01:57:10.744
She and her husband,
they move into their new house,


01:57:10.845 --> 01:57:12.472
and one night they throw
this painting party.


01:57:12.581 --> 01:57:13.673
And what's a painting party?


01:57:13.782 --> 01:57:15.750
It's a party where people come
and help you paint.


01:57:15.850 --> 01:57:16.942
Sounds like a terrible party.


01:57:17.052 --> 01:57:20.818
Well, supposedly,
somebody who's not Waters shows up.


01:57:20.922 --> 01:57:22.787
And Darlene is terrified of him.


01:57:22.891 --> 01:57:24.620
So you think that Darlene knew Zodiac?


01:57:24.726 --> 01:57:29.186
And if Zodiac knew Darlene,
then maybe Mageau knows Zodiac.


01:57:29.297 --> 01:57:31.128
Maybe. But Mageau's gone.


01:57:31.232 --> 01:57:32.824
So if you wanna connect
Darlene to Zodiac,


01:57:32.934 --> 01:57:34.333
you're gonna have to find another way.


01:57:34.436 --> 01:57:35.767
I have another way.


01:57:35.870 --> 01:57:37.462
Phone calls the night
of Darlene's murder.


01:57:37.572 --> 01:57:40.666
- Yeah, Zodiac called the police.
- No, Dave, there were four other calls.


01:57:40.775 --> 01:57:43.073
There were two to Darlene's house,
one to Darlene's brother-in-law,


01:57:43.178 --> 01:57:45.476
and one to Darlene's father-in-law.
Just heavy breathing.


01:57:45.580 --> 01:57:47.411
They started around 1:30 a. <i>M.,</i>


01:57:47.515 --> 01:57:51.178
and this was before anyone in the family
knew that Darlene had been shot.


01:57:51.286 --> 01:57:53.379
- This was in the Vallejo files?
- Yeah.


01:57:53.488 --> 01:57:54.512
God damn it.


01:57:54.623 --> 01:57:56.352
It's got to be more
than just a coincidence, right?


01:57:56.458 --> 01:57:59.325
I mean, somebody doesn't just randomly
prank phone call a victim's entire family


01:57:59.427 --> 01:58:01.452
90 minutes after they were shot.


01:58:01.563 --> 01:58:03.622
So, either Zodiac shoots
a random couple,


01:58:03.732 --> 01:58:05.222
then he recognizes Darlene...


01:58:05.333 --> 01:58:07.324
Or Darlene was shot on purpose.


01:58:07.435 --> 01:58:10.632
Either way,
Zodiac had to have known Darlene.


01:58:12.540 --> 01:58:14.269
That's good, Robert.


01:58:14.776 --> 01:58:17.973
So, I can't find Mageau,
so maybe I can find Darlene's sister.


01:58:18.079 --> 01:58:19.979
And maybe she can tell me
who this mystery man is.


01:58:20.081 --> 01:58:22.879
Try that. I've got to go. She's very cute.


01:58:26.788 --> 01:58:28.312
You know,


01:58:28.423 --> 01:58:31.756
it's interesting that you should mention
Zodiac calling people at home.


01:58:31.860 --> 01:58:33.293
He did that in San Francisco once.


01:58:33.395 --> 01:58:34.885
What? Who did he call?


01:58:34.996 --> 01:58:38.056
I can't tell you.
That's privileged information.


01:58:38.700 --> 01:58:40.861
But maybe Melvin Belli could.


01:58:43.538 --> 01:58:45.062
Melvin Belli.


01:58:46.007 --> 01:58:48.271
How do I get to Melvin Belli?


01:58:48.376 --> 01:58:51.368
- He should be along soon.
- Oh, that's all right.


01:58:51.479 --> 01:58:53.845
I've really...
I've only been waiting two hours, so...


01:58:53.948 --> 01:58:55.779
He's usually not this late.


01:58:55.884 --> 01:58:58.648
Oh, cookies. Thank you.
These look great.


01:58:59.487 --> 01:59:03.389
- You are here on business?
- I'm writing a book about the Zodiac.


01:59:03.491 --> 01:59:06.426
I remember that. I spoke to him.


01:59:06.528 --> 01:59:11.124
- You mean to Mr. Belli about the case?
- No, to the Zodiac when he called.


01:59:11.232 --> 01:59:14.531
He said he had to kill
because it was his birthday.


01:59:14.636 --> 01:59:17.867
He said it... Wait.
He said it was his birthday?


01:59:17.972 --> 01:59:20.497
Yes. You want something to drink?


01:59:21.543 --> 01:59:25.536
- When was this?
- Oh, so many years ago.


01:59:27.248 --> 01:59:29.808
Mr. Belli was away for Christmas.


01:59:29.918 --> 01:59:31.146
Gone for a week.


01:59:31.252 --> 01:59:33.584
The Zodiac called,
wanting to talk to him.


01:59:33.688 --> 01:59:35.383
I said, "He is not here."


01:59:35.490 --> 01:59:38.391
He said, "I have to kill.
Today is my birthday."


01:59:38.493 --> 01:59:40.427
And then he hangs up.


01:59:40.528 --> 01:59:42.018
Then the letter arrived.


01:59:42.130 --> 01:59:46.157
So, the call came
before the letter of December 20th.


01:59:46.267 --> 01:59:48.201
Mr. Belli was gone for a week?


01:59:48.303 --> 01:59:52.034
He came back on Christmas.
Not a good day to work.


01:59:52.140 --> 01:59:54.074
So, he left on the 18th.


01:59:55.276 --> 01:59:56.743
Is that helpful?


01:59:56.845 --> 01:59:58.278
She said it was his birthday.


01:59:58.379 --> 02:00:02.179
<i>Well, you'd have to confirm that,</i>
<i>now wouldn't you?</i>


02:00:02.283 --> 02:00:03.682
How?


02:00:03.785 --> 02:00:06.879
<i>Well, I never spoke to her,</i>
<i>but maybe my partner did.</i>


02:00:06.988 --> 02:00:09.821
- How do I get a hold of him?
- <i>You don't. Bill wanted out of this.</i>


02:00:09.924 --> 02:00:12.188
<i>As far as I'm concerned,</i>
<i>he should stay out.</i>


02:00:12.293 --> 02:00:13.555
How do I confirm it?


02:00:13.661 --> 02:00:16.186
<i>Well, if my partner</i>
<i>did talk to someone from Justice,</i>


02:00:16.297 --> 02:00:17.855
<i>then they would've had</i>
<i>to put that in a report.</i>


02:00:17.966 --> 02:00:20.264
<i>That's standard procedure.</i>


02:00:20.368 --> 02:00:22.427
- Okay.
- <i>Mel Nicolai.</i>


02:00:22.537 --> 02:00:24.471
- Thank you.
- <i>Goodbye.</i>


02:00:24.572 --> 02:00:26.733
I just need to confirm a date.


02:00:26.841 --> 02:00:28.172
- Mr. Graysmith...
- I've narrowed it down


02:00:28.276 --> 02:00:30.540
between the 18th and the 20th
of December, and I just need...


02:00:30.645 --> 02:00:33.944
Okay, I'll play.
Let's say this phone call did take place.


02:00:34.048 --> 02:00:35.481
Let's say it really was Zodiac.


02:00:35.583 --> 02:00:38.347
Why would he volunteer
the day he was born?


02:00:38.453 --> 02:00:40.580
Plus, nobody died on December 18th,


02:00:40.688 --> 02:00:43.486
just like nobody died over the weekend
when he was gonna kill a dozen people,


02:00:43.591 --> 02:00:45.923
or when he was gonna
shoot school kids or blow up buses.


02:00:46.027 --> 02:00:47.392
He's a liar, Mr. Graysmith.


02:00:47.495 --> 02:00:49.156
What if he made a mistake?


02:00:49.264 --> 02:00:51.289
What if he wasn't lying?
What if it was him on the phone?


02:00:51.399 --> 02:00:53.765
He didn't expect to pick it up,
a nice person to pick up.


02:00:53.868 --> 02:00:55.199
What if? What if? What if?


02:00:55.303 --> 02:00:58.636
Look, off the record,
Bill Armstrong checked this out.


02:00:58.740 --> 02:01:01.334
We took this very seriously.


02:01:01.442 --> 02:01:04.673
None of the suspects had the
same birthday as this phantom caller.


02:01:04.779 --> 02:01:06.940
Bill Armstrong.


02:01:12.520 --> 02:01:14.488
Can I give you a piece of advice?


02:01:14.589 --> 02:01:16.147
You're looking in the wrong place.


02:01:16.257 --> 02:01:19.283
Handwriting, fingerprints,
that's what this whole thing's about.


02:01:19.394 --> 02:01:20.759
Stick to the evidence.


02:01:21.796 --> 02:01:22.820
Hi.


02:01:31.139 --> 02:01:34.267
- Hey. How was your day?
- Long.


02:01:39.714 --> 02:01:41.113
Who's Sherwood Morrill?


02:01:41.216 --> 02:01:43.980
He's a handwriting expert
in Sacramento.


02:01:44.085 --> 02:01:45.177
He called.


02:01:45.286 --> 02:01:47.379
He said he can meet you
tomorrow morning at 7:00.


02:01:47.488 --> 02:01:48.750
Oh, great.


02:01:48.857 --> 02:01:51.690
- So you're taking off work?
- Just an hour.


02:01:53.494 --> 02:01:55.587
Sacramento's two hours away.


02:01:56.731 --> 02:01:58.323
- Really?
- Yes.


02:01:59.100 --> 02:02:00.624
What's this?


02:02:00.735 --> 02:02:03.363
Oh, that's that article.


02:02:03.471 --> 02:02:07.032
"Robert Graysmith has quietly been
shopping his book about the Zodiac."


02:02:07.141 --> 02:02:08.233
Yeah.


02:02:08.343 --> 02:02:10.971
It talks all about you
researching Zodiac.


02:02:11.079 --> 02:02:12.478
Well, that's what the article's about.


02:02:12.580 --> 02:02:15.014
I'm not so sure that's something
we want people to know about.


02:02:15.116 --> 02:02:16.174
Why? Are you embarrassed?


02:02:16.284 --> 02:02:19.447
Robert, what's the one thing
we know about Zodiac?


02:02:20.121 --> 02:02:21.315
He reads the <i>Chronicle.</i>


02:02:21.422 --> 02:02:23.913
Yeah, but he's never
gonna read Herb Caen.


02:02:28.596 --> 02:02:30.894
- Hello.
- <i>Mr. Graysmith?</i>


02:02:30.999 --> 02:02:33.559
<i>The Robert Graysmith</i>
<i>mentioned in the paper today?</i>


02:02:33.668 --> 02:02:36.762
- Yeah?
- <i>I can tell you who the Zodiac is.</i>


02:02:40.575 --> 02:02:41.599
Who is this?


02:02:41.709 --> 02:02:43.836
<i>The Zodiac Killer</i>
<i>is obsessed with movies.</i>


02:02:43.945 --> 02:02:46.641
<i>He recorded his murders on film.</i>


02:02:46.748 --> 02:02:50.115
<i>I tried to tell the police,</i>
<i>but they wouldn't follow through on it.</i>


02:02:50.218 --> 02:02:53.153
<i>There's a man you need to find.</i>
<i>His name is Bob Vaughn.</i>


02:02:53.254 --> 02:02:55.779
- Pen, pen.
- <i>V- A-U-G-H-N.</i>


02:02:55.890 --> 02:02:58.017
<i>He's a friend of the Zodiac's.</i>


02:02:58.126 --> 02:03:00.253
<i>Mr. Vaughn does not know</i>
<i>his friend is a killer,</i>


02:03:00.361 --> 02:03:02.955
<i>and he is storing</i>
<i>some film canisters for him.</i>


02:03:03.064 --> 02:03:04.759
<i>In these canisters is the evidence.</i>


02:03:04.866 --> 02:03:08.233
Okay, yeah, friend? Who is this friend?


02:03:08.336 --> 02:03:09.963
<i>You have quite enough to get started.</i>


02:03:10.071 --> 02:03:11.800
Oh, please.


02:03:11.906 --> 02:03:15.205
<i>The Zodiac's name is Rick Marshall.</i>


02:03:19.080 --> 02:03:20.911
Your toast is burning.


02:03:21.950 --> 02:03:23.484
We choose at some point in our lives
how to physically construct each letter.


02:03:23.484 --> 02:03:26.942
We choose at some point in our lives
how to physically construct each letter.


02:03:27.755 --> 02:03:29.950
Once we lock that into our brains,


02:03:30.058 --> 02:03:32.356
our handwriting may change
over the years,


02:03:32.460 --> 02:03:35.122
but the moves themselves
remain unaltered.


02:03:35.229 --> 02:03:36.719
- Understand?
- Yes.


02:03:38.333 --> 02:03:40.267
Except Zodiac's doesn't.


02:03:41.869 --> 02:03:43.803
Specifically with his "K."


02:03:45.039 --> 02:03:47.940
In his first letters,
he executed the "K" with two strokes.


02:03:48.042 --> 02:03:49.509
Later letters, he did them with three.


02:03:49.610 --> 02:03:51.874
- Why?
- We don't know.


02:03:51.980 --> 02:03:53.914
Excuse me, I've got to spray this.


02:03:54.015 --> 02:03:57.143
How many suspects
were cleared through handwriting?


02:03:57.251 --> 02:03:58.684
All of them.


02:03:58.786 --> 02:04:02.244
Also the print in the cab.
No match was ever found.


02:04:02.357 --> 02:04:06.384
Is there any way that someone
could beat a handwriting test?


02:04:06.494 --> 02:04:07.483
No.


02:04:07.595 --> 02:04:10.758
Whoever the Zodiac is,
he's not someone I cleared.


02:04:11.699 --> 02:04:15.157
About a month ago, a man showed up
on my doorstep very distraught.


02:04:15.269 --> 02:04:17.328
His name was Wallace Penny.


02:04:18.272 --> 02:04:20.536
He said he knew who the Zodiac was.


02:04:20.641 --> 02:04:22.666
Gave me a name.


02:04:22.777 --> 02:04:24.972
Rick. Rick somebody.


02:04:25.079 --> 02:04:27.479
- Rick Marshall?
- Yeah.


02:04:27.582 --> 02:04:30.107
I think that the man
who you talked to called me, too.


02:04:30.218 --> 02:04:32.812
After he left, then I checked my files.


02:04:32.920 --> 02:04:34.615
I never cleared a Rick Marshall.


02:04:41.896 --> 02:04:43.022
Hello?


02:04:48.202 --> 02:04:49.897
Hello? Who is this?


02:05:00.081 --> 02:05:01.981
It's a wrong number.


02:05:07.955 --> 02:05:11.083
Does the name Rick Marshall
mean anything to you?


02:05:12.126 --> 02:05:14.151
What are you after?


02:05:14.262 --> 02:05:15.320
What do you got?


02:05:15.430 --> 02:05:19.662
Hypothetically, you just named
my favorite suspect in the whole case.


02:05:20.835 --> 02:05:22.302
This is off the record.


02:05:22.403 --> 02:05:24.735
Couple years back,
I was trying to get Marshall's prints.


02:05:24.839 --> 02:05:26.568
I handed him a photo.


02:05:26.674 --> 02:05:29.040
He looks at it. He's about to give it back
and he stops and he says,


02:05:29.143 --> 02:05:31.577
"My goodness,
I got fingerprints all over this."


02:05:31.679 --> 02:05:33.510
And he wipes them off.


02:05:34.248 --> 02:05:35.943
Why didn't you test him for handwriting?


02:05:36.050 --> 02:05:38.678
Because when they finally
did run his prints,


02:05:38.786 --> 02:05:41.050
they cleared him
against the one in Stine's cab.


02:05:41.155 --> 02:05:43.248
- So, then, it's not him.
- Maybe yes, maybe no.


02:05:43.357 --> 02:05:45.382
No. What do you mean?


02:05:45.493 --> 02:05:47.859
Zodiac left gloves behind at the scene.


02:05:47.962 --> 02:05:49.987
If he had the foresight
to bring gloves with him,


02:05:50.098 --> 02:05:52.089
how the hell's he gonna
accidentally leave a print behind?


02:05:52.200 --> 02:05:54.191
But it was in the victim's blood.


02:05:54.302 --> 02:05:55.633
Could have been one of the bystanders,


02:05:55.736 --> 02:05:58.102
or a cop just reaches out,
boom, false print.


02:05:58.206 --> 02:06:00.572
Yeah, but that print
disqualified 2,500 suspects.


02:06:00.675 --> 02:06:01.972
Which is why we also used handwriting.


02:06:02.076 --> 02:06:03.373
But not for Rick Marshall.


02:06:03.478 --> 02:06:06.538
SFPD saw a handwritten sign
in the window of his house.


02:06:06.647 --> 02:06:10.481
Decided it looked nothing
like the Z letters, so they just moved on.


02:06:10.585 --> 02:06:12.815
How do they know
that Rick Marshall wrote the sign?


02:06:12.920 --> 02:06:14.182
My thoughts exactly.


02:06:15.189 --> 02:06:18.852
Rick Marshall was a Navy man.
He received code training.


02:06:18.960 --> 02:06:21.394
He was also a projectionist
at a silent film theater.


02:06:21.496 --> 02:06:23.589
Well, then, how do I get copies
of Rick Marshall's handwriting?


02:06:23.698 --> 02:06:27.566
Three ways.
One, get a warrant, which you can't.


02:06:27.668 --> 02:06:29.795
Two, get him to volunteer,
which he won't.


02:06:29.904 --> 02:06:31.804
Yeah, and three?


02:06:31.906 --> 02:06:33.533
Get creative.


02:06:33.641 --> 02:06:36.371
<i>I don't know what to tell you.</i>
<i>You get it, I'll analyze it.</i>


02:06:36.477 --> 02:06:37.842
<i>Beyond that, you're on your own.</i>


02:06:37.945 --> 02:06:40.379
Okay, what about
the guy who came to see you,


02:06:40.481 --> 02:06:41.880
the one who called me?


02:06:41.983 --> 02:06:44.451
<i>You mean Wallace Penny?</i>


02:06:44.552 --> 02:06:46.645
Yeah. Did he leave a number?


02:06:55.997 --> 02:06:59.262
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Hi, this is Robert Graysmith.


02:06:59.367 --> 02:07:00.356
<i>How did you find me?</i>


02:07:00.468 --> 02:07:02.493
I need a sample
of Rick Marshall's handwriting.


02:07:02.603 --> 02:07:03.900
<i>I told you. Vaughn is who...</i>


02:07:04.005 --> 02:07:06.974
Mr. Penny,
if Rick Marshall is the Zodiac,


02:07:07.074 --> 02:07:09.542
I need a sample of his handwriting
to confirm it.


02:07:09.644 --> 02:07:11.236
Can you help me or not?


02:07:12.947 --> 02:07:17.611
<i>Rick used to draw movie posters</i>
<i>for the theater Vaughn worked at.</i>


02:07:17.718 --> 02:07:19.618
- <i>I'll send one down.</i>
- Thank you.


02:07:29.630 --> 02:07:32.030
- I'll need to see more samples.
- Yeah, but is it...


02:07:32.133 --> 02:07:34.624
It's as close as I've ever seen.
We have to tread lightly here.


02:07:34.735 --> 02:07:37.169
We're talking about
implicating this man as the Zodiac.


02:07:37.271 --> 02:07:40.263
I can get more. I'll just find Vaughn
and I'll track down Linda.


02:07:40.374 --> 02:07:42.342
I mean, Linda is Darlene's sister.


02:07:42.443 --> 02:07:45.139
I've been to the DMV,
and I talked to her parents,


02:07:45.246 --> 02:07:48.340
but still, nobody knows
where to find her.


02:07:48.449 --> 02:07:52.909
Mr. Graysmith, most of the writing
matches the exemplar.


02:07:53.020 --> 02:07:56.046
In a way, though, it's the part that
doesn't match that scares me the most.


02:07:56.157 --> 02:07:58.557
- What do you mean?
- Well, on the poster,


02:07:58.659 --> 02:08:01.753
the one letter that absolutely,
positively does not match


02:08:01.862 --> 02:08:03.420
is the letter "K."


02:08:05.433 --> 02:08:09.301
You wouldn't happen to have any
animal crackers in there, would you?


02:08:09.403 --> 02:08:12.964
<i>Unit Five.</i>
<i>Toschi needs to call in on a landline.</i>


02:08:24.986 --> 02:08:27.352
- <i>Dispatch.</i>
- Hey. Dave Toschi.


02:08:27.455 --> 02:08:29.047
<i>I'll connect you.</i>


02:08:29.991 --> 02:08:31.390
- <i>Dave?</i>
- Yeah. What's up?


02:08:31.492 --> 02:08:33.926
Jennings here from the <i>Chronicle.</i>


02:08:34.028 --> 02:08:35.825
It came in this morning
and you need to see it right now.


02:08:35.930 --> 02:08:36.988
See what?


02:08:37.098 --> 02:08:39.828
<i>The new Zodiac letter.</i>
<i>And it mentions you.</i>


02:08:39.934 --> 02:08:40.992
Okay, okay.


02:08:43.304 --> 02:08:45.568
Shit. All right, come on.


02:08:45.673 --> 02:08:47.607
Hall of Justice!


02:08:47.708 --> 02:08:50.768
Now! Come on, come on,
come on, come on, come on!


02:08:57.118 --> 02:08:58.176
Dave!


02:08:59.320 --> 02:09:01.254
Do you have it with you?


02:09:04.525 --> 02:09:06.720
"This is the Zodiac speaking.
I'm back with you.


02:09:06.827 --> 02:09:09.887
"Tell Herb Caen I am here,
I have always been here.


02:09:09.997 --> 02:09:13.023
"That city pig Toschi is good,
but I am smarter and better.


02:09:13.134 --> 02:09:16.001
"He will get tired, then leave me alone.


02:09:16.103 --> 02:09:19.402
"I'm waiting for a good movie about me.
Who will play me?


02:09:19.507 --> 02:09:21.600
"I'm now in control of all things."


02:09:21.709 --> 02:09:24.371
These guys are from Internal Affairs.


02:09:26.213 --> 02:09:27.805
We need to talk.


02:09:27.915 --> 02:09:28.149
<i>Good evening. Our top story tonight,</i>


02:09:28.149 --> 02:09:29.673
<i>Good evening. Our top story tonight,</i>


02:09:29.784 --> 02:09:32.275
<i>the San Francisco Police Department</i>
<i>has confirmed</i>


02:09:32.386 --> 02:09:34.877
<i>that the man</i>
<i>who calls himself the Zodiac</i>


02:09:34.989 --> 02:09:39.358
<i>and terrorized the Bay Area</i>
<i>has broken his silence of 51 months.</i>


02:09:39.460 --> 02:09:42.088
<i>In a letter claiming,</i>
<i>"I am back with you,"</i>


02:09:42.196 --> 02:09:45.825
<i>the Zodiac makes no overt threats</i>
<i>against the citizenry,</i>


02:09:45.933 --> 02:09:48.766
<i>and muses that his life and times</i>
<i>would make the best movie script yet.</i>


02:09:48.869 --> 02:09:50.359
These carrots are perfect.


02:09:50.471 --> 02:09:51.836
<i>The terse 66 word message</i>
<i>also manages...</i>


02:09:51.939 --> 02:09:52.963
Just go.


02:09:53.074 --> 02:09:56.043
<i>... to mention</i> San Francisco Chronicle
<i>columnist Herb Caen</i>


02:09:56.143 --> 02:09:59.078
<i>and the Department's own</i>
<i>David Toschi by name.</i>


02:09:59.180 --> 02:10:00.772
- May I be excused?
- <i>Are they targets?</i>


02:10:00.881 --> 02:10:01.870
Fine, but you have to come back


02:10:01.982 --> 02:10:03.609
and finish at least half
of what's on that plate.


02:10:03.718 --> 02:10:04.810
<i>More team coverage</i>
<i>on the cipher slayer's return...</i>


02:10:04.919 --> 02:10:05.908
- Okay?
- Okay.


02:10:06.020 --> 02:10:08.488
<i>... begins as Alan Freeman has more.</i>


02:10:08.589 --> 02:10:09.715
<i>Thank you, Eric.</i>


02:10:09.824 --> 02:10:12.292
San Francisco Chronicle <i>columnist</i>
<i>Armistead Maupin says</i>


02:10:12.393 --> 02:10:14.987
<i>that he thinks not only</i>
<i>is this new letter a forgery,</i>


02:10:15.096 --> 02:10:17.030
<i>but it was written by the very man</i>


02:10:17.131 --> 02:10:20.862
<i>trusted to hunt down this killer,</i>
<i>David Toschi.</i>


02:10:20.968 --> 02:10:24.631
<i>Maupin, a very well-respected author,</i>
<i>has gone on record saying</i>


02:10:24.739 --> 02:10:29.335
<i>that he believes Toschi wrote the letter</i>
<i>to drum up publicity for himself.</i>


02:10:29.443 --> 02:10:32.503
Maupin used David
as a character in his column.


02:10:32.613 --> 02:10:34.513
David got a kick out of it


02:10:34.615 --> 02:10:36.606
and so he wrote
a couple of anonymous letters


02:10:36.717 --> 02:10:38.617
asking for the character
to be brought back.


02:10:38.719 --> 02:10:41.711
<i>It was like</i>
<i>writing fan mail to himself. That's all.</i>


02:10:41.822 --> 02:10:44.017
<i>But David did not write that letter.</i>


02:10:44.125 --> 02:10:47.253
No, I'm sure that he didn't.
And I'm sure that this will all blow over.


02:10:47.361 --> 02:10:48.692
<i>Blow over?</i>


02:10:48.796 --> 02:10:50.991
They kicked him out of Homicide.


02:10:51.098 --> 02:10:54.363
They made him give his handwriting
like some common criminal.


02:10:54.468 --> 02:10:56.800
- May I talk to him?
- <i>No.</i>


02:10:57.872 --> 02:10:59.032
Okay, can you just ask him


02:10:59.140 --> 02:11:01.506
if he ever investigated
a man named Rick Marshall?


02:11:01.609 --> 02:11:03.372
Is that all you can think about?


02:11:03.477 --> 02:11:06.878
Mr. Graysmith,
Maupin works at your paper. We trust...


02:11:12.686 --> 02:11:14.051
This girl, she wants music lessons?


02:11:14.155 --> 02:11:15.622
Dave! Dave!


02:11:18.125 --> 02:11:20.320
I'll catch up to you.


02:11:20.428 --> 02:11:22.623
You stop calling my house.
Do you understand me?


02:11:22.730 --> 02:11:24.425
I just need your help to find Linda.


02:11:24.532 --> 02:11:26.591
- Jesus.
- Look, two seconds.


02:11:28.569 --> 02:11:30.969
Look, we've been
running handwriting samples.


02:11:31.071 --> 02:11:33.301
- Who's we?
- Sherwood and I.


02:11:33.407 --> 02:11:34.499
Sherwood?


02:11:34.608 --> 02:11:36.701
Sherwood who was fired
from Questioned Documents?


02:11:36.811 --> 02:11:38.369
Sherwood who drinks
like Paul Avery now?


02:11:38.479 --> 02:11:40.970
- He retired.
- Is that what he told you?


02:11:41.081 --> 02:11:45.245
- What, are you saying he's wrong?
- I'm saying stop calling my house.


02:11:45.853 --> 02:11:47.377
- We ran them on Rick Marshall.
- No, Robert.


02:11:47.488 --> 02:11:48.785
No, I know you don't think it's him.


02:11:48.889 --> 02:11:50.322
I mean, no, I am not having
this conversation.


02:11:50.424 --> 02:11:53.257
But I think that Marshall knew Darlene,
and I can't talk to Mageau or Linda,


02:11:53.360 --> 02:11:54.349
so I'm gonna talk to Bob Vaughn.


02:11:54.462 --> 02:11:55.690
- Robert. Robert, stop it!
- What?


02:11:55.796 --> 02:11:58.026
Okay, the Rick Marshalls
of this world will suck you dry.


02:11:58.132 --> 02:11:59.099
They're blind alleys.


02:11:59.200 --> 02:12:01.668
But he said he wasn't gonna announce
his murders anymore, Dave.


02:12:01.769 --> 02:12:02.827
He was just gonna do them.


02:12:02.937 --> 02:12:05.872
Do you know what the chances
of us arresting someone are now?


02:12:05.973 --> 02:12:10.069
Too much time has gone by, okay?
Too much of the evidence is lost.


02:12:10.177 --> 02:12:13.340
People get old, Robert. They forget.


02:12:13.447 --> 02:12:17.577
Now, I have been a cop for 25 years.
Murder police for 12.


02:12:17.685 --> 02:12:19.983
- What do you do for a living?
- You know what I do for a living.


02:12:20.087 --> 02:12:22.317
- You're a cartoonist.
- So what are you saying?


02:12:22.423 --> 02:12:25.551
I am saying Zodiac was my job.
It is not yours.


02:12:28.796 --> 02:12:31.128
- He's still out there, Dave.
- No, Robert. I am through with this.


02:12:31.232 --> 02:12:33.097
I am through with you.


02:12:39.473 --> 02:12:41.964
What about September 26, 1970?


02:12:42.076 --> 02:12:45.603
- Okay, which one was that?
- The Lake Tahoe nurse goes missing.


02:12:48.616 --> 02:12:49.947
One day before the vernal equinox.


02:12:50.050 --> 02:12:51.950
- Dad?
- Yeah. Mark that.


02:12:52.052 --> 02:12:55.681
Got another one. June 19th, 1971.


02:12:55.789 --> 02:12:58.553
That's got to be
near the summer solstice.


02:13:00.928 --> 02:13:02.190
Oh, guys.


02:13:02.296 --> 02:13:05.322
Don't tell Mom about
our special project, okay?


02:13:05.866 --> 02:13:09.461
How come you and Mom
don't sleep in the same bed anymore?


02:13:13.040 --> 02:13:14.007
Hello.


02:13:14.108 --> 02:13:16.167
<i>Mr. Graysmith,</i>
<i>it's Ken Narlow from Napa.</i>


02:13:16.277 --> 02:13:20.543
Oh, Captain Narlow.
Thank you for calling me back.


02:13:20.648 --> 02:13:22.513
<i>Yeah. How can I help?</i>


02:13:22.616 --> 02:13:25.278
I called you because we've been
cross-referencing lunar cycles


02:13:25.386 --> 02:13:27.047
with the Zodiac's timeline.


02:13:27.154 --> 02:13:31.386
More often than not, each cycle
since '69 corresponds with an attack


02:13:31.492 --> 02:13:34.359
or with one of the letters,
or an unsolved homicide.


02:13:34.461 --> 02:13:37.294
- <i>Who's working with you on this?</i>
- Some colleagues.


02:13:37.398 --> 02:13:38.422
Dad?


02:13:39.767 --> 02:13:42.201
- Ken, can you hold on one second?
- Dad?


02:13:42.303 --> 02:13:44.294
- What is it?
- What's this?


02:13:48.175 --> 02:13:51.235
<i>In the decade since the Zodiac's</i>
<i>last cipher was received,</i>


02:13:51.345 --> 02:13:54.803
<i>every federal agency</i>
<i>has taken a crack at decoding it.</i>


02:13:54.915 --> 02:13:57.679
<i>But today,</i>
<i>where those agencies had failed,</i>


02:13:57.785 --> 02:14:00.413
<i>a cartoonist has succeeded.</i>


02:14:00.521 --> 02:14:02.045
<i>How did you do it?</i>


02:14:02.156 --> 02:14:07.560
<i>Oh, just a lot of books from the library,</i>
<i>and I love puzzles, so I just...</i>


02:14:09.663 --> 02:14:11.858
Yeah. The fucking library.


02:14:11.966 --> 02:14:15.094
<i>I believe that you can accomplish</i>
<i>anything that you put your mind...</i>


02:14:18.005 --> 02:14:20.769
That's a "J"? Okay. Honor Camp?


02:14:22.409 --> 02:14:24.036
Thank you so much.


02:14:26.046 --> 02:14:28.276
Hey, we found Linda.
She's in jail. Isn't that great?


02:14:28.382 --> 02:14:29.508
Why'd you do it?


02:14:29.617 --> 02:14:31.050
Because she'll be able to identify Rick...


02:14:31.151 --> 02:14:33.847
- What are you talking about?
- You went on TV.


02:14:34.455 --> 02:14:36.116
You put yourself out there
for him to see.


02:14:36.223 --> 02:14:37.713
Oh, hon, you're being paranoid.


02:14:37.825 --> 02:14:39.816
Then who's been calling our house
in the middle of the night


02:14:39.927 --> 02:14:40.916
at least once a week?


02:14:41.028 --> 02:14:42.188
Nobody.


02:14:44.198 --> 02:14:45.859
What's it gonna take
for you to be done with this?


02:14:45.966 --> 02:14:48.867
I can't talk about this now.
I have to go see Bob Vaughn.


02:14:48.969 --> 02:14:52.302
Well, that's too bad,
because we're gonna talk about this.


02:14:52.406 --> 02:14:54.738
And when is it gonna be finished?


02:14:54.842 --> 02:14:56.673
When you catch him?
When you arrest him?


02:14:56.777 --> 02:14:58.972
- Be serious.
- I am serious.


02:15:00.814 --> 02:15:04.306
I need to know who he is.


02:15:04.418 --> 02:15:07.546
I need to stand there,


02:15:07.655 --> 02:15:11.557
I need to look him in the eye
and I need to know that it's him.


02:15:13.460 --> 02:15:15.724
Is that more important
than your family's safety?


02:15:15.829 --> 02:15:17.296
Of course not.


02:15:19.299 --> 02:15:21.665
Why? Why do you need to do this?


02:15:23.570 --> 02:15:24.628
Why?


02:15:26.640 --> 02:15:28.608
Because nobody else will.


02:15:28.709 --> 02:15:30.643
That's not good enough.


02:15:30.744 --> 02:15:32.609
Are you done? Can I go?


02:15:47.928 --> 02:15:49.953
- Mr. Vaughn?
- Mr. Graysmith?


02:15:50.064 --> 02:15:51.088
- Yes.
- Hi.


02:15:51.198 --> 02:15:52.529
You needed to speak to me?


02:15:52.633 --> 02:15:55.033
Yes. There's a coffee shop
right on the corner.


02:15:55.135 --> 02:15:58.195
- Why don't we just go to my home?
- Oh, I don't wanna put you out.


02:15:58.305 --> 02:16:00.205
It's no trouble at all.


02:16:00.307 --> 02:16:02.775
- Where are you parked?
- Just right there.


02:16:02.876 --> 02:16:06.209
- You can follow me.
- Oh. Okay.


02:16:24.932 --> 02:16:26.490
Watch your step.


02:16:28.001 --> 02:16:29.662
Come in.


02:16:31.105 --> 02:16:34.233
- Very nice house.
- Oh, thank you.


02:16:34.341 --> 02:16:36.172
It's very rustic.


02:16:36.276 --> 02:16:39.439
- Can I take your jacket?
- No, thank you, I'm fine.


02:16:39.546 --> 02:16:41.514
Okay. This way, please.


02:16:44.318 --> 02:16:46.047
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.


02:16:46.153 --> 02:16:48.678
- How about some tea?
- Oh, no, I'm all right.


02:16:48.789 --> 02:16:50.222
- You sure?
- Yes.


02:16:51.125 --> 02:16:54.856
I wanted to ask you about a film
that the Avenue may have played


02:16:54.962 --> 02:16:56.862
while you were the organist there.


02:16:56.964 --> 02:16:59.228
<i>The Most Dangerous Game?</i>


02:16:59.333 --> 02:17:02.666
Oh, it's a classic. RKO. 1932.


02:17:02.770 --> 02:17:07.469
Fay Wray, Joel McCrea, Leslie Banks.
We've run that picture many times.


02:17:07.574 --> 02:17:09.064
In '68, '69?


02:17:10.711 --> 02:17:12.906
I'd have to check my records. Why?


02:17:13.013 --> 02:17:15.072
Do you remember the Zodiac?


02:17:17.317 --> 02:17:19.581
This is about Rick Marshall, isn't it?


02:17:19.686 --> 02:17:23.087
- He was a projectionist there, right?
- For a time, yes.


02:17:23.190 --> 02:17:27.217
But I have no occasion
to correspond with him these days.


02:17:27.327 --> 02:17:29.795
Okay. Well, there is a connection


02:17:29.897 --> 02:17:32.661
between one of the Zodiac attacks
and that film.


02:17:32.766 --> 02:17:34.495
You mean the symbol?


02:17:35.769 --> 02:17:36.963
Hold on.


02:17:37.538 --> 02:17:41.634
The Zodiac symbol on film.
It's on the countdown.


02:17:45.546 --> 02:17:48.140
It's trimmed off each reel
before it's shown,


02:17:48.248 --> 02:17:50.773
but it always arrives with it.


02:17:50.884 --> 02:17:52.249
Right there.


02:17:52.886 --> 02:17:56.549
The first time I saw it in the papers,
I thought about that.


02:17:57.424 --> 02:17:58.948
We got a tip


02:17:59.059 --> 02:18:03.018
that Rick left a film canister here
that he told you never to open.


02:18:03.130 --> 02:18:06.258
A tip about a mysterious film canister?


02:18:07.134 --> 02:18:08.465
Is it true?


02:18:10.404 --> 02:18:11.564
Yes.


02:18:12.272 --> 02:18:14.570
- Did you open it?
- No.


02:18:14.675 --> 02:18:18.941
- May I see it?
- Rick took it back in 1972.


02:18:20.681 --> 02:18:25.448
This tip is how you got it in your head
that Rick is the Zodiac?


02:18:25.552 --> 02:18:27.213
That and the poster.


02:18:27.321 --> 02:18:28.652
The poster?


02:18:30.624 --> 02:18:32.387
The poster that Rick drew.


02:18:32.492 --> 02:18:35.689
The handwriting is the closest
that we have ever come to a match.


02:18:35.796 --> 02:18:39.061
- Rick didn't draw any posters.
- No, he drew this one.


02:18:39.166 --> 02:18:42.602
Mr. Graysmith, I do the posters myself.


02:18:44.004 --> 02:18:45.835
That's my handwriting.


02:18:54.114 --> 02:18:56.981
I won't take any more of your time.


02:18:57.084 --> 02:19:02.454
Why don't I just go and find out
when we played that film?


02:19:02.556 --> 02:19:04.023
Oh, that's all right.


02:19:04.124 --> 02:19:07.525
It's not a problem.
They're just down in the basement.


02:19:09.363 --> 02:19:12.264
Not many people
have basements in California.


02:19:14.968 --> 02:19:16.026
I do.


02:19:18.238 --> 02:19:20.206
You coming, Mr. Graysmith?


02:19:31.518 --> 02:19:35.181
The original studio one-sheets,
I always kept for myself.


02:19:37.090 --> 02:19:39.615
The cheapo knock-offs
like you brought today


02:19:39.726 --> 02:19:42.854
I end up tossing into the back alley.


02:19:57.377 --> 02:19:58.867
'69.


02:20:04.584 --> 02:20:05.812
You live alone?


02:20:05.919 --> 02:20:11.687
<i>Most Dangerous Game</i> ran in May '69.


02:20:11.792 --> 02:20:14.226
So, that would be about


02:20:15.162 --> 02:20:18.427
nine weeks before
the first Zodiac letter, correct?


02:20:21.368 --> 02:20:22.426
Yeah.


02:20:26.940 --> 02:20:31.206
Do you think he saw the film
in our theater and was inspired?


02:20:37.317 --> 02:20:40.184
Are you sure
there's nobody else in the house?


02:20:41.822 --> 02:20:44.484
Would you like
to go upstairs and check?


02:20:45.225 --> 02:20:46.214
No.


02:20:49.363 --> 02:20:51.888
Thank you. Thanks for everything.


02:20:52.766 --> 02:20:54.233
You're welcome.


02:21:15.555 --> 02:21:16.920
It's locked.


02:21:27.801 --> 02:21:29.098
Thank you.


02:21:32.239 --> 02:21:34.230
Good night, Mr. Graysmith!


02:21:54.194 --> 02:21:57.857
Two killers. Got to be two killers.
One has the...


02:22:05.739 --> 02:22:06.899
Guys?


02:22:40.474 --> 02:22:42.408
You've got five minutes.


02:22:50.584 --> 02:22:51.710
Linda?


02:22:52.886 --> 02:22:54.353
Hi, I'm Robert.


02:22:58.325 --> 02:23:00.054
Did you get my note?


02:23:01.027 --> 02:23:02.995
- What's this about?
- Zodiac.


02:23:04.564 --> 02:23:05.758
Figures.


02:23:07.134 --> 02:23:09.864
- You got the look.
- What look?


02:23:09.970 --> 02:23:11.961
I didn't mean anything.


02:23:13.206 --> 02:23:15.572
Tell me about this painting party.


02:23:16.776 --> 02:23:19.370
I told the cops about that so long ago.


02:23:22.849 --> 02:23:24.612
Darlene always had
a lot of boys around,


02:23:24.718 --> 02:23:26.652
even though she was married.


02:23:26.753 --> 02:23:28.744
And this one guy was weird, though.


02:23:28.855 --> 02:23:32.188
He used to bring her presents
from Tijuana and...


02:23:33.426 --> 02:23:36.020
I don't know why
she was friends with him.


02:23:36.129 --> 02:23:38.597
She once told me he'd killed somebody.


02:23:38.698 --> 02:23:40.256
Really?


02:23:40.367 --> 02:23:42.562
Yeah, I think maybe
when he was in the service.


02:23:42.669 --> 02:23:44.637
- Navy?
- I think so.


02:23:44.738 --> 02:23:46.899
Was he into movies?
Was he a movie buff?


02:23:47.007 --> 02:23:49.908
I can tell you that
he was not into people.


02:23:50.010 --> 02:23:51.341
The party Darlene threw,


02:23:51.444 --> 02:23:54.345
people were supposed to
just show up and drink beer, help paint.


02:23:54.447 --> 02:23:56.677
But this guy showed up in a suit,


02:23:56.783 --> 02:23:59.718
and just sat in a chair
all by himself all night long.


02:23:59.819 --> 02:24:01.252
Didn't talk to anyone.


02:24:01.354 --> 02:24:03.185
And Darlene told me
to stay away from him.


02:24:03.290 --> 02:24:05.121
She was scared of him.


02:24:07.394 --> 02:24:09.862
And a couple of weeks later,
she was dead.


02:24:09.963 --> 02:24:12.431
I'm sorry. Do you remember his name?


02:24:13.433 --> 02:24:17.301
I mean, it was short,
like a nickname, like Stan.


02:24:17.404 --> 02:24:19.702
- Rick?
- No, I don't think so.


02:24:20.607 --> 02:24:22.802
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.


02:24:22.909 --> 02:24:25.434
How can you be sure?
It was a long time ago. Think hard.


02:24:25.545 --> 02:24:27.570
I am thinking hard.


02:24:27.681 --> 02:24:29.046
It was Rick.


02:24:30.083 --> 02:24:31.175
No, it wasn't.


02:24:31.284 --> 02:24:33.650
- It was Rick. It was Rick Marshall.
- No.


02:24:33.753 --> 02:24:35.448
Just say it!


02:24:35.555 --> 02:24:37.386
It wasn't Rick.


02:24:50.170 --> 02:24:51.501
It was Leigh.


02:24:54.674 --> 02:24:55.575
- Leigh?
- Yeah, Leigh.


02:24:55.575 --> 02:24:57.202
- Leigh?
- Yeah, Leigh.


02:24:58.545 --> 02:24:59.842
Sounds right.


02:25:04.684 --> 02:25:07.517
Officer! I need you to let me in.


02:25:07.621 --> 02:25:09.748
- Is this an emergency?
- No, I just need to see one file.


02:25:09.856 --> 02:25:11.483
No, you need to come back
tomorrow morning.


02:25:11.591 --> 02:25:13.786
- One file, just for one second.
- 8:00 a. <i>M.,</i> when we're open.


02:25:13.893 --> 02:25:15.520
Sergeant! Sergeant Mulanax!


02:25:15.629 --> 02:25:18.063
Sergeant, I just need to see one file!


02:25:18.164 --> 02:25:21.565
Just give me five minutes.
I know exactly where it is.


02:25:22.569 --> 02:25:23.729
Please!


02:25:37.117 --> 02:25:38.778
I shouldn't be talking to you.


02:25:38.885 --> 02:25:40.876
- You got five minutes.
- Okay.


02:25:43.156 --> 02:25:44.384
Here. Here.


02:25:44.491 --> 02:25:48.257
Linda states that some of
Darlene's closest friends are Leigh,


02:25:48.361 --> 02:25:51.330
who used to bring Darlene
presents from Tijuana.


02:25:51.431 --> 02:25:53.331
- So what?
- He knew her.


02:25:53.433 --> 02:25:55.128
Linda said Leigh. This is Leigh.


02:25:55.235 --> 02:25:57.669
No. That's just one name in a file
that contains hundreds.


02:25:57.771 --> 02:25:59.204
It's nothing.


02:25:59.973 --> 02:26:02.134
- Dave Toschi...
- Agrees with me.


02:26:02.676 --> 02:26:05.543
Our investigation
into this subject is over.


02:26:08.548 --> 02:26:09.810
I'm sorry.


02:26:18.992 --> 02:26:20.118
Hello.


02:26:35.308 --> 02:26:36.707
Who's there?


02:26:40.180 --> 02:26:43.672
- You didn't return my calls.
- Oh, I've been kind of busy.


02:26:43.783 --> 02:26:45.614
Yeah. I can see that.


02:26:47.854 --> 02:26:49.685
How's the book coming?


02:26:52.759 --> 02:26:54.750
I tried to send you these.


02:26:55.862 --> 02:26:57.625
I called the <i>Chron.</i>


02:26:57.731 --> 02:27:00.495
Well, I'm not a cartoonist anymore, so...


02:27:02.068 --> 02:27:03.262
I heard.


02:27:08.441 --> 02:27:11.035
When's the last time
you ate something?


02:27:13.580 --> 02:27:15.673
Nothing makes sense anymore.


02:27:18.385 --> 02:27:20.649
- Did it ever?
- Yeah, it did.


02:27:22.155 --> 02:27:25.056
Robert, it was just the date
that didn't end.


02:27:25.558 --> 02:27:27.321
You don't mean that.


02:27:28.762 --> 02:27:29.956
A little.


02:27:32.832 --> 02:27:34.629
The kids miss you.


02:27:34.734 --> 02:27:37.828
- I can't have them see me like this.
- Neither can I.


02:27:38.605 --> 02:27:40.698
So, do whatever you have to,


02:27:41.674 --> 02:27:43.198
but finish this.


02:28:10.770 --> 02:28:11.828
Dave!


02:28:12.705 --> 02:28:14.332
Dave! It's Robert!


02:28:16.509 --> 02:28:18.136
- Dave!
- Is he actually here?


02:28:18.244 --> 02:28:19.939
I'm gonna kill him.


02:28:20.313 --> 02:28:22.907
I'm calling SFPD. Where's my gun?


02:28:25.485 --> 02:28:26.611
Dave!


02:28:26.719 --> 02:28:28.448
Robert! Go away!


02:28:28.555 --> 02:28:30.523
Dave! He made a mistake!


02:28:30.623 --> 02:28:32.591
- Get away from the window.
- I'll meet you around front.


02:28:32.692 --> 02:28:34.159
No, you won't.


02:28:35.328 --> 02:28:37.523
- You have to hear this!
- No, I don't, Robert!


02:28:37.630 --> 02:28:40.098
The birthday was the one time
that he was weak!


02:28:40.200 --> 02:28:41.997
The one time
that he gave something away!


02:28:42.101 --> 02:28:45.400
- Robert, I am calling the police.
- It's Arthur Leigh Allen!


02:28:50.443 --> 02:28:52.707
Where did you get that name?


02:28:52.812 --> 02:28:54.336
He called the Bellis' house.


02:28:54.447 --> 02:28:56.677
December '69.
"I need to kill. Today's my birthday."


02:28:56.783 --> 02:28:58.751
It was his birthday.


02:28:58.852 --> 02:29:01.753
Arthur Leigh Allen
was born on December 18th.


02:29:04.824 --> 02:29:06.189
Get in here.


02:29:08.328 --> 02:29:10.489
- Here you go.
- Thanks.


02:29:13.466 --> 02:29:15.297
He wrote me, you know?


02:29:16.002 --> 02:29:17.128
2,500 suspects,


02:29:17.237 --> 02:29:20.798
the only one who ever wrote me
a letter was Leigh Allen.


02:29:21.741 --> 02:29:23.436
They like to help, you know, sometimes.


02:29:23.543 --> 02:29:25.306
Yes, Robert, I know.


02:29:26.446 --> 02:29:29.142
He was arrested January 1975
for molestation.


02:29:29.249 --> 02:29:31.149
He sent me that when he got out.


02:29:31.251 --> 02:29:33.981
"Dear Dave, if I can ever be
of any help to you, just let me know.


02:29:34.087 --> 02:29:35.918
"I'm sorry I wasn't your man."


02:29:36.022 --> 02:29:37.580
And it's typewritten.


02:29:37.690 --> 02:29:40.056
Using a typewriter is not a crime.


02:29:41.528 --> 02:29:43.291
And he knew Darlene.


02:29:44.697 --> 02:29:46.688
It's in the Vallejo files.


02:29:51.905 --> 02:29:55.238
Mulanax said that
he was your favorite suspect.


02:29:55.341 --> 02:29:59.300
That you spent two years on him,
and that nobody ever came close.


02:30:02.382 --> 02:30:04.350
All the evidence said no.


02:30:05.652 --> 02:30:07.882
Sherwood disqualified his handwriting.


02:30:07.987 --> 02:30:11.115
The same Sherwood
that drinks like Paul Avery now?


02:30:12.025 --> 02:30:13.959
Yes, you have Sherwood Morrill
in writing saying,


02:30:14.060 --> 02:30:15.084
"I'm sorry, this just won't work."


02:30:15.194 --> 02:30:16.957
- But you also have Terry Pascoe...
- His protégé.


02:30:17.063 --> 02:30:18.087
Yeah, fine, it's his protégé,


02:30:18.197 --> 02:30:20.028
but he's a handwriting expert
nonetheless, and he's saying,


02:30:20.133 --> 02:30:20.400
"Do not disqualify this suspect
on the basis of handwriting."


02:30:20.400 --> 02:30:22.834
"Do not disqualify this suspect
on the basis of handwriting."


02:30:22.936 --> 02:30:24.870
- So the two cancel each other out.
- No, they don't.


02:30:24.971 --> 02:30:26.268
It was Sherwood's case.


02:30:26.372 --> 02:30:27.839
He was the head
of Questioned Documents.


02:30:27.941 --> 02:30:29.272
If it went to trial,


02:30:29.375 --> 02:30:32.344
all the defense would have to do
is call Sherwood to the stand.


02:30:32.445 --> 02:30:35.073
And there was no way of getting Allen
into court in the first place,


02:30:35.181 --> 02:30:36.409
because there was no evidence, Robert.


02:30:36.516 --> 02:30:37.676
What do you mean,
there's no evidence?


02:30:37.784 --> 02:30:38.876
You have him seen with the ciphers.


02:30:38.985 --> 02:30:41.215
The military boot prints.
The same size shoes and gloves.


02:30:41.321 --> 02:30:43.516
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>
The Zodiac watch.


02:30:43.623 --> 02:30:44.817
The background with school children.


02:30:44.924 --> 02:30:46.755
The misspellings of Christ-mass.
The bloody knives.


02:30:46.859 --> 02:30:48.724
All circumstantial.


02:30:48.828 --> 02:30:51.558
Paul Stine's shirt, his wallet, his keys.


02:30:51.664 --> 02:30:53.427
We should have found
one of those things in that trailer.


02:30:53.533 --> 02:30:55.228
- We didn't.
- That's...


02:30:57.670 --> 02:30:59.661
Okay. Catherine Allen states that


02:30:59.772 --> 02:31:01.899
"Leigh cleaned out his trailer
on Friday after work


02:31:02.008 --> 02:31:05.671
"and moved it to Santa Rosa
on Saturday, August 7th, 1971."


02:31:05.778 --> 02:31:07.769
You interviewed him
at the refinery on August 4th.


02:31:07.880 --> 02:31:09.404
- Yeah.
- So, he's cleaning out his trailer,


02:31:09.515 --> 02:31:13.349
he's moving into a different county
48 hours after you interviewed him?


02:31:14.954 --> 02:31:17.946
Okay. Okay.
Look at the stuff side by side, Dave.


02:31:18.057 --> 02:31:19.149
All right.


02:31:19.258 --> 02:31:22.022
Okay, Arthur Leigh Allen
and the Zodiac, their timelines.


02:31:22.128 --> 02:31:24.790
- When was the first murder in Vallejo?
- Christmas, 1968.


02:31:24.897 --> 02:31:27.491
Eight months before that,
Allen is fired for molesting his students


02:31:27.600 --> 02:31:29.693
and his family discovers
that he's a pedophile.


02:31:29.802 --> 02:31:32.100
- Now, when do the letters begin?
- July, '69.


02:31:32.205 --> 02:31:33.866
After the murder of Darlene Ferrin.


02:31:33.973 --> 02:31:37.033
And they continue
until you go to see him at work.


02:31:37.143 --> 02:31:40.374
Now, after that, do any of the letters
contain swatches of Paul Stine's shirt?


02:31:40.480 --> 02:31:42.277
No. Because he dumped them,
because he got scared.


02:31:42.382 --> 02:31:44.111
Because he knew
that you were on to him.


02:31:44.217 --> 02:31:47.948
- So, when's the next letter from Zodiac?
- Not until January of 1974.


02:31:48.054 --> 02:31:49.453
He is silent for three years.


02:31:49.555 --> 02:31:51.352
Then, in '74, he feels comfortable again


02:31:51.457 --> 02:31:53.322
because everybody's moved off
Allen as a suspect.


02:31:53.426 --> 02:31:54.415
And what do we get?


02:31:54.527 --> 02:31:58.520
Three new letters from Zodiac
in January, May, and July in '74.


02:31:58.631 --> 02:32:01.725
- But then the letters stop.
- What happens to Allen?


02:32:05.271 --> 02:32:06.738
He's arrested.


02:32:07.674 --> 02:32:11.007
January, 1975,
they send him to Atascadero.


02:32:11.110 --> 02:32:14.011
We don't get another letter from Zodiac
the entire time he's there.


02:32:14.113 --> 02:32:16.741
- When is he released?
- August, '77.


02:32:16.849 --> 02:32:20.580
Allen gets out. He types you an apology,
and then what?


02:32:20.687 --> 02:32:23.850
We get our first new Zodiac letter
in four years.


02:32:29.495 --> 02:32:32.862
Okay. Zodiac had to have known
Darlene Ferrin, right?


02:32:32.965 --> 02:32:35.195
Yes, because of the phone calls
on the night of her murder.


02:32:35.301 --> 02:32:38.099
Because of the Vallejo file,


02:32:38.204 --> 02:32:40.195
we know that Darlene knew
a man named Leigh?


02:32:40.306 --> 02:32:41.295
Yes.


02:32:41.407 --> 02:32:43.170
So, all coincidence aside, Robert,


02:32:43.276 --> 02:32:46.074
how can you be sure that Leigh Allen
is the Leigh from this file?


02:32:46.179 --> 02:32:48.647
Now, Vallejo is a small town,
but it's not that small.


02:32:48.748 --> 02:32:50.045
How do you put
the two of them together?


02:32:50.149 --> 02:32:53.312
This is a case that's covered
both Northern and Southern California,


02:32:53.419 --> 02:32:55.785
with victims and suspects
spread over hundreds of miles.


02:32:55.888 --> 02:32:57.617
- Would you agree?
- Yes.


02:32:58.891 --> 02:33:01.689
Darlene Ferrin worked
at the Vallejo House of Pancakes


02:33:01.794 --> 02:33:04.285
on the corner of Tennessee and Caroll.


02:33:07.133 --> 02:33:11.866
Arthur Leigh Allen lived in his
mother's basement on Fresno Street.


02:33:13.606 --> 02:33:16.973
Door to door, that is less than 50 yards.


02:33:20.413 --> 02:33:21.880
Is that true?


02:33:22.915 --> 02:33:24.405
I've walked it.


02:33:28.254 --> 02:33:29.687
Jesus Christ.


02:33:36.395 --> 02:33:37.384
So?


02:33:41.334 --> 02:33:42.892
The prints, the handwriting...


02:33:43.002 --> 02:33:45.971
- I'm not asking you as a cop.
- But I am a cop.


02:33:48.841 --> 02:33:50.866
I can't prove this.


02:33:50.977 --> 02:33:53.912
Just because you can't prove it,
doesn't mean it's not true.


02:33:54.013 --> 02:33:55.640
Easy, Dirty Harry.


02:33:59.252 --> 02:34:00.776
Finish the book.


02:34:09.729 --> 02:34:12.197
Thank you. Thank you for breakfast.


02:35:20.466 --> 02:35:21.956
Can I help you?


02:35:23.636 --> 02:35:24.625
No.


02:36:46.018 --> 02:36:47.349
Mr. Mageau.


02:36:48.054 --> 02:36:50.352
Thanks for coming to see me.


02:36:50.456 --> 02:36:51.787
You're the one I talked to on the phone?


02:36:51.891 --> 02:36:55.418
I'm George Bawart. Vallejo PD.
I took over for Jack Mulanax.


02:36:56.462 --> 02:36:59.431
It's been 22 years.
I don't know how I can help you.


02:36:59.532 --> 02:37:00.692
Well, this is just a formality.


02:37:00.800 --> 02:37:02.199
I'm gonna show you
a group of photographs.


02:37:02.301 --> 02:37:04.166
Now, the person that shot you
may or may not be


02:37:04.270 --> 02:37:06.295
among these photographs.


02:37:06.405 --> 02:37:07.599
You don't have to pick anybody out


02:37:07.707 --> 02:37:09.868
just because I'm showing you
these pictures, you understand?


02:37:09.976 --> 02:37:11.500
Yes, sir, I do.


02:37:12.411 --> 02:37:13.742
All right.


02:37:14.780 --> 02:37:16.270
Take your time.


02:37:16.782 --> 02:37:19.580
If you don't recognize anyone,
that's okay.


02:37:31.063 --> 02:37:32.394
That's him.


02:37:33.899 --> 02:37:35.833
How sure are you?


02:37:35.935 --> 02:37:37.766
Yeah, I'm pretty sure.


02:37:40.473 --> 02:37:41.599
He had a round face like this guy.


02:37:41.707 --> 02:37:42.901
Wait. Am I to understand


02:37:43.009 --> 02:37:44.772
that you're now identifying
the second photograph?


02:37:44.877 --> 02:37:47.937
No, no. Just that
he had a round face like that.


02:37:50.016 --> 02:37:51.483
It's this man.


02:37:52.418 --> 02:37:53.715
All right.


02:37:55.554 --> 02:37:58.614
Now, on a scale of one to 10,
10 being positive,


02:38:02.728 --> 02:38:04.320
how sure are you?


02:38:08.100 --> 02:38:09.727
At least an eight.


02:38:12.538 --> 02:38:16.372
The last time I saw this face
was July 4th, 1969.


02:38:19.645 --> 02:38:22.341
I am very sure
that's the man who shot me.

